ds automatic learning writes. This ledger counts reserved units per kind and res\n## modules/brain/self_model.py: Real self-model for the brain.  Every provider reads live NeuroCore state; failures are reported as provider errors rather than replaced with plausible-looking mock values.\n## modules/brain/state.py: Persistent brain state and mode definitions.\n## modules/brain/trends.py: Bounded metric-trend detection for reviewable self-repair proposals (ADR-058).  The detector is deterministic: it compares the mean of the most recent window with the previous window and only reports a meaningful fall in evaluation pass rate or a meaningful rise in provider errors. It never changes \n## modules/brain/service.py: AI-Brain control service: observe/suggest cycles, state and evaluation.\n## modules/tools/sandbox.py: Tool Execution Sandbox for NeuroCore  Provides a secure execution environment for custom Python tools with: - Restricted builtins and globals - Resource limits (timeout, memory, output size) - Network access controls - Filesystem restrictions\n## modules/tools/node.py: -\n## core/node_retry.py: Opt-in per-node retry policy with bounded exponential backoff (ADR-060).  Retries are off by default: a node may have external effects, so re-running it must be an explicit operator decision. When enabled, only transient failures are retried (timeouts, connection errors and retryable LLM HTTP status\n## core/flow_runner.py: -\n## core/module_manager.py: -\n## core/flow_manager.py: -\n## modules/memory/backend.py: -\n## modules/knowledge_base/backend.py: -\n## modules/messaging_bridge/node.py: -\n## core/research_gateway.py: Allowlisted research sources with SSRF protection, caching and provenance.  Every request leaves through one of three fixed adapters (Wikipedia, arXiv, PubMed) and every URL, including each redirect hop, must stay on that adapter's hosts and resolve to a public address. Responses are size- and time-\n## core/statistics_engine.py: Statistics Engine  P