{"parentUuid":"9d0a8f69-d9b3-480b-88e7-e345b47552e9","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgX1JRScF1UvhHpzJa78e","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 229 open neurocore ideas now have a decision recorded in the idea register, each with a reason and, where I checked code, file references. The register validates and the matrix is regenerated.\n\n| Decision | Count | Meaning |\n|---|---|---|\n| Approved | 14 | The work list, with priority P1–P6 in each reason |\n| Deferred | 135 | Each reason names when to revisit it |\n| Rejected | 60 | 37 don't fit neurocore (game, 3D/image pipeline, multi-tenant), 16 are already built, 7 have nothing in neurocore that would use them |\n| Superseded | 26 | Merged into another idea and pointing to it |\n\n64 ideas also carry the `duplicate` tag. Every change is in each idea's history under `claude:idea-review` (for example, `idea-catcher history IDEA-370`).\n\n**Approved, in order:**\n- **P1 – the bug:** 370 + 120, the message-trimming fix.\n- **P2:** 063, the DNS-rebinding hole in the SSRF check.\n- **P3:** 334 and 030, injection defences on memory writes and on content placed into prompts.\n- **P4:** 369 (token budget) and 060 (step risk).\n- **P5:** 058, 591, 588.\n- **P6:** 619, 625, 629, 631.\n\n**The bug is recorded in two places:**\n- In the register, on IDEA-370 (Approved, P1), with the file and line references.\n- In a new \"Known Bugs & Gaps\" section at the top of [docs/IDEAS.md](projects/neurocore/docs/IDEAS.md). It describes the bug: when a conversation goes over the token limit, the agent loop's message trimming keeps only the last system message, so the persona prompt is lost. It also lists three gaps found during the review:\n  - **SSRF check:** a DNS-rebinding attack gets past the address check.\n  - **Token budget:** it isn't enforced when the provider reports no token usage.\n  - **Step risk:** the agent's own risk rating defaults to \"low\" when it is missing.\n\n  The entry ends with a fix plan that starts from a failing test.\n\n**Three verdicts from the earlier review that I reversed after checking the code:**\n- **576:** the code it proposes already exists in `FlowEvolution`.\n- **572:** nothing would use a pausable budget clock.\n- **507:** it comes from a network-security game and doesn't fit neurocore.\n\n**Not done:**\n- The register is git-ignored, so its changes need no commit.\n- The `docs/IDEAS.md` edit is left uncommitted in the neurocore repo, because you didn't ask me to commit. The large `.aikit/reforge.json` diff showing there was already present before I started.\n- I read \"every idea / goal\" as every neurocore idea. I didn't review the ~400 ideas aimed at other targets, or neurocore's in-app goal list. Tell me if you meant either of those.\n- `docs/IDEAS.md` still marks memory consolidation as not started, though `modules/memory/consolidation.py` exists. I left that line alone.\n\nA backup of the register from before these changes is at `C:\\Users\\YUNUS-~1\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\c--Users-Yunus-Emre-Desktop-portable-agent-kit\\05aa96e5-db7a-4aed-bad4-f0f3cebd2787\\scratchpad\\ideas.before.json`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":483,"cache_read_input_tokens":155775,"output_tokens":1170,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":26},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":483,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1170,"cache_read_input_tokens":155775,"cache_creation_input_tokens":483,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":483},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifie