omplete`), state statements, next actions, at least one citation, an explicit omission list and a byte budget. Activation happens at a provider-observed Source boundary, the receiver ackn\n322 [D] Composite Truth-Table Conformance Suite :: The source documents each composite's return semantics in a comment and then violates them: `Selector` promises \"Failure if all components failed\" but returns `Running` as soon as one child fails with siblings left. A truth-table suite makes the documented return matrix executable: for every composite and every combination of ch\n325 [D] Tree Definition Validator with Acyclicity and Leaf Contracts :: The source builds trees in code, so a mistyped child, a node used twice where a fresh instance was intended, or a cycle created by assigning a node as its own descendant is only discovered at runtime — often as a stack overflow inside `Behave`. A declaration-time validator checks the tree as data: unique node ids, every referenc\n332 [D] One-Shot Failure Evidence Capture Attached to the Gate Report :: Airtest assertions take `snapshot=True`: on failure they capture the screen once and attach it to the step log, so the report shows the exact state that failed. AIKit's gates report a failure message, but a subagent or dogfood run that fails deep in a sequence leaves the reviewer reconstructing the state from the log. A failure \n336 [D] Lock Lease with Process Incarnation and Dead-Lock Sweep :: The source stores, for each lock: a token, the owner pid, an *incarnation* string derived from the process start time, and the acquisition timestamp. A competing process reclaims a lease only when it can prove the holder is dead (pid gone, or the incarnation changed so the pid was reused) or when the lease is older than `stale_m\n340 [D] Frozen Public-Surface Snapshot for Adapters :: The source ships an `xlua-adapter` tool that compiles a binding layer against a **frozen subset of the public interface** and runs 21 protocol checks. A binding can therefore not silently depend on an internal class, and a public API change breaks the adapter build before it breaks a game. AIKit has several host adapters (Claude\n346 [D] Index-Plus-Topic-Article Projection with a Measured Token Budget :: The idea-catcher `MATRIX.md` already lists every idea for every target, which is useful for an audit and expensive for a consumer that needs one target's open work. codesight's pattern is a two-level projection: a small index that names the topics and one short article per topic, each with its own token budget. For idea-catcher \n347 [D] Detector Registry with AST-First, Regex-Fallback and Confidence :: codesight runs a per-language extractor and then a set of detectors that are mostly language-agnostic. The README is explicit that TypeScript gets AST precision while other languages use \"battle-tested regex detection across the same frameworks\" — a declared degradation, not a hidden one. AIKit's codebase map is Python-AST-first\n348 [D] Impact-Scoped Repair Admission by Blast-Radius Union :: codesight's `analyzeBlastRadius` walks reverse imports up to a depth and returns the affected files; `analyzeMultiFileBlastRadius` unions several files' radii. Aegean Reforge decides whether a repair is automatic or needs review by the *kind* of defect alone. Adding the blast radius makes the decision depend on the code it touch\n349 [D] Test-Impact Map Keyed by Route and Model Identity :: codesight's coverage detector maps each extracted route and schema model to a test file that mentions it, using path heuristics and quoted-path/identifier search, and reports the untested set. Aegean Reforge runs the project's tests after a repair; a test-impact map would let it run *the tests that mention the changed route, mod\n358 [D] Heartbeat-Refreshed Lock with Inactivity-Based Steal :: `file_lock` in `scripts/disruption_recovery.py` protects the ledger with an `O_CREAT|O_EXCL` lockfile, and breaks any lock whose **mtime is older than 30 seconds**. That is an age heuristic, and it is wrong in both directions: a process that legitimately holds the lock for longer (a full knowledge regeneration, a large ledger re\n359 [R] Delegation Contract Enforcement :: VibeGame's `enforce-team-mode.py` intercepts an `Agent` tool call, recognizes a role name, and **denies it**, replying with the command that would have run it correctly: ``` architect agent must be spawned via vibegame lead to get task context. Use: vibegame lead agent --name architect-... --agent-type architect --prompt '...' `","numLines":70,"startLine":71,"totalLines":272}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"afc9d0ae-b0fe-440e-be5c-aa052b832cb7","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"C:\\Users\\Yunus-Emre\\Desktop\\portable_agent_kit","sessionId":"05aa96e5-db7a-4aed-bad4-f0f3cebd2787","version":"2.1.312","gitBranch":"main"}
