   \"026\": \"Domain packages: `aikit new --kind software|game|science` already seeds per-kind content; revisit if \"\n           \"users ask for richer starters.\",\n    \"035\": \"Rule-quality rubric for .aikit/guidelines.md: project guidelines are few and short; revisit when a \"\n           \"project accumulates stub rules.\",\n    \"036\": \"Debt baseline: three checked projects have zero hygiene findings; revisit when an attached project starts with debt.\",\n    \"042\": \"Shortcut ledger: PRINCIPLE-007 bans TODO/stubs outright, so marked shortcuts would contradict it; \"\n           \"revisit only if that rule is relaxed.\",\n    \"053\": \"Description linter: one skill and six roles; revisit when the skill library grows.\",\n    \"065\": \"log_safe: --resume prints ledger text written by other agents; revisit if multi-agent ledgers carry \"\n           \"untrusted text that could forge [OK] lines.\",\n    \"071\": \"Path representability: Windows device names are already refused for project names; revisit for NFKC \"\n           \"or trailing-dot collisions if reported.\",\n    \"078\": \"Filename pipeline: only project names become paths and they are validated; revisit if more \"\n           \"user text becomes filenames.\",\n    \"084\": \"Generated-artefact provenance: --check gates already prove freshness for the map, MATRIX and capsules; \"\n           \"revisit for a new generated artefact without a check.\",\n    \"085\": \"Description collisions: ~40 project descriptions are human-written; revisit when the catalogue grows.\",\n    \"086\": \"Single canonical parser: no duplicate frontmatter parsers found (no frontmatter parse functions in \"\n           \"scripts/); revisit if a second Markdown/YAML reader is added.\",\n    \"091\": \"Change-record classifier: gates read the working tree, which suits local use; revisit if changes must \"\n           \"be justified after the fact (audits).\",\n    \"092\": \"Impact-scoped validation: the full gate se