      \"process tier before work, which is this idea.\"),\n    \"346\": (\"Rejected\", P + \"Already implemented for consumers: `idea-catcher ideas --target <t>` returns one \"\n            \"target's open work without reading MATRIX.md.\"),\n    \"292\": (\"Rejected\", P + \"_SYMBOL_CACHE in update_knowledge_base.py is an in-process dict that dies with the \"\n            \"process, so a stale-implementation key cannot outlive a code change.\"),\n    \"028\": (\"Rejected\", OFF + \"conversation compaction and recap are performed by the host, not by AIKit; the \"\n            \"ledger --handoff already carries the next action.\"),\n    \"072\": (\"Rejected\", P + \"Rejected: every regex AIKit runs is its own fixed pattern; no user- or model-supplied \"\n            \"pattern reaches re, so catastrophic-backtracking isolation has nothing to guard.\"),\n    \"079\": (\"Rejected\", OFF + \"AIKit has no range-set selectors; reforge windows are three integers.\"),\n    \"115\": (\"Rejected\", OFF + \"the codebase map does not cluster modules into areas, so there is no identity to stabilise.\"),\n    \"192\": (\"Rejected\", OFF + \"file reads are host tools; AIKit cannot cache or diff them.\"),\n    \"193\": (\"Rejected\", OFF + \"AIKit does not assemble model context, so there is nothing to grade.\"),\n    \"195\": (\"Rejected\", OFF + \"AIKit performs no metered context-saving actions to ledger.\"),\n    \"310\": (\"Rejected\", OFF + \"AIKit does not filter host tool output, so there is no filter to retire.\"),\n    \"311\": (\"Rejected\", OFF + \"AIKit does not trim per-turn context; its budgets are static file sizes.\"),\n    \"408\": (\"Rejected\", OFF + \"single-author repositories; area ownership names one person everywhere.\"),\n    \"424\": (\"Rejected\", OFF + \"AIKit does not intercept or wrap tool results.\"),\n    \"322\": (\"Rejected\", OFF + \"behaviour-tree composite semantics from a game AI dossier; AIKit has no BT runtime.\"),\n    \"325\": (\"Rejected\", OFF + \"behaviour-tree definition validation; AIKit has no BT runtime.\"),\n    \"361\": (\"Rejected\", OFF + \"frame-rate limiter fix from a game-capture framework.\"),\n    \"427\": (\"Rejected\", OFF + \"game-studio feature contracts with per-discipline requirements.\"),\n    \"428\": (\"Rejected\", OFF + \"design-intent/art/engineering traceability matrix for game production.\"),\n    \"515\": (\"Rejected\", OFF + \"bilingual game-design-document schema.\"),\n    \"521\": (\"Rejected\", OFF + \"game settings.json schema (board size, minimax depth).\"),\n    \"549\": (\"Rejected\", OFF + \"Kubernetes DNS-proxy and L3/L4 network-control evidence.\"),\n    \"550\": (\"Rejected\", OFF + \"gVisor/runc isolation-tier attestation.\"),\n    \"584\": (\"Rejected\", OFF + \"mobile device test matrix.\"),\n    \"585\": (\"Rejected\", OFF + \"mobile build/device stamp in Allure reports.\"),\n    \"586\": (\"Rejected\", OFF + \"retry bound to mobile locator/device objects.\"),\n    \"587\": (\"Rejected\", OFF + \"image-matching threshold stamp for device tests.\"),\n    \"105\": (\"Deferred\", P + \"Corrected from Rejected: AIKit writes .claude/settings.json and could ship a PreToolUse \"\n            \"hook, so this is reachable on hosts with hooks. Revisit if agents are seen editing files they never read.\"),\n    \"255\": (\"Deferred\", P + \"Corrected from Rejected: host hooks could count tool calls. Revisit if runaway sessions \"\n            \"appear; enforce only on hosts with hooks.\"),\n    \"482\": (\"Deferred\", P + \"Corrected from Rejected: the tools/idea_catcher.py move (bug under IDEA-406) is this \"\n            \"failure — an entry point moved with no shim. Revisit at the next entry-point move: leave a forwarding \"\n            \"shim and an ADR.\"),\n}\n\nD = {\n    \"004\": \"Thrashing detector: no milestone has been re-checkpointed repeatedly in the ledgers; revisit if one is.\",\n    \"008\": \"Three-zone self-modification policy: agents can still edit GUIDELINES.md and gates; PRINCIPLE-000 forbids \"\n           \"gaming them in prose only. Revisit with IDEA-147 if an agent weakens a gate.\",\n    \"026\": \"Domain packages: `aikit new --kind software|game|science` already seeds per-kind content; revisit if \"\n           \"users ask for richer starters.\",\n    \"035\": \"Rule-quality rubric for .aikit/guidelines.md: project guidelines are few and short; revisit when a \"\n           \"project accumulates stub rules.\",\n    \"036\": \"Debt baseline: three checked projects have zero hygiene findings; revisit when an attached project starts with debt.\",\n    \"042\": \"Shortcut ledger: PRINCIPLE-007 bans TODO/stubs outright, so marked shortcuts would contradict it; \"\n           \"revisit only if that rule is relaxed.\",\n    \"053\": \"Description linter: one skill and six roles; revisit when the skill library grows.\",\n    \"065\": \"log_safe: --resume prints ledger text written by other agents; revisit if multi-agent ledgers carry \"\n           \"untrusted text that could forge [OK] lines.\",\n    \"071\": \"Path representability: Windows device names are already refused for project names; revisit for NFKC \"\n           \"or trailing-dot collisions if reported.\",\n    \"078\": \"Filename pipeline: only project names become paths and they are validated; revisit if more \"\n           \"user text becomes filenames.\",\n    \"084\": \"Generated-artefact provenance: --check gates already prove freshness for the map, MATRIX and capsules; \"\n           \"revisit for a new generated artefact without a check.\",\n    \"085\": \"Description collisions: ~40 project descriptions are human-written; revisit when the catalogue grows.\",\n    \"086\": \"Single canonical parser: no duplicate frontmatter parsers found (no frontmatter parse functions in \"\n           \"scripts/); revisit if a second Markdown/YAML reader is added.\",\n    \"091\": \"Change-record classifier: gates read the working tree, which suits local use; revisit if changes must \"\n           \"be justified after the fact (audits).\",\n    \"092\": \"Impact-scoped validation: the full gate set is affordable at 727 budgeted tests; revisit if Phase 4 gets slow.\",\n    \"098\": \"Settings resolver: precedence is fixed in code across few files; revisit on a precedence bug.\",\n    \"104\": \"Destructive-command matrix: hygiene already checks subprocess call shape; revisit if a destructive git \"\n           \"argument is ever built from user input.\",\n    \"110\": \"Harness capability registry: TIER1_TARGETS already lists hosts; revisit if hosts diverge in features AIKit uses.\",\n    \"112\": \"Identifier normalisation: no two-spellings bug recorded; revisit if one appears (project, task or gate ids).\",\n    \"113\": \"Reverse blast radius: useful but IDEA-009 was superseded; revisit with a concrete refactor that needs it.\",\n    \"119\": \"Calibrated token bound: capsule budgets use a character heuristic with headroom; revisit if a host \"\n           \"truncates a capsule that passed --check.\",\n    \"125\": \"Singleton boundary: no hidden-global bug recorded; revisit if test order dependence appears.\",\n    \"126\": \"Injective framing: ui_contract hashes newline-joined entries; collision needs a newline inside an entry. \"\n           \"Revisit if entries can contain newlines.\",\n    \"133\": \"Projection events: derived files are regenerated and checked; revisit if a projection is trusted while stale.\",\n    \"138\": \"Directory-sync outcome: fsync_dir is a no-op on win32; revisit for POSIX deployments.\",\n    \"140\": \"Measured risk assessment: --risks is prose by design; revisit if plans' risks diverge from what changed.\",\n    \"141\": \"Multi-feature file guard: revisit if a shared-dispatch file regresses one feature while changing another.\",\n    \"142\": \"Rule feedback loop: needs [APPLIES RULES] annotations on plans; revisit with IDEA-217 ablation.\",\n    \"147\": \"Base-held trust manifest: verify_commit judges a commit with gates from that same commit, so a change can \"\n           \"edit its own gate. Revisit with IDEA-008 if any gate weakening is caught.\",\n    \"153\": \"Declared vs observed model: delegate already pins free models per role; revisit if paid fallbacks appear.\",\n    \"158\": \"Commit-pinned module sync: AIKit pulls no remote modules; revisit if it starts.\",\n    \"162\": \"Trace DAG: dogfood logs are short; revisit when subagent transcripts are reviewed regularly.\",\n    \"176\": \"Quality-delta gate: reforge already reports what a commit adds; revisit if quality slides between commits.\",\n    \"177\": \"Symbol notes: invariants live in docstrings and ADRs; revisit if a known gotcha is re-broken.\",\n    \"179\": \"Floor-vs-zero evidence: claim_audit already separates absent/unknown; revisit for other counts.\",\n    \"182\": \"Run manifest: dogfood writes one log; revisit when a dogfood failure cannot be reproduced.\",\n    \"198\": \"Completion distillation: ADRs capture decisions at commit time; revisit if lessons are lost between tasks.\",\n    \"199\": \"ADR locator gate: 0 dangling ADR citations today; fold into IDEA-406's linter if one appears.\",\n    \"200\": \"Machine-evaluable conditions: deferred reasons are now explicit but prose; revisit when the register is re-triaged.\",\n    \"201\": \"Checkpoint decay: ledgers are 10–19 KB, so --resume output is not crowded yet; revisit as they grow.\",\n    \"204\": \"Knowledge delta merge: ADRs are append-only; revisit if knowledge/ pages drift from accepted ADRs.\",\n    \"206\": \"Explore-before-plan: the explorer role exists; revisit if plans skip option comparison and fail.\",\n    \"212\": \"Hash-chained ledger: ledgers are small and agents cannot Edit them (.claude/settings.json); revisit if \"\n           \"an edited checkpoint is ever found.\",\n    \"214\": \"Plan-scope gate: PRINCIPLE-007 already forbids out-of-plan changes; revisit if out-of-plan edits ship.\",\n    \"215\": \"Replay lint for dogfood transcripts: dogfood is deterministic CLI runs; revisit if it gains model calls.\",\n    \"217\": \"Rule ablation: valuable at a model change; revisit when the default model changes and capsules may be stale.\",\n    \"220\": \"Harness checklist gate: most items are already principles; revisit for items not yet gated.\",\n    \"222\": \"Gate taxonomy: gates are pre-flight by nature; revisit if a revision loop without a cap appears.\",\n    \"224\": \"Predicate context: principles are cited by ID already; revisit if briefs paraphrase rules wrongly.\",\n    \"225\": \"Tests-only auditor: the tester role writes tests; revisit if it edits implementation.\",\n    \"226\": \"Requirement coverage: revisit if a milestone ships without the requirement it named.\",\n    \"228\": \"History vs liveness split: ledger holds both but is tiny; revisit if heartbeats are added.\",\n    \"229\": \"Cross-provider review: delegate can run a reviewer on another provider; revisit to record the SHA \"\n           \"when that becomes routine.\",\n    \"231\": \"Deletion tombstones: AIKit deletes only temp buffers (clean); revisit if state files are ever garbage-collected.\",\n    \"232\": \"Ledger export: every host already reads the same files; revisit if another tool must import AIKit state.\",\n    \"235\": \"Skill eval harness: one skill; revisit when skills multiply.\",\n    \"236\": \"Third-party skill scanner: no skill intake path; revisit if skills are installed from outside.\",\n    \"238\": \"Contract-keyed regeneration: generation is fast; revisit if regeneration becomes slow or model-based.\",\n    \"239\": \"Staged candidates: media candidates already await review before apply; revisit for other generators.\",\n    \"241\": \"Narrow storage interfaces: state helpers are shared functions; revisit if a second backend is needed.\",\n    \"242\": \"Persona reviewers: revisit if single-reviewer audits miss doc defects.\",\n    \"243\": \"Design drift report: architecture.md is prose; revisit with IDEA-300.\",\n    \"244\": \"Brief-to-draft gate: revisit if large features start without an approved design.\",\n    \"245\": \"Multi-host plugin: AIKit syncs eight hosts by files; revisit if users want one-command install.\",\n    \"247\": \"Append-only ledger: ledgers are 10–19 KB, so whole-file rewrites are cheap; revisit above ~1 MB.\",\n    \"254\": \"Learning capture: `aikit guideline --source user` records user rules; revisit if corrections are lost.\",\n    \"256\": \"STOP file: `reforge stop` covers the only long loop; revisit if another loop is added.\",\n    \"258\": \"Touched-surface audits: revisit when an optional audit (publish, media) is skipped and breaks.\",\n    \"259\": \"Core regression tier: the full suite is fast enough; revisit if the inner loop slows.\",\n    \"261\": \"Optional capability registry: subcommands are the registry; revisit if optional features multiply.\",\n    \"263\": \"Plan fits context: revisit if a milestone fails from context exhaustion.\",\n    \"264\": \"Instruction compile lint: sync_principles --check validates schema; revisit with IDEA-406.\",\n    \"271\": \"Strict reference resolution: revisit if a typo in a gate or principle id is silently dropped.\",\n    \"273\": \"Plan attestation: PRINCIPLE-004 makes the ledger plan authoritative after compaction; revisit if an agent \"\n           \"acts on a reconstructed plan.\",\n    \"274\": \"Worker journal: subagents report through their final message; revisit if findings get lost.\",\n    \"275\": \"Environment doctor: `aikit fix`, --audit and status cover it; revisit if environment failures go undiagnosed.\",\n    \"280\": \"Local overlay: `aikit guideline` writes tracked rules on purpose; revisit if machine-specific rules leak in.\",\n    \"281\": \"Truncation contract: revisit if a gate failure tail cuts the line that explains it.\",\n    \"290\": \"Trace learning loop: revisit when transcripts are collected systematically.\",\n    \"296\": \"Reuse table: PRINCIPLE-003 R2 requires a call-site grep; revisit with IDEA-005's reuse digest.\",\n    \"297\": \"Irreversible-action classifier: AIKit never force-pushes; revisit if a destructive step runs unasked.\",\n    \"298\": \"Claim falsification: revisit if commit messages claim behaviour the diff lacks.\",\n    \"299\": \"Deletion intent: IDEA-262 catches large deletions first; revisit if a deletion drops behaviour silently.\",\n    \"300\": \"Architecture spine lint: revisit if architecture.md is found wrong.\",\n    \"301\": \"Path-scoped capsules: --involved gives principle lookup; revisit if Tier 1 outgrows its budget.\",\n    \"302\": \"Pre-code artefact budget: revisit if Track C paperwork outgrows the change.\",\n    \"305\": \"As-of projection: revisit for a post-mortem that needs past ledger state.\",\n    \"306\": \"Risk-weighted ordering: revisit if failure triage time becomes a problem.\",\n    \"307\": \"Capability-gated skips: revisit if tests fail on machines without git/network/browser.\",\n    \"308\": \"Side-effect receipts: revisit if publish or push reports success that did not happen.\",\n    \"312\": \"Immutable records with active pointer: revisit for media or license artefacts needing rollback.\",\n    \"313\": \"Scoped sub-agent view: read-only roles are enforced by tool lists; revisit if a role writes outside scope.\",\n    \"314\": \"Optimistic commit: the ledger lock is held only for a short read-modify-write; revisit if waits appear.\",\n    \"315\": \"Cost-ordered gates: revisit if an expensive gate runs before a cheap one that would fail.\",\n    \"318\": \"Revisioned entries: history fields record changes; revisit if lost updates appear in the register.\",\n    \"319\": \"Bounded handoff: --handoff exists with parse_handoff; revisit to add citations/omissions if handoffs fail.\",\n    \"332\": \"Failure evidence capture: revisit if deep dogfood failures cannot be diagnosed.\",\n    \"336\": \"Lock lease with incarnation: lock holds are short; revisit if a reused PID steals a live lock.\",\n    \"340\": \"Frozen adapter surface: host files are generated from one source; revisit if adapters gain code.\",\n    \"347\": \"Detector registry: the map is Python-AST only, so non-Python projects get thin maps; revisit when a \"\n           \"non-Python project needs one.\",\n    \"348\": \"Impact-scoped repair admission: revisit if reforge auto-repairs touch widely imported code.\",\n    \"349\": \"Test-impact map: revisit if reforge verification gets slow.\",\n    \"358\": \"Heartbeat lock: lock holds are short; revisit if a long holder is ever broken at 30 s.\",\n    \"360\": \"Completion admissibility: revisit if tasks complete with open review findings.\",\n    \"362\": \"Skill compatibility version: revisit when skills are shared across AIKit versions.\",\n    \"363\": \"Out-of-band diagnostics: revisit if instrumentation slows a gate.\",\n    \"364\": \"Staged replace: atomic writes already validate before swap in most generators; revisit with IDEA-398.\",\n    \"367\": \"Expiring overrides: `hygiene: allow` markers never expire; revisit if stale markers accumulate.\",\n    \"373\": \"Finding fingerprints: revisit if gate output repeats one defect many times.\",\n    \"377\": \"Output round-trip: revisit if a --json output fails to parse for a consumer.\",\n    \"378\": \"Blind review: revisit if reviews echo the author's rationale instead of checking the diff.\",\n    \"381\": \"Sitting-based durations: revisit if task durations are reported.\",\n    \"384\": \"Capability contracts: revisit if a named dependency is replaced.\",\n    \"386\": \"Bundle integrity manifest: AIKit is not installed as a bundle; revisit if it is.\",\n    \"387\": \"Three-way upgrade: same condition as IDEA-386.\",\n    \"388\": \"Defect re-entry: revisit if a late defect forces redoing a whole task.\",\n    \"395\": \"Elapsed-time plausibility: revisit if checkpoints claim