e map has no clusters whose identity could drift.\n\n**Corrections to my own earlier verdicts:**\n- **105 and 255:** I had rejected these as needing host hooks AIKit doesn't control. But AIKit writes `.claude/settings.json`, which can hold hooks, and approved IDEA-262 is itself a hook. Both are now Deferred.\n- **482, deprecation without deletion:** the `tools/idea_catcher.py` path bug under IDEA-406 is exactly this failure: an entry point moved with no forwarding shim left behind. It's now Deferred, with \"leave a shim at the next entry-point move\" as the condition.\n\n**Kept as Rejected:** the 25 already-built rejections keep their recorded evidence. The 11 earlier rejections for having nothing to use them survived the re-read and still stand (archives, plugin command names, encrypted envelopes, container reaping and similar). IDEA-107 belongs to a decision made by another agent, `kilo:main`, so I left it alone.\n\n**Worth a decision when you have time:**\n- **147 + 008:** `verify_commit` runs the gates from the commit being judged, so a change could weaken its own gate. These stay deferred until that is actually caught happening.\n- **412 + 498:** agents read dossier text taken from untrusted repositories, which is a prompt-injection path. Both are deferred until a hostile repository is actually reviewed.\n\nNothing was committed (the register is git-ignored). A backup from before this pass is at `C:\\Users\\YUNUS-~1\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\c--Users-Yunus-Emre-Desktop-portable-agent-kit\\05aa96e5-db7a-4aed-bad4-f0f3cebd2787\\scratchpad\\ideas.before-aikit-pass2.json`.\n\nThe neurocore Deferred and Rejected ideas haven't had this kind of re-read yet. They already have individual reasons, but I haven't checked them against their blueprints. I can do that next if you want."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":300,"cache_read_input_tokens":273120,"output_t