NCIPLE-001 R4)\"]\n864\t    seen: Dict[str, int] = {}\n865\t    for line in (l.strip() for l in text[heading.end():].splitlines()):\n866\t        if not line:\n867\t            continue\n868\t        rule = _GUIDELINE_RULE.match(line)\n869\t        if not rule:\n870\t            errors.append(f\"'{line[:60]}' is not '- **G-NNN** (source): rule' (PRINCIPLE-001 R4)\")\n871\t            continue\n872\t        gid = rule.group(1)\n873\t        seen[gid] = seen.get(gid, 0) + 1\n874\t        if seen[gid] == 2:\n875\t            errors.append(f\"{gid} is used twice; each rule keeps its own ID (PRINCIPLE-001 R4)\")\n876\t        if _GUIDELINE_OVERRIDE.search(rule.group(3)):\n877\t            errors.append(f\"{gid} overrides a principle; project guidelines only add to them (PRINCIPLE-000 R6)\")\n878\t    return errors\n879\t\n880\t\n881\tdef memory_dir(root: Path) -> Path:\n882\t    \"\"\"Where `root` keeps its map and decisions: a project's `.aikit/`, else `knowledge/`.\n883\t\n884\t    The `.aikit/project.json` marker decides, so a tool state folder inside AIKit (Reforge writes\n885\t    `.aikit/reforge.json`) cannot hide AIKit's own `knowledge/` (ADR-253).\n886\t    \"\"\"\n887\t    memory = root / \".aikit\"\n888\t    if memory.is_dir() and ((memory / \"project.json\").is_file() or not (root / \".agents\").is_dir()):\n889\t        return memory\n890\t    return root / \"knowledge\"\n891\t\n892\t\n893\tdef check_workspace(root: Path = ROOT_DIR) -> bool:\n894\t    \"\"\"\n895\t    Every read-only audit of `--check`, for AIKit or for a project it builds: the codebase map\n896\t    (a project's only once `aikit fix` has written one), the full PRINCIPLE-005 README audit,\n897\t    unfinished code, code structure and the ADR register. One code path, so a project is held to\n898\t    exactly AIKit's checks; a size-only README check let a README listing nine deleted files pass\n899\t    (ADR-128). Reports every failure before returning, never stopping at the first.\n900\t    \"\"\"\n901\t    memory = memory_dir(root)\n902\t    ok = True\n903\t    map_path = memory / \"codebase_map.md\"\n904\t    if map_path.is_file() or root == ROOT_DIR:\n905\t        rel = map_path.relative_to(root)\n906\t        if check_codebase_map_freshness(memory, root=root, strict=False):\n907\t            print(f\"[OK] {rel} is fresh and synchronized with the AST.\")\n908\t        else:\n909\t            # The exact command for this folder: a project's stale map used to point at AIKit's.\n910\t            remedy = (\"python scripts/update_knowledge_base.py\" if root == ROOT_DIR\n911\t                      else f'python scripts/update_knowledge_base.py --workspace \"{root}\"')\n912\t            print(f\"[FAIL] {rel} is stale. Fix: run `{remedy}`.\")\n913\t            ok = False\n914\t    ok = report_readme(check_readme(root)) and ok\n915\t    ok = report_lazy_code(check_lazy_code(root)) and ok\n916\t    ok = report_architecture(check_architecture(root)) and ok\n917\t    guidelines = memory / \"guidelines.md\"\n918\t    if guidelines.is_file():\n919\t        rel = guidelines.relative_to(root)\n920\t        errors = guideline_errors(guidelines.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n921\t        for error in errors:\n922\t            print(f\"[FAIL] {rel}: {error}\")\n923\t        if errors:\n924\t            print(\"   Why: a project's guidelines add rules below AIKit's principles; a broken or overriding \"\n925\t                  \"rule would be read differently by each agent.\")\n926\t            print(\"   Fix: correct each line above, or rewrite the rule as a constraint the principles allow.\")\n927\t        else:\n928\t            print(f\"[OK] {rel}: every rule is well-formed and adds to the principles.\")\n929\t        ok = ok and not errors\n930\t    decisions = memory / \"decisions.md\"\n931\t    if decisions.is_file():\n932\t        rel = decisions.relative_to(root)\n933\t        errors = audit_adr_register(decisions.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n934\t        for