CONCEPTS.md footer and an import comment) still told users to run `python tools/idea_catcher.py`, which no longer exists. The README gate checks only `python scripts/*.py`, and only in README.md, so nothing noticed (IDEA-406).\r","+- **Decision**: The hints now name the documented `python aikit.py idea-catcher <command>`. `update_knowledge_base.py --check` gains `audit_script_references`: every `python <path>.py` in AIKit's tracked code, Markdown and host instruction files must name an existing file. The append-only ADR register, `tests/`, `projects/`, `references/`, `scratch/` and `licenses/` are not scanned; a `hygiene: allow <reason>` marker on the line or the line above exempts an example or a path inside a named project. The audit runs for the AIKit root only.\r","+- **Consequences**: A moved or deleted entry point fails `--check` with `file:line` instead of shipping dead hints; on the pre-change tree the audit reports 12 references (the 10 above plus two that are now marked). Projects are not covered: their docs name AIKit's own `aikit.py` and `scripts/`, which live in the AIKit folder, so all 44 projects measured would fail; extending it needs AIKit-relative resolution first. `git ls-files` moved into a shared `tracked_files()` used by the README audit too.\r","+- **Cross-principle check**: no principle section changed. Serves PRINCIPLE-003 (a printed command is grounded in a real file), PRINCIPLE-005 (documented commands resolve), PRINCIPLE-011 R6 (a `Fix:` line must work) and PRINCIPLE-016 (the knowledge check owns reference integrity)."]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["C:\\Users\\Yunus-Emre\\Desktop\\portable_agent_kit\\knowledge\\decisions.md"]}},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"662b43da-1db9-4f44-abdc-81b05cfa92e9","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/c/Users/Yunus-Emre/Desktop/portable_agent_kit","root":"/c/Users/Yunus-Emre/Desktop/portable_agent_kit","branch":"main","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":10,"un