{"parentUuid":"5445a23a-26c5-4024-9313-1f6643d69a03","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgX4Y1jLCiEuxuTgrkEy3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"IDEA-406 is implemented and all of Phase 4 passed. Nothing is committed yet, because your host settings only allow commits you explicitly ask for.\n\n**The bug fix.** All ten idea-catcher hints that told you to run `python tools/idea_catcher.py` now say `python aikit.py idea-catcher <command>`. You can see it working: after `set-status`, the tool now prints `next: python aikit.py idea-catcher render`, which runs. The broken path came from commit `63759e3`, which removed the standalone Idea Catcher without updating its messages.\n\n**The new guard.** `update_knowledge_base.py --check` now flags any `python <path>.py`, in AIKit's code, Markdown or host instruction files, that points at a file that doesn't exist. It reports each one as `file:line`.\n- **Proof it works:** run against the committed versions of the files I changed, it reports 12 problems: the 10 hints plus 2 legitimate references, which I've now marked with `hygiene: allow <reason>`. On the current tree it reports none.\n- **Scope:** it skips the append-only ADR file, tests and other repositories.\n- **AIKit only, not projects:** every project's docs name `aikit.py`, which lives in AIKit's folder, so all 44 projects would fail. That limit is recorded in ADR-280.\n- **One mistake along the way:** I wrote this check before its test. I made up for it by confirming the tests fail against the committed code before trusting them. The tests also caught a real problem: the allow marker needs a first word of at least three characters, which my first markers didn't have.\n\n**Phase 4 results:**\n\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| Both test tiers | 732 tests pass within budget (44 s) |\n| Read-only gates | Sync, knowledge base, reachability, secrets, licenses and hygiene all pass |\n| Dogfood | 5 of 5 tracks |\n\nAn earlier run had an integration timeout and slow `--help` startup. Both passed on re-run, so they were load on the machine, not this change.\n\n**Also updated:**\n- The README's `--check` row mentions the new failure.\n- ADR-280 is added, and the codebase map is regenerated.\n- The task ledger has a Phase 4 checkpoint.\n- IDEA-406 is marked Integrating in the register; it becomes Integrated once committed.\n\nThese 10 files are modified and uncommitted, matching the change exactly:\n- `README.md`, `knowledge/decisions.md`, `knowledge/codebase_map.md`\n- `idea_catcher/registry.py`, `idea_catcher/concept_map.py`\n- `scripts/update_knowledge_base.py`, `scripts/project_media.py`, `scripts/ui_contract.py`\n- `tests/test_kit.py`, `.agents/task_ledger.json`\n\nSay \"commit\" and I'll commit them as `fix(idea-catcher): name the live entry point and check python script references`. Next on the list is IDEA-398: marked blocks so regenerating files stops overwriting your own content.\n\nSeparately, the PNN project's docs mention three scripts that don't exist: `scripts/analyze_pk.py`, `scripts/analyze_wfa.py` and `scripts/property_filter.py`. That's outside this change, so I left it alone."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":243,"cache_read_input_tokens":330154,"output_tokens":1100,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":243,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1100,"cache_read_input_tokens":330154,"cache_creation_input_tokens":243,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":243},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverCl