{"parentUuid":"45a874b6-83c9-44f4-9512-24d9c9933ef4","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"a96664c9-b051-4537-af91-e4f15164d542","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015EZMnTRPZtCv1aFG7k3Mpc","type":"tool_result","content":".idea-catcher/dossiers/game-ai-framework-swordsmancat.md\n.idea-catcher/dossiers/gsd-core.md\n### `IDEA-262`: Write-shrink and path guard hooks\n- **Target Project**: `aikit`\n- **Priority / Effort vs. Impact**: `High Impact / Low Effort`\n\n#### Core Mechanism & Value\nGSD ships guard hooks that run on tool calls: a secret-file guard, a **write-shrink** guard (flags a write that makes a file far smaller, a common sign that an agent overwrote content), a worktree-path guard and a prompt-injection guard. They are deterministic scripts, not model calls.\n\n#### Potential Improvements\nA write-shrink guard directly protects AIKit's data-loss concerns (PRINCIPLE-013): before a commit, compare each staged file's size with HEAD and flag a drop above a threshold unless the plan names that file for reduction. The secret-file guard complements `check_secrets.py` by also blocking reads or writes of credential paths.\n\n#### Potential Weaknesses\nLegitimate deletions and refactors trigger it. Thresholds are arbitrary. Hooks may not run on every host.\n\n#### How to Combat These\nIgnore files under a minimum size, report instead of blocking at first, and allow an explicit `shrink-ok: <reason>` line in the checkpoint description. Run the same check in the pre-commit gate so it does not depend on host hooks.\n\n#### Cold-Start Agent Implementation Blueprint\n1. **Target Workspace & Pre-Flight Command**:\n   - Workspace: root AIKit repo\n   - Resume/Status: `python scripts/disruption_recovery.py --resume`\n2. **Target Files & Symbols to Modify/Create**:\n   - `scripts/check_shrink.py` (new): `shrunk(files: dict[str, tuple[int, int]], ratio, min_size) -> list[str]`, `staged_sizes()`\n   - Wire into the pre-commit gate; find it with `git grep -w -e check_secrets scripts/`\n3. **Contract & DTO Specification**:\n   - `files` maps path to `(old_size, new_size)`; flag when `new < old * ratio` and `old >= min_size`; defaults `ratio=0.5`, `min_size=400`\n   - Git calls use `subprocess.run(..., timeout=10)`; the pure function takes sizes so unit tests spawn nothing\n4. **Failing-First Test Specification (PRINCIPLE-014)**:\n   - Test file: `tests/test_check_shrink.py`\n   - Cases to assert: a 70% drop is flagged; a small file is ignored; a growing file passes; a new file passes; a `shrink-ok` reason clears the flag\n5. **Step-by-Step Integration Sequence**:\n   - Step 1: Write the failing test.\n   - Step 2: Implement the pure function and the staged-size reader.\n   - Step 3: Add it to the gate as a warning, run the AIKit gates and record the ADR.\n\n### `IDEA-263`: Plan-fits-context fit check per milestone\n- **Target Project**: `aikit`\n- **Priority / Effort vs. Impact**: `Medium Impact / Low Effort`\n\n#### Core Mechanism & Value\nThe plan step verifies that each plan fits a fresh context window, because quality degrades as context fills (context rot), and each executor then starts clean. The fit check happens before execution, not after degradation shows.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"af0d9d40-88a2-4e14-9ccc-80a7e71d05ac","timestamp":"2026-10-29T19:20:23.422Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":".idea-catcher/dossiers/game-ai-framework-swordsmancat.md\n.idea-catcher/dossiers/gsd-core.md\n### `IDEA-262`: Write-shrink and path guard hooks\n- **Target Project**: `aikit`\n- **Priority / Effort vs. Impact**: `High Impact / Low Effort`\n\n#### Core Mechanism & Value\nGSD ships guard hooks that run on tool calls: a secret-file guard, a **write-shrink** guard (flags a write that makes a file far smaller, a common sign that an agent overwrote content), a worktree-path guard and a prompt-injection guard. They are deterministic scripts, not model calls.\n\n#### Potential Improvements\nA write-shrink guard directly prot