dStart":3070,"oldLines":3,"newStart":3070,"newLines":11,"lines":[" - **Decision**: `scripts/marked_blocks.py` owns the convention: `markers`, `block_span`, `fenced` and `replace_block` for `<!-- aegean:<name>:start/end -->` pairs. The License section now writes its generated paragraph between `aegean:license` markers under the heading; a refresh replaces only that paragraph. A README without the markers takes the previous path once (its first License section is replaced, now marked). The media, screenshots and brand-assets blocks use the same helper; a differential run over 20 README shapes produced identical bytes before and after.\r"," - **Consequences**: A user's own text in the License section, or anywhere outside a block, survives every refresh. Each project's README gains the two invisible license markers at its next license write; no README is rewritten by this change. A user who edits inside a block still loses that edit, which is the contract the markers state. A reversed or unmatched pair is not a block, so the old path runs instead of cutting text.\r"," - **Cross-principle check**: no principle section changed. Serves PRINCIPLE-003 (a generator edits only text it can prove it wrote), PRINCIPLE-005 (README refreshes stay exact), PRINCIPLE-009 (one helper replaces three copies) and PRINCIPLE-013 (generated output never destroys user state).\r","+\r","+### ADR-282: Post-Commit Verification Warns When a Commit Halves a File\r","+- **Date**: 2026-10-29\r","+- **Status**: Accepted\r","+- **Context**: A file an agent overwrote by mistake passes every gate: the tests, the map and the secret scan judge what is there, not what went missing (IDEA-262). Nothing compared a commit's files with its parent's. Measured over AIKit's 334 commits, no accidental overwrite of this kind is on record: the guard is preventive, and the earlier note that it would have caught the README repair in 4ec9ffa was wrong, since that fix repaired added and mislabelled lines, not a shrink.\r","+- **Decision**: `verify_commit.py` lists the parent's and the commit's trees (`git ls-tree -r -l -z`, two reads) and warns for every modified file of at least 400 bytes left under half its size, naming both sizes with Why/Fix. Added, deleted and `task_ledger.json` files are skipped (a ledger is pruned by its own commands and keeps a `.bak`). A `shrink-ok: <reason>` line in the commit message clears the warning. It is a warning: the exit code, the PRINCIPLE-018 R3 gate list and the principle text are unchanged.\r","+- **Consequences**: Over the same history the rule warns on 3 of 334 commits (a license swap, an architecture page cut to a generated one, AGENTS.md becoming a capsule), all intended and each a fair place for a `shrink-ok:` line; ledger prunes no longer warn. A content loss under half a file, or in a file under 400 bytes, is not seen. Promoting it to a failure would be a principle change and needs its own ADR.\r","+- **Cross-principle check**: no principle section changed. Serves PRINCIPLE-013 (lost content is data loss), PRINCIPLE-018 R7 (the commit is judged alone, before the push) and PRINCIPLE-011 R6 (the warning carries Why/Fix)."]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["C:\\Users\\Yunus-Emre\\Desktop\\portable_agent_kit\\knowledge\\codebase_map.md","C:\\Users\\Yunus-Emre\\Desktop\\portable_agent_kit\\knowledge\\decisions.md"]}},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"c376e7d0-7711-425e-835d-4e9fdea28872","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/c/Users/Yunus-Emre/Desktop/portable_agent_kit","root":"/c/Users/Yunus-Emre/Desktop/portable_agent_kit","branch":"main","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":12,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":1},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"AegeanWorks/AIKit","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"AegeanWorks/AIKit","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"gi