{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"05aa96e5-db7a-4aed-bad4-f0f3cebd2787","hash":"2a3c5114a8f646c4c4aaadc6a8efaadb0a2933931ae72f8ceb308e816d0e761d","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Q2yw4iZ6wSPZ7AthZYmYhJ","name":"Edit","input":{"file_path":"c:\\Users\\Yunus-Emre\\Desktop\\portable_agent_kit\\README.md","old_string":"exits 1 when the commit holds less than the tree it was tested in (PRINCIPLE-018 R7)|","new_string":"exits 1 when the commit holds less than the tree it was tested in (PRINCIPLE-018 R7); warns on a file cut below half its size unless the message says `shrink-ok: <reason>`|"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01L7LTrNUSy1PgFFHKUb7oQa","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd \"C:/Users/Yunus-Emre/Desktop/portable_agent_kit\"; python - <<'E'\nadr = \"\"\"\n### ADR-282: Post-Commit Verification Warns When a Commit Halves a File\n- **Date**: 2026-10-29\n- **Status**: Accepted\n- **Context**: A file an agent overwrote by mistake passes every gate: the tests, the map and the secret scan judge what is there, not what went missing (IDEA-262). Nothing compared a commit's files with its parent's. Measured over AIKit's 334 commits, no accidental overwrite of this kind is on record: the guard is preventive, and the earlier note that it would have caught the README repair in 4ec9ffa was wrong, since that fix repaired added and mislabelled lines, not a shrink.\n- **Decision**: `verify_commit.py` lists the parent's and the commit's trees (`git ls-tree -r -l -z`, two reads) and warns for every modified file of at least 400 bytes left under half its size, naming both sizes with Why/Fix. Added, deleted and `task_ledger.json` files are skipped (a ledger is pruned by its own commands and keeps a `.bak`). A `shrink-ok: <reason>` line in the commit message clears the warning. It is a warning: the exit code, the PRINCIPLE-018 R3 gate list and the principle text are unchanged.\n- **Consequences**: Over the same history the rule warns on 3 of 334 commits (a license swap, an architecture page cut to a generated one, AGENTS.md becoming a capsule), all intended and each a fair place for a `shrink-ok:` line; ledger prunes no longer warn. A content loss under half a file, or in a file under 400 bytes, is not seen. Promoting it to a failure would be a principle change and needs its own ADR.\n- **Cross-principle check**: no principle section changed. Serves PRINCIPLE-013 (lost content is data loss), PRINCIPLE-018 R7 (the commit is judged alone, before the push) and PRINCIPLE-011 R6 (the warning carries Why/Fix).\n\"\"\"\np='knowledge/decisions.md'\nb=open(p,'rb').read()\nopen(p,'wb').write(b + adr.replace('\\n','\\r\\n').encode('utf-8'))\nE\npython - <<'E'\nimport subprocess,sys; sys.path.insert(0,'.')\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom scripts.verify_commit import shrink_warnings, run_command\nshas=subprocess.run(['git','rev-list','HEAD'],capture_output=True,text=True).stdout.split()\nprint(sum(1 for s in shas if any(l.startswith('[WARN]') for l in shrink_warnings(s,Path('.'),run_command))),'of',len(shas))\nE\npython scripts/update_knowledge_base.py 2>&1 | grep -E \"FAIL|ADR\"","description":"Append ADR-282, re-measure, regenerate knowledge","timeout":600000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
