{"parentUuid":"7bc1f47c-d21a-4a32-acde-754a26c1e637","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"a96664c9-b051-4537-af91-e4f15164d542","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AVeSoLftG5YprMqUEDsS2Q","type":"tool_result","content":"#### Core Mechanism & Value\nIn `base-research.md` (Section 1.5: *Multi-level Layered Architecture - Cognitive Compression*) and Cell 11 of the orchestrator notebook, the author addresses small context windows by distilling repositories into multi-depth representations: instead of injecting full files or a massive symbol catalog, a model can read a highly compressed \"attractor\" index (module name + 1-line core responsibility \n#### Potential Improvements\n- In large AIKit projects like `NeuroCore`, `.aikit/codebase_map.md` is **6,862 lines** (~260 KB). A cold-start agent or free OpenCode subagent (`PRINCIPLE-012`) cannot read a 6,862-line codebase map at once (`PRINCIPLE-004 R5` caps reads at $\\le 100$ lines).\n- Adding a **Tier-0 Compressed Module Directory** table at the top of `codebase_map.md` (or via `python scripts/update_knowledge_base.py --summary`) gives cold-start agents a 1-line-per-module overview (path, line count, module docstring summary, and class/function count) before the detailed symbol listings.\n#### Potential Weaknesses\n- If the summary table duplicates every function name, it bloats `codebase_map.md` further and increases diff churn on minor edits.\n#### How to Combat These\n- **Module-Level Digest Only**: Bound each row in the top-of-file index or `--summary` output to `(Module Path, Lines, Classes/Funcs Count, 1-line Docstring Capsule <= 80 chars)`.\n- Zero extra files required if exposed as a CLI flag `python scripts/update_knowledge_base.py --summary [--workspace <path>]` that prints a terse $\\le 100$-line cognitive-compressed index on stdout.\n#### Cold-Start Agent Implementation Blueprint\n1. **Target Workspace & Pre-Flight Command**:\n   - Workspace: `AIKit` root (`c:/Users/Yunus-Emre/Desktop/portable_agent_kit`)\n   - Resume/Status: `python scripts/disruption_recovery.py --resume`\n2. **Target Files & Symbols to Modify/Create**:\n   - `scripts/update_knowledge_base.py`: Add `render_compact_digest(root: Path) -> str` and CLI flag `--digest` (or `--summary`) to print a 1-line-per-module cognitive compression of any workspace.\n3. **Contract & DTO Specification**:\n   - `def render_compact_digest(root: Path) -> str`: Uses the existing AST extractor (`extract_python_files` / `extract_python_symbols`) to emit a compact Markdown table `| Module | Lines | Symbols | Purpose |`.\n4. **Failing-First Test Specification (PRINCIPLE-014)**:\n   - Test file: `tests/test_unit.py`\n   - Cases to assert:\n     - `test_render_compact_digest_summarizes_modules_within_budget`: Verifies every Python module is listed with its docstring summary and symbol counts, and `--digest` exits 0 in $<250\\text{ms}$.\n5. **Step-by-Step Integration Sequence**:\n   - Step 1: Inspect `scripts/update_knowledge_base.py` CLI parsing and symbol extraction.\n=====\n#### Core Mechanism & Value\nThe source builds a no-model digest of top-level symbols per folder under a character budget, prioritizing shared-code folders (`utils`, `lib`, `common`, `service`, `core`, `schema`, `api`) so \"reuse what already exists\" costs no search. AIKit already has an AST-based `codebase_map.md`, which is more exact; what is missing is a small, prioritized slice an agent can read in one step (PRINCIPLE-004 \n#### Potential Improvements\n- `update_knowledge_base.py --digest [--chars 2000]` prints a budgeted digest, shared folders first.\n#### Potential Weaknesses\nDesign-level: a hard budget silently truncates, so an agent may assume absent symbols do not exist; the source regex also misses nested or dynamic definitions.\n#### How to Combat These\nEnd the digest with an explicit `truncated: N folders omitted` line; derive symbols from the existing AST map rather than regexes; ensure output is deterministic (sorted) so it is cacheable.\n#### Cold-Start Agent Implementation Blueprint\n1. **Target Workspace & Pre-Flight Command**: workspace `c:/Users/Yunus-Emre/Desktop/portable_agent_kit`; `python scripts/disruption_recovery.py --resume`.\n2. **Target Files & Symbols**: `scripts/update_knowledge_base.py` add `build_digest(symbols_by_folder, budget)`; reuse its existing symbol extraction.\n3. **Contract & DTO Specification**:\n   ```python\n   SHARED_HINTS = (\"util\", \"helper\", \"lib\", \"common\", \"shared\", \"service\", \"core\", \"schema\", \"api\")\n   def build_digest(symbols_by_folder: dict[str, list[str]], budget: int = 2000) -> str:\n       \"\"\"Return at most `budget` chars; shared folders first; last line states truncation.\"\"\"\n   ```\n4. **Failing-First Test Specification**: output length `<= budget`; a `utils/` folder appears before an `app/` folder when only one fits; a truncated digest ends with `truncated:`; identical input gives identical output.\n5. **Step-by-Step Integration Sequence**: read the map generator and tests; write failing tests; implement; add the `--digest` flag; document; run suite and gates.\n6. **Verification & Rollback**: unit tests; the flag is additive; revert to roll back.\n### `IDEA-045`: Fair-Baseline A/B Arms Eval with Correctness Gate, Adversarial Safety Tier & Median Aggregation\n- **Target Project**: `neurocore`\n- **Priority / Effort vs. Impact**: `Med-High Impact / Med Effort`\n#### Core Mechanism & Value\n=====","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"a159f489-26e2-4719-a712-1f29cb85ead1","timestamp":"2026-10-29T19:26:03.584Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"#### Core Mechanism & Value\nIn `base-research.md` (Section 1.5: *Multi-level Layered Architecture - Cognitive Compression*) and Cell 11 of the orchestrator notebook, the author addresses small context windows by distilling repositories into multi-depth representations: instead of injecting full files or a massive symbol catalog, a model can read a highly compressed \"attractor\