{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"05aa96e5-db7a-4aed-bad4-f0f3cebd2787","hash":"481cfd541947fbf3b421d2103df6ed825fbe5f1e0fa8db0f57a7e06c1e45f03c","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01J1iJthPYFQoRfxxDzfAtcm","type":"tool_result","content":"14\t---\n15\t\n16\t## 🌐 Host Client Operation Matrix\n17\t\n18\t- **Antigravity**: Native chat harness. Discovers this skill via `.agents/skills/aikit/SKILL.md` and rule files in `.agents/rules/`.\n19\t- **Claude (Code CLI / Desktop)**: Reads `CLAUDE.md` automatically on startup. Discovers this skill natively via `.claude/skills/aikit/SKILL.md`. Executes kit commands directly via terminal tool calls.\n20\t- **OpenCode**: Runs headless subagent profiles (`architect`, `coder`, `tester`, etc.) via `opencode run --standalone` and slash commands via `opencode.jsonc`.\n21\t- **Cursor / VS Code / Windsurf / Cline**: Loads `.cursorrules`, `.github/copilot-instructions.md`, `.windsurfrules`, `.clinerules`. Runs terminal commands.\n22\t- **State SSOT**: All clients interact with workspace state strictly through `python scripts/disruption_recovery.py` and `.agents/task_ledger.json` (a project's: `.aikit/task_ledger.json`).\n23\t\n24\t---\n25\t\n26\t## 🧱 Projects: Building Software Other Than AIKit (PRINCIPLE-011 R8)\n27\tThe user's software lives in its own project, never in AIKit's tree:\n28\t```bash\n29\tpython aikit.py list                 # which projects exist\n30\tpython aikit.py new <name> --description \"<10-350 chars>\" [--topic <t>]... [--kind software|game|science]  # own repo + .aikit memory; auto-detects UI, generates model logo/social candidates (POLLINATIONS_API_KEY) or local fallback, writes media pending; --publish refuses until logo/social are reviewed and applied (ADR-243)\n31\tpython aikit.py attach <path>        # an existing folder: adds .aikit/ memory and an AIKit Integrated badge under its README title (uncommitted)\n32\tpython aikit.py status <name>        # its task, changes, latest decision and its gates\n33\tpython aikit.py check <name>         # its Phase 4: tests, stack gates, hygiene, guidelines, secret scan; exit 0 to commit; never pushes, add --push only when push delivery is authorized (PRINCIPLE-018 R4)\n34\tpython aikit.py guideline <name> \"<rule>\" --source user   # a project rule, below the principles\n35\tpython aikit.py publish <name> [--public] [--owner <org>] [--license auto]  # its own GitHub repo with the README description, the recorded AI-chosen topics and an AI-chosen license; needs a 10-350 char README paragraph; only when the user asks\n36\tpython aikit.py license <name> [--suggest [--json]|--set software|game|science|--restrict]  # AL-1.1, AGL-1.1 (DRM-free games) or ASL-1.1 (science); --restrict, only when the user asks, makes later versions All Rights Reserved from HEAD (earlier releases keep their license), drops COMMERCIAL.md, blocks publish --public, and allows check --push or publish only to a repository gh reports private (ADR-214)\n37\tpython aikit.py topics <name> --brief --json   # bounded evidence for an AI to choose tags; no tag chosen automatically\n38\tpython aikit.py topics <name> --from-file <json> [--apply]  # record the AI's choice; apply only with --apply (ADR-236)\n39\tpython aikit.py topics <name> --review [--json]  # audit current/recorded tags without choosing\n40\tpython aikit.py ui-id <name> [--set auto|yes|no] [--kind <k>]  # durable has_ui/ui_kind evidence (ADR-233)\n41\tpython aikit.py media init --art <name>  # IMAGE MODEL: POLLINATIONS_API_KEY env only; gen.pollinations.ai free flux model renders title+category, then the square is reframed to 1280x640; never commit the key (ADR-239, ADR-241)\n42\tpython aikit.py fix <name>           # self-heals memory, adopts UI, cleans temp buffers, syncs codebase map\n43\tpython aikit.py checkpoint <name>    # disruption checkpoint on the project ledger; --agent <host>:<session> names you\n44\tpython aikit.py resume <name>        # disruption resume on the project\n45\tpython aikit.py complete <name>      # mark project task complete; another agent's task needs --take-over\n46\tpython scripts/disruption_recovery.py --suspend \"<reason>\" --workspace projects/<name>  # pause a task, keep it resumable\n47\tpython scripts/disruption_recovery.py --resume-task <task_id> --workspace projects/<name>  # reactivate a paused or superseded task (ADR-219)\n48\tpython aikit.py clean <name>         # clean dangling project buffers\n49\tpython aikit.py reforge start <name> --start 3 --step 3 --stop 15  # independent run; per-project lock\n50\tpython aikit.py reforge audit <name>   # write the next window's review packet (commit:path:line)\n51\tpython aikit.py reforge fix <name> --findings answer.json  # validate, repair, verify\n52\tpython aikit.py reforge run <name> --findings answer.json --push  # audit, repair, verify, push\n53\tpython aikit.py reforge run <name> --rules  # deterministic rule pass, no host review\n54\tpython aikit.py reforge settings|stop|resume|runs|status|report <name>  # manage runs (ADR-232, ADR-249)\n55\tpython reforge.py <path> --help        # same engine against any repo, no project registry (ADR-248)\n56\tpython aikit.py idea-catcher status     # shipped tool over the private .idea-catcher/ register (ADR-246, ADR-252)\n57\tpython aikit.py idea-catcher validate   # targets, ideas, dossiers and generated matrix; render --check\n58\tpython aikit.py idea-catcher render --check  # fail when MATRIX.md is stale\n59\tpython aikit.py idea-catcher sync --repo <path> --project <target>  # register delivered IDEA-NNN references and refresh MATRIX.md\n60\t```\n61\t- Reforge in one paragraph: window N is `start + step*(N-1)`, capped by `stop`; a stage inspects only the lines its own commits add and attributes each finding to the commit that introduced it. Five Python rules repair mechanically (`bare-except`, `mutable-default`, `shell-true`, `verify-false`, `unsafe-yaml-load`), each with a generated regression test; a line marked `hygiene: allow <reason>` is honoured, not reported; every other Python rule, every text check and every host finding is reported for a human, or applied only through a validated replacement. A red test or gate restores the exact bytes, and `--commit`/`--push` stage only reviewed paths plus `.aikit/reforge.json`, never forcing (in a project that file is committed memory; at AIKit's own root `.aikit/` is git-ignored tool state, so only reviewed paths are committed). Reforge may repair beside unrelated uncommitted work: those paths are snapshotted, never staged, and a commit is refused only when a finding's own target file was already dirty (`--allow-dirty` overrides). Python files use the opt-in AST detectors (`--rules`) and every other changed text file uses `reforge/textdetect.py`, so only binary files print as `[SKIP] ... not analysed` instead of passing silently. `audit`/`run` write each new commit's own hunks, oldest to newest, to `.aikit/reforge.reviews/` with credential spans redacted; a later hunk may correct an earlier one, so findings must quote the current file. No model is called and no subagent starts. The host agent reads that packet and returns `path`, `line`, `severity`, `kind`, `message`, `evidence`, optional `commit`/`hunk`, optional `reviewed_hunks` coverage and an optional exact `fix`; `fix --findings answer.json` validates the answer against the stage (path, line, commit, hunk, current evidence, exact-once replacement, stage overlap, Python parse) and applies it. Each project has its own resolved lock and state, so projects audit in parallel while one project refuses a second run. Every run also appends `reforge:<run-id>` checkpoints to the repo's AIKit ledger without touching `active_task`, so `--resume` shows it; a plain checkout without a ledger is audited anyway. `reforge/` + `reforge.py` are the only source; the standalone repository is archived (ADR-263, ADR-266).\n62\t- Request names no single project: ask which one, or the name of a new one, before writing code.\n63\t- Before writing code in a project, read its guidelines (`status` or `resume` prints them): its own rules, which add to the principles and never override one (PRINCIPLE-000 R6). When the user states a lasting rule for the project, record it with `aikit guideline`.\n64\t- A UI project is adopted by `fix` when it has a test command: it writes `.aikit/ui.json`, sets `ui_required`, and runs the project test command as its fast proof; without a test command it reports the gap instead of inventing one. A game/project may declare `mechanics.core` (existing paths) and `mechanics.test` in `.aikit/project.json`; `check` validates it and adds the mechanics command as a gate, so an agent and the UI exercise the same headless core.\n65\t- In the steps below, project work replaces the repository with the project: use the cockpit subcommands above, or add `--workspace <project path>` to every `disruption_recovery.py` command, write ADRs in `<project>/.aikit/decisions.md`, stage and commit inside the project, and run `python aikit.py check <name>` as Phase 4. `aikit fix <name>` self-heals project memory and cleans temporary buffers. AIKit's other gates are for changes to AIKit only.\n66\t- The project check runs the built-in hygiene scan of its source and static assets: mark a deliberate finding `hygiene: allow <reason>` on its own line or the line directly above it. After the check passes, record the checklist outcome (`checklists: passed`, or the failed or skipped item IDs) in the task's latest checkpoint description before the commit (PRINCIPLE-001 R8, PRINCIPLE-011 R8).\n67\t\n68\t---\n69\t\n70\t## 🤝 Delegating to Sub-Agents (PRINCIPLE-008 R6, PRINCIPLE-012 R8)\n71\t- **Claude Code**: hand bounded work to the project sub-agents in `.claude/agents/` through the Agent tool: `explorer` (searches, haiku), `worker` (docs and boilerplate, haiku), `architect` (read-only design), `reviewer` (audits, runs read-only gates), `tester` and `coder` (sonnet). Brief each with the milestone, the files it may change and the commands that verify it; run Phase 4 on what comes back.\n72\t- **Other hosts**: `python aikit.py delegate <role> \"<brief>\" [--project <name>]` runs the same role through OpenCode, on free models only: `architect` and `reviewer` on Gemini 3.8 Flash (needs `GEMINI_API_KEY` in the environment), the rest on OpenCode `-free` models (no key). A paid `--model` is refused (ADR-132).\n73\t- Roles have one text, `.opencode/agents/<role>.md`; `python scripts/sync_principles.py` regenerates the Claude copies. No agent can Edit or Write a task ledger (`.claude/settings.json`).\n74\t\n75\t## 🧭 Phase 1: Orientation & Cold-Start Recovery"},{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015GaSLFuYtcdvYrhQ2Cy9Qn","type":"tool_result","content":"120\t---\n121\t\n122\t## 🛠️ Phase 3: Implementation & Synchronization\n123\t\n124\t### 1. Synchronize Principles & IDE Instructions\n125\tAfter modifying `GUIDELINES.md` or `.agents/rules/domain.md`, update all 8 host client instruction files and README:\n126\t```bash\n127\tpython scripts/sync_principles.py\n128\t```\n129\t- Verify zero budget violations (<1,750 tokens per target):\n130\t```bash\n131\tpython scripts/sync_principles.py --check\n132\t```\n133\t\n134\t### 2. Synchronize AST Codebase Map & Knowledge Base\n135\tAfter creating or refactoring symbols:\n136\t```bash\n137\tpython scripts/update_knowledge_base.py\n138\t```\n139\t- Verify link integrity and codebase map freshness:\n140\t```bash\n141\tpython scripts/update_knowledge_base.py --check\n142\t```\n143\t\n144\t### 3. Subagent Delegation via OpenCode (PRINCIPLE-012 R8)\n145\tDelegate bulk token-heavy work to free or local subagents using headless non-interactive mode:\n146\t```bash\n147\t# High-speed grep and symbol exploration\n148\topencode run --standalone --format json --agent explorer \"<query>\"\n149\t\n150\t# Architecture & deep reasoning (SWE-bench 49.2%)\n151\topencode run --standalone --format json --agent architect \"<prompt>\"\n152\t\n153\t# High-fidelity code refactoring (SWE-bench 39.8%)\n154\topencode run --standalone --format json --agent coder --file <target> \"<prompt>\"\n155\t\n156\t# Automated test creation and regression verification\n157\topencode run --standalone --format json --agent tester --file <test_file> \"<prompt>\"\n158\t\n159\t# Documentation, link and claim-fidelity audit\n160\topencode run --standalone --format json --agent reviewer \"<audit_prompt>\"\n161\t\n162\t# Offline / Air-gapped code generation via local Ollama\n163\topencode run --standalone --format json --agent coder --model ollama/qwen2.5-coder:latest --auto \"<prompt>\"\n164\t```\n165\t*(Subagents MUST NOT write to the ledger; only the root orchestrator writes checkpoints).*\n166\t\n167\t---\n168\t\n169\t## 🔒 Phase 4: Verification Gate Shield (Pre-Commit Delivery Triad)\n170\t\n171\tBefore committing any Track B or Track C changes, ALL gates must pass:"}]}}
