{"parentUuid":"0f51594e-fd12-4a7f-89fa-b8be2088c43e","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"a96664c9-b051-4537-af91-e4f15164d542","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Kwd86V9ejKB5RfmkLvFUrq","type":"tool_result","content":"SKILL.md 8336 174\r\nprojects.md 7053 40\r\ndelegation.md 2052 31","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"d7ea3ddf-2823-43c4-8660-51dec4f327b8","timestamp":"2026-10-29T19:30:31.648Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"SKILL.md 8336 174\r\nprojects.md 7053 40\r\ndelegation.md 2052 31","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\Yunus-Emre\\Desktop\\portable_agent_kit\\.agents\\skills\\aikit\\SKILL.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":24,"oldLines":53,"newStart":24,"newLines":16,"lines":[" ---"," "," ## 🧱 Projects: Building Software Other Than AIKit (PRINCIPLE-011 R8)","-The user's software lives in its own project, never in AIKit's tree:","-```bash","-python aikit.py list                 # which projects exist","-python aikit.py new <name> --description \"<10-350 chars>\" [--topic <t>]... [--kind software|game|science]  # own repo + .aikit memory; auto-detects UI, generates model logo/social candidates (POLLINATIONS_API_KEY) or local fallback, writes media pending; --publish refuses until logo/social are reviewed and applied (ADR-243)","-python aikit.py attach <path>        # an existing folder: adds .aikit/ memory and an AIKit Integrated badge under its README title (uncommitted)","-python aikit.py status <name>        # its task, changes, latest decision and its gates","-python aikit.py check <name>         # its Phase 4: tests, stack gates, hygiene, guidelines, secret scan; exit 0 to commit; never pushes, add --push only when push delivery is authorized (PRINCIPLE-018 R4)","-python aikit.py guideline <name> \"<rule>\" --source user   # a project rule, below the principles","-python aikit.py publish <name> [--public] [--owner <org>] [--license auto]  # its own GitHub repo with the README description, the recorded AI-chosen topics and an AI-chosen license; needs a 10-350 char README paragraph; only when the user asks","-python aikit.py license <name> [--suggest [--json]|--set software|game|science|--restrict]  # AL-1.1, AGL-1.1 (DRM-free games) or ASL-1.1 (science); --restrict, only when the user asks, makes later versions All Rights Reserved from HEAD (earlier releases keep their license), drops COMMERCIAL.md, blocks publish --public, and allows check --push or publish only to a repository gh reports private (ADR-214)","-python aikit.py topics <name> --brief --json   # bounded evidence for an AI to choose tags; no tag chosen automatically","-python aikit.py topics <name> --from-file <json> [--apply]  # record the AI's choice; apply only with --apply (ADR-236)","-python aikit.py topics <name> --review [--json]  # audit current/recorded tags without choosing","-python aikit.py ui-id <name> [--set auto|yes|no] [--kind <k>]  # durable has_ui/ui_kind evidence (ADR-233)","-python aikit.py media init --art <name>  # IMAGE MODEL: POLLINATIONS_API_KEY env only; gen.pollinations.ai free flux model renders title+category, then the square is reframed to 1280x640; never commit the key (ADR-239, ADR-241)","-python aikit.py fix <name>           # self-heals memory, adopts UI, cleans temp buffers, syncs codebase map","-python aikit.py checkpoint <name>    # disruption checkpoint on the project ledger; --agent <host>:<session> names you","-python aikit.py resume <name>        # disruption resume on the project","-python aikit.py complete <name>      # mark project task complete; another agent's task needs --take-over","-python scripts/disruption_recovery.py --suspend \"<reason>\" --workspace projects/<name>  # pause a task, keep it resumable","-python scripts/disruption_recovery.py --resume-task <task_id> --workspace projects/<name>  # reactivate a paused or superseded task (ADR-219)","-python aikit.py clean <name>         # clean dangling project buffers","-python aikit.py reforge start <name> --start 3 --step 3 --stop 15  # independent run; per-project lock","-python aikit.py reforge audit <name>   # write the next window's review packet (commit:path:line)","-python aikit.py reforge fix <name> --findings answer.json  # validate, repair, verify","-python aikit.py reforge run <name> --findings answer.json --push  # audit, repair, verify, push","-python aikit.py reforge run <name> --rules  # deterministic rule pass, no host review","-python aikit.py reforge settings|stop|resume|runs|status|report <name>  # manage runs (ADR-232, ADR-249)","-python reforge.py <path> --help        # same engine against any repo, no project registry (ADR-248)","-python aikit.py idea-catcher status     # shipped tool over the private .idea-catcher/ register (ADR-246, ADR-252)","-python aikit.py idea-catcher validate   # targets, ideas, dossiers and generated matrix; render --check","-python aikit.py idea-catcher render --check  # fail when MATRIX.md is stale","-python aikit.py idea-catcher sync --repo <path> --project <target>  # register delivered IDEA-NNN references and refresh MATRIX.md","-```","-- Reforge in one paragraph: window N is `start + step*(N-1)`, capped by `stop`; a stage inspects only the lines its own commits add and attributes each finding to the commit that introduced it. Five Python rules repair mechanically (`bare-except`, `mutable-default`, `shell-true`, `verify-false`, `unsafe-yaml-load`), each with a generated regression test; a line marked `hygiene: allow <reason>` is honoured, not reported; every other Python rule, every text check and every host finding is reported for a human, or applied only through a validated replacement. A red test or gate restores the exact bytes, and `--commit`/`--push` stage only reviewed paths plus `.aikit/reforge.json`, never forcing (in a project that file is committed memory; at AIKit's own root `.aikit/` is git-ignored tool state, so only reviewed paths are committed). Reforge may repair beside unrelated uncommitted work: those paths are snapshotted, never staged, and a commit is refused only when a finding's own target file was already dirty (`--allow-dirty` overrides). Python files use the opt-in AST detectors (`--rules`) and every other changed text file uses `reforge/textdetect.py`, so only binary files print as `[SKIP] ... not analysed` instead of passing silently. `audit`/`run` write each new commit's own hunks, oldest to newest, to `.aikit/reforge.reviews/` with credential spans redacted; a later hunk may correct an earlier one, so findings must quote the current file. No model is called and no subagent starts. The host agent reads that packet and returns `path`, `line`, `severity`, `kind`, `message`, `evidence`, optional `commit`/`hunk`, optional `reviewed_hunks` coverage and an optional exact `fix`; `fix --findings answer.json` validates the answer against the stage (path, line, commit, hunk, current evidence, exact-once replacement, stage overlap, Python parse) and applies it. Each project has its own resolved lock and state, so projects audit in parallel while one project refuses a second run. Every run also appends `reforge:<run-id>` checkpoints to the repo's AIKit ledger without touching `active_task`, so `--resume` shows it; a plain checkout without a ledger is audited anyway. `reforge/` + `reforge.py` are the only source; the standalone repository is archived (ADR-263, ADR-266).","+The user's software lives in its own project, never in AIKit's tree. The full command matrix (`new`, `attach`, `check`, `license`, `publish`, `media`, `reforge`, `idea-catcher` and more) and the Reforge protocol are in `projects.md`; read it before project work."," - Request names no single project: ask which one, or the name of a new one, before writing code."," - Before writing code in a project, read its guidelines (`status` or `resume` prints them): its own rules, which add to the principles and never override one (PRINCIPLE-000 R6). When the user states a lasting rule for the project, record it with `aikit guideline`.","-- A UI project is adopted by `fix` when it has a test command: it writes `.aikit/ui.json`, sets `ui_required`, and runs the project test command as its fast proof; without a test command it reports the gap instead of inventing one. A game/project may declare `mechanics.core` (existing paths) and `mechanics.test` in `.aikit/project.json`; `check` validates it and adds the mechanics command as a gate, so an agent and the UI exercise the same headless core."," - In the steps below, project work replaces the repository with the project: use the cockpit subcommands above, or add `--workspace <project path>` to every `disruption_recovery.py` command, write ADRs in `<project>/.aikit/decisions.md`, stage and commit inside the project, and run `python aikit.py check <name>` as Phase 4. `aikit fix <name>` self-heals project memory and cleans temporary buffers. AIKit's other gates are for changes to AIKit only."," - The project check runs the built-in hygiene scan of its source and static assets: mark a deliberate finding `hygiene: allow <reason>` on its own line or the line directly above it. After the check passes, record the checklist outcome (`checklists: passed`, or the failed or skipped item IDs) in the task's latest checkpoint description before the commit (PRINCIPLE-001 R8, PRINCIPLE-011 R8)."," "," ---"," "," ## 🤝 Delegating to Sub-Agents (PRINCIPLE-008 R6, PRINCIPLE-012 R8)","-- **Claude Code**: hand bounded work to the project sub-agents in `.claude/agents/` through the Agent tool: `explorer` (searches, haiku), `worker` (docs and boilerplate, haiku), `architect` (read-only design), `reviewer` (audits, runs read-only gates), `tester` and `coder` (sonnet). Brief each with the milestone, the files it may change and the commands that verify it; run Phase 4 on what comes back.","-- **Other hosts**: `python aikit.py delegate <role> \"<brief>\" [--project <name>]` runs the same role through OpenCode, on free models only: `architect` and `reviewer` on Gemini 3.8 Flash (needs `GEMINI_API_KEY` in the environment), the rest on OpenCode `-free` models (no key). A paid `--model` is refused (ADR-132).","-- Roles have one text, `.opencode/agents/<role>.md`; `python scripts/sync_principles.py` regenerates the Claude copies. No agent can Edit or Write a task ledger (`.claude/settings.json`).","+Before delegating, read `delegation.md`: the Claude Code roles, `aikit delegate` on free models, headless OpenCode runs, and the rule that no sub-agent writes a task ledger."," "," ## 🧭 Phase 1: Orientation & Cold-Start Recovery"," "]},{"oldStart":141,"oldLines":28,"newStart":104,"newLines":7,"lines":[" python scripts/update_knowledge_base.py --check"," ```"," ","-### 3. Subagent Delegation via OpenCode (PRINCIPLE-012 R8)","-Delegate bulk token-heavy work to free or local subagents using headless non-interactive mode:","-```bash","-# High-speed grep and symbol exploration","-opencode run --standalone --format json --agent explorer \"<query>\"","-","-# Architecture & deep reasoning (SWE-bench 49.2%)","-opencode run --standalone --format json --agent architect \"<prompt>\"","-","-# High-fidelity code refactoring (SWE-bench 39.8%)","-opencode run --standalone --format json --agent coder --file <target> \"<prompt>\"","-","-# Automated test creation and regression verification","-opencode run --standalone --format json --agent tester --file <test_file> \"<prompt>\"","-","-# Documentation, link and claim-fidelity audit","-opencode run --standalone --format json --agent reviewer \"<audit_prompt>\"","-","-# Offline / Air-gapped code generation via local Ollama","-opencode run --standalone --format json --agent coder --model ollama/qwen2.5-coder:latest --auto \"<prompt>\"","-```","-*(Subagents MUST NOT write to the ledger; only the root orchestrator writes checkpoints).*","+The headless OpenCode commands are in `delegation.md` (sub-agents never write the ledger)."," "," ---"," "]}