mmit:path:line)","+python aikit.py reforge fix <name> --findings answer.json  # validate, repair, verify","+python aikit.py reforge run <name> --findings answer.json --push  # audit, repair, verify, push","+python aikit.py reforge run <name> --rules  # deterministic rule pass, no host review","+python aikit.py reforge settings|stop|resume|runs|status|report <name>  # manage runs (ADR-232, ADR-249)","+python reforge.py <path> --help        # same engine against any repo, no project registry (ADR-248)","+python aikit.py idea-catcher status     # shipped tool over the private .idea-catcher/ register (ADR-246, ADR-252)","+python aikit.py idea-catcher validate   # targets, ideas, dossiers and generated matrix; render --check","+python aikit.py idea-catcher render --check  # fail when MATRIX.md is stale","+python aikit.py idea-catcher sync --repo <path> --project <target>  # register delivered IDEA-NNN references and refresh MATRIX.md","+```","+- Reforge in one paragraph: window N is `start + step*(N-1)`, capped by `stop`; a stage inspects only the lines its own commits add and attributes each finding to the commit that introduced it. Five Python rules repair mechanically (`bare-except`, `mutable-default`, `shell-true`, `verify-false`, `unsafe-yaml-load`), each with a generated regression test; a line marked `hygiene: allow <reason>` is honoured, not reported; every other Python rule, every text check and every host finding is reported for a human, or applied only through a validated replacement. A red test or gate restores the exact bytes, and `--commit`/`--push` stage only reviewed paths plus `.aikit/reforge.json`, never forcing (in a project that file is committed memory; at AIKit's own root `.aikit/` is git-ignored tool state, so only reviewed paths are committed). Reforge may repair beside unrelated uncommitted work: those paths are snapshotted, never staged, and a commit is refused only when a finding's own target file was already dirty (`--allow-dirty` overrides). Python files use the opt-in AST detectors (`--rules`) and every other changed text file uses `reforge/textdetect.py`, so only binary files print as `[SKIP] ... not analysed` instead of passing silently. `audit`/`run` write each new commit's own hunks, oldest to newest, to `.aikit/reforge.reviews/` with credential spans redacted; a later hunk may correct an earlier one, so findings must quote the current file. No model is called and no subagent starts. The host agent reads that packet and returns `path`, `line`, `severity`, `kind`, `message`, `evidence`, optional `commit`/`hunk`, optional `reviewed_hunks` coverage and an optional exact `fix`; `fix --findings answer.json` validates the answer against the stage (path, line, commit, hunk, current evidence, exact-once replacement, stage overlap, Python parse) and applies it. Each project has its own resolved lock and state, so projects audit in parallel while one project refuses a second run. Every run also appends `reforge:<run-id>` checkpoints to the repo's AIKit ledger without touching `active_task`, so `--resume` shows it; a plain checkout without a ledger is audited anyway. `reforge/` + `reforge.py` are the only source; the standalone repository is archived (ADR-263, ADR-266).","+- A UI project is adopted by `fix` when it has a test command: it writes `.aikit/ui.json`, sets `ui_required`, and runs the project test command as its fast proof; without a test command it reports the gap instead of inventing one. A game/project may declare `mechanics.core` (existing paths) and `mechanics.test` in `.aikit/project.json`; `check` validates it and adds the mechanics command as a gate, so an agent and the UI exercise the same headless core."]}],"created":true}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["C:\\Users\\Yunus-Emre\\Desktop\\portable_agent_kit\\.agents\\skills\\aikit\\SKILL.md","C:\\Users\\Yunus-Emre\\Desktop\\portable_agent_kit\\.agents\\skills\\aikit\\delegation.md","C:\\Users\\Yunus-Emre\\Desktop\\portable_agent_kit\\.agents\