{"parentUuid":"b8d0f708-3553-4ae9-bfd2-a04e71eff1cb","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgX5pyBNRZbNELHAwpfSV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01CaXK6XxNWkVDiZnaGbng7U","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd \"C:/Users/Yunus-Emre/Desktop/portable_agent_kit\"; python - <<'E'\nadr = \"\"\"\n### ADR-284: The Runbook Is an Index with Topic Files Read on Demand\n- **Date**: 2026-10-29\n- **Status**: Accepted\n- **Context**: `.agents/skills/aikit/SKILL.md` (mirrored to `.claude/`) was 231 lines and 16.8 KB, and a host loads it whole every time the skill triggers: at PRINCIPLE-012's 16k payload cap and past PRINCIPLE-004's 100-line read. Half of it (8.2 KB) was the project command matrix and the Reforge protocol, which a task on AIKit itself never uses (IDEA-210).\n- **Decision**: `SKILL.md` keeps the five lifecycle phases and the binding project rules (ask which project, read its guidelines, `--workspace` and `aikit check` as its Phase 4, the checklist record). The project command matrix, the Reforge paragraph and UI/mechanics adoption move verbatim to `projects.md`; the sub-agent roles, `aikit delegate` and the headless OpenCode commands move to `delegation.md`. `SKILL.md` names each file at the point it is needed. `RUNBOOK_TOPICS` in `sync_principles.py` mirrors both to `.claude/skills/aikit/`, and `--check` reports a drifted copy as it does for the index. A test bounds the index at 9,000 characters and requires every topic file it names to exist and be mirrored byte for byte; the rule-citation test covers the new files.\n- **Consequences**: Each trigger loads 8.3 KB instead of 16.7 KB. Project and delegation work costs one extra read of 7.1 KB or 2.1 KB. A host that never opens the topic file would miss the matrix, so every binding rule stayed in the index; only commands and their descriptions moved. The README is now within 100 characters of its 30,000 limit.\n- **Cross-principle check**: no principle section changed. Serves PRINCIPLE-001 (progressive disclosure), PRINCIPLE-004 and PRINCIPLE-012 (bounded always-loaded text) and PRINCIPLE-017 (topic files are generated mirrors under the same check).\n\"\"\"\np='knowledge/decisions.md'\nb=open(p,'rb').read()\nopen(p,'wb').write(b + adr.replace('\\n','\\r\\n').encode('utf-8'))\nE\npython scripts/update_knowledge_base.py 2>&1 | grep -E \"FAIL|ADR|README\"; python scripts/check_test_budgets.py 2>&1 | grep -E \"PASS|FAIL|OK\\]\"; for g in \"sync_principles.py --check\" \"update_knowledge_base.py --check\" \"check_reachability.py\" \"check_secrets.py\" \"sync_licenses.py --check\"; do printf \"== %s: \" \"$g\"; python scripts/$g >/tmp/g.out 2>&1; echo \"rc=$?\"; grep -E \"FAIL|OUT OF SYNC\" /tmp/g.out | head -3; done; python scripts/dogfood.py 2>&1 | grep -E \"tracks passed|FAIL\"","description":"Append ADR-284, regenerate, run full Phase 4","timeout":600000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2178,"cache_read_input_tokens":437672,"output_tokens":1357,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":76},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2178,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1357,"cache_read_input_tokens":437672,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2178,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2178},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01CaXK6XxNWkVDiZnaGbng7U":{"command":"cd \"C:/Users/Yunus-Emre/Desktop/portable_agent_kit\"; python - <<'E'\nadr = \"\"\"\n### ADR-284: The Runbook Is an Index with Topic Files Read on Demand\n- **Date**: 2026-10-29\n- **Status**: A