{"parentUuid":"7cb41754-0aae-45a4-bfc7-4d44237458ef","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgX5usgN3FEUJXRjKddhb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All five approved AIKit ideas are implemented and pass Phase 4: every test in budget, all read-only gates, and dogfood 5 of 5. Nothing is committed, because your host settings only allow commits you explicitly request. Each idea has an ADR and shows \"Integrating\" in the register.\n\n| Idea | What changed | ADR |\n|---|---|---|\n| **406** | Idea-catcher's hints now name `python aikit.py idea-catcher …`, which works, instead of the missing `tools/idea_catcher.py`. `update_knowledge_base.py --check` now fails on any `python <path>.py` that points at a missing file. | 280 |\n| **398** | A new helper, `scripts/marked_blocks.py`. The License paragraph now sits between `aegean:license` markers, so a note you add under the License heading survives later license switches. The media, screenshot and brand-asset blocks use the same helper, with byte-identical output across 20 test cases. | 281 |\n| **262** | `verify_commit.py` warns, without blocking, when a commit leaves a file at under half its previous size. A `shrink-ok: <reason>` line in the commit message clears the warning. Only 3 of 334 past commits would have warned, and all three cuts were intended. | 282 |\n| **005** | `update_knowledge_base.py --digest` prints one line per module, readable in one go: 58 lines for AIKit. Neurocore needs 100 lines and ends by saying how many modules it left out (188). | 283 |\n| **210** | The skill runbook loaded on every trigger dropped from 16.7 KB to 8.3 KB. The project command matrix and delegation detail moved unchanged into `projects.md` and `delegation.md`, which are mirrored to `.claude/` automatically. | 284 |\n\n**Things you should know:**\n- **IDEA-262 is preventive, not a fix.** I had cited a past README bug as evidence for it, but checking the history showed that bug wasn't a shrink. No accidental overwrite of this kind is on record. ADR-282 and the register now say so.\n- **IDEA-406 skips projects for now.** Every project's docs mention `aikit.py`, which lives in AIKit's folder, so all 44 projects would fail the check. Covering projects needs that resolved first.\n- **The README is nearly full:** 29,927 of its 30,000-character limit. The next README addition will need something trimmed first.\n- **Another agent is mid-edit in research-engine.** `projects/research-engine/engine/cli.py` doesn't currently parse. It isn't part of AIKit's checks and I didn't touch it.\n\nThe working tree has 15 modified and 5 new files for these five changes. Say \"commit\" and I'll commit them as five separate commits, one per idea, each re-verified on its own before any push."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1217,"cache_read_input_tokens":441558,"output_tokens":930,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1217,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":930,"cache_read_input_tokens":441558,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1217,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1217},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"0a6ab570-1555-4c0e-b3b5-78e67a4b0a88","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgX5usLXSRF2jjcWa9gH6","requestRef":"cf92c8b5-0be2-461f-9e54-039c3ba5e3ec","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"7887a71d-6d48-45a1-be08-a57b11c2def2","timestamp":"2026-10-29T19:32:15.117Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userTyp