{"parentUuid":"35b03e0d-61ae-4373-8410-9e482a1ea782","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgX6D1NwpNNKZHxKaFoqS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"For AIKit, no: all 5 approved ideas are implemented and sit at \"Integrating\". Three pieces of work are left, though.\n\n**1. Commit the AIKit work.** The five changes are verified but still uncommitted (15 modified files, 5 new). They become \"Integrated\" once committed. Say \"commit\" and I'll make one commit per idea, each verified on its own.\n\n**2. Neurocore's 14 approved ideas, all still to do.** In priority order:\n\n| Priority | Ideas | What |\n|---|---|---|\n| P1 | 370 + 120 | The truncation bug: the persona/system prompt is silently dropped when a conversation goes over the token limit |\n| P2 | 063 | DNS-rebinding hole in the SSRF check |\n| P3 | 334, 030 | Scan memory writes for injected text; mark untrusted content with random boundary tags |\n| P4 | 369, 060 | Token budget not enforced when the provider reports no usage; step risk defaults to \"low\" when unset |\n| P5 | 058, 591, 588 | Default-deny tool policy, embedding-model identity check, per-model capability limits |\n| P6 | 619, 625, 629, 631 | Recorded LLM responses for tests, guardrail evasion matrix, two-lens reflection critique, system-prompt digest check |\n\n**3. Neurocore's Deferred and Rejected ideas still need the second-pass re-read.** AIKit got one; neurocore's 195 haven't been checked against their dossier blueprints yet.\n\nI'd start with neurocore P1: it's a real bug, and the backlog note and plan are already in its `docs/IDEAS.md`. Neurocore has its own workflow rules in its `CLAUDE.md` (propose first, then implement, then tests), and I'd follow those."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":470,"cache_read_input_tokens":443851,"output_tokens":599,"output_tokens_det