{"parentUuid":"36cebbb1-b888-446a-bef7-8e3ac50e8776","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"deferred_tools_record","entries":[],"toolInputCopies":[{"id":"toolu_01MqUPBVY3jDDas3bTbakJ1B","copy":"wire"}]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"dbbb2eb9-11f7-42c2-8608-1401627f59f5","timestamp":"2026-10-29T19:39:00.847Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"C:\\Users\\Yunus-Emre\\Desktop\\portable_agent_kit","sessionId":"05aa96e5-db7a-4aed-bad4-f0f3cebd2787","version":"2.1.312","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"dbbb2eb9-11f7-42c2-8608-1401627f59f5","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgX6RkoTw7fHBWDJUpQ6v","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I re-read all 195 of neurocore's Deferred and Rejected ideas against their dossier blueprints. The most important finding is a new security gap.\n\n**New gap: injected text can make the agent send email.** The `SendEmail` tool is on by default and sends to any address without asking. The only safeguard is a line in its description: \"use only when the user explicitly asks\". Meanwhile, untrusted text reaches the same agent through incoming email, `FetchURL` and knowledge-base documents. A malicious email or web page could therefore instruct the agent to send data anywhere. IDEA-032 fixes this: the tool writes a draft, and only a later, explicit message from you sends it. I've moved it from Deferred to Approved at P2 and added it to the Known Bugs list in neurocore's `docs/IDEAS.md`, uncommitted.\n\n**Another agent already fixed some of the work.** I checked commit `d5629fd` myself:\n\n| Idea | State |\n|---|---|\n| 370 + 120 (truncation bug) | Fixed: every system message is kept, tool calls stay with their results, and dropped messages are logged. The agent-loop and budget suites pass (94 tests). Marked Integrated. |\n| 369 (token budget) | Fixed: tokens are estimated when the provider doesn't report usage. Marked Integrated. |\n| 063 (DNS rebinding) | Only partly fixed (`e0cf494`). Addresses are now checked, but each connection looks the host up again, so the hole is still open. Stays Approved. |\n\nOne side effect of the truncation fix: system messages now move to the front of the conversation, so the memory goal no longer sits just before your latest message. Nothing breaks, but the prompt order has changed.\n\n**Other corrections:**\n- **3 more rejected:** 160, 609 and 610. Their blueprints only make sense inside a game engine.\n- **10 compaction ideas:** their revisit condition was \"after IDEA-370/120 land\", and both have landed. The new condition is evidence from real runs that truncation loses facts that matter.\n- **309 and 462:** their reasons misread the blueprint and are rewritten.\n\nEverything else held up: the blueprints confirmed the existing reasons.\n\nNeurocore now stands at 12 Approved, 3 Integrated, 131 Deferred, 63 Rejected and 26 Superseded.\n\n**Still open for neurocore, in priority order:**\n\n| Priority | Ideas |\n|---|---|\n| P2 | 063 (DNS rebinding), 032 (email draft gate) |\n| P3 | 334 (scan memory writes), 030 (boundary tags on untrusted content) |\n| P4 | 060 (step risk defaults to \"low\") |\n| P5 | 058 (default-deny tool policy), 591 (embedding identity), 588 (model capabilities) |\n| P6 | 619, 625, 629, 631 |\n\nThe five AIKit changes are also still waiting for your \"commit\"."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":513,"cache_read_input_tokens":482891,"output_tokens":982,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":513,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":982,"cache_read_input_tokens":482891,"cache_creation_input_tokens":513,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":513},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"94658a2a-9cc0-4dfe-a288-12d277d97ab6","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgX6RkRtZwj45CPX45mH1","requestRef":"7fde9de5-8ddd-4520-93de-2328eb4114c0","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"22dc1374-075a-4297-8f55-046a6fb23e55","timestamp":"2026-10-29T19:39:00.846Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-