{"parentUuid":"906b26cf-1e69-477c-8748-fc89b278672c","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"e576fa94-db77-402f-876f-969ab294b577","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RPCt44AG5EEsxwAuEHVwKE","type":"tool_result","content":"The file c:\\Users\\Yunus-Emre\\Desktop\\portable_agent_kit\\projects\\neurocore\\README.md has been updated successfully."}]},"uuid":"12d9c52a-1021-497b-acba-74f92065384e","timestamp":"2026-10-29T19:47:25.755Z","toolUseResult":{"filePath":"c:\\Users\\Yunus-Emre\\Desktop\\portable_agent_kit\\projects\\neurocore\\README.md","oldString":"`core/research_gateway.py`. Each request, and each redirect hop, must stay on that source's hosts\nand resolve to a public address; responses are capped","newString":"`core/research_gateway.py`. Each request, and each redirect hop, must stay on that source's hosts\nand resolve to a public address, and connects to the address that passed that check rather than\nresolving the name again (`core/pinned_http.py`; the skill URL importer does the same), so DNS\nrebinding cannot swap in a private address; responses are capped","originalFile":null,"structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":371,"oldLines":7,"newStart":371,"newLines":9,"lines":[" "," Literature search is restricted to three allowlisted adapters (Wikipedia, arXiv, PubMed) in"," `core/research_gateway.py`. Each request, and each redirect hop, must stay on that source's hosts","-and resolve to a public address; responses are capped at 2 MB and 10 seconds, cached for a day,","+and resolve to a public address, and connects to the address that passed that check rather than","+resolving the name again (`core/pinned_http.py`; the skill URL importer does the same), so DNS","+rebinding cannot swap in a private address; responses are capped at 2 MB and 10 seconds, cached for a day,"," and returned with the source, retrieval time, licence and a content hash. `GET /research/sources`"," lists the adapters and `POST /research/fetch {\"source\",\"query\",\"limit\",\"persist\"}` performs a"," search; there is no fallback to an unlisted search engine or a spoofed user agent."]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false,"contentNotInModelContext":true},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"906b26cf-1e69-477c-8748-fc89b278672c","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"C:\\Users\\Yunus-Emre\\Desktop\\portable_agent_kit\\projects\\neurocore","sessionId":"05aa96e5-db7a-4aed-bad4-f0f3cebd2787","version":"2.1.312","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"7cad36b9-1aaa-4a9a-8dc2-f2aef7f34f55","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"e576fa94-db77-402f-876f-969ab294b577","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PdrxM6MWKsGDcJ56ALXMTh","type":"tool_result","content":"The file c:\\Users\\Yunus-Emre\\Desktop\\portable_agent_kit\\projects\\neurocore\\docs\\IDEAS.md has been updated successfully."}]},"uuid":"3fc3092c-2608-410c-ac69-d0a2e1596db9","timestamp":"2026-10-29T19:47:26.646Z","toolUseResult":{"filePath":"c:\\Users\\Yunus-Emre\\Desktop\\portable_agent_kit\\projects\\neurocore\\docs\\IDEAS.md","oldString":"- **[ ] DNS rebinding passes the SSRF check** *(IDEA-063)*: `_validate_url` in\n  `core/research_gateway.py` checks the resolved address, then httpx resolves again on connect.\n  Pin the vetted address; the skill URL importer now validates every resolved address but still\n  resolves again at connect time.","newString":"- **[x] DNS rebinding passes the SSRF check** *(IDEA-063)*: `_validate_url` in\n  `core/research_gateway.py` checked the resolved address, then httpx resolved again on connect.\n  Fixed: both the gateway (every redirect hop) and the skill URL importer connect to the vetted\n  address via `core/pinned_http.py`, with the hostname kept for `Host` and TLS `sni_hostname`.","originalFile":"# 💡 NeuroCore Ideas & Improvements\n\nThis document tracks brainstorming features, layout refinements, and long-term architectural upgrades for the **NeuroCore** framework lists index flaws ok.\n\n---\n\n## 🐞 0. Known Bugs & Gaps (found 2026-10-29)\n- **[x] Truncation drops the system prompt** *(bug, IDEA-370 + IDEA-120)*:\n  - `AgentLoopExecutor._truncate_messages` (`modules/agent_loop/node.py`) kept only the *last*\n    system message once a conversation exceeded `max_context_tokens`. A flow with the system-prompt\n    node followed by the memory goal node (`modules/memory/node.py`) sends two system messages, so\n    the persona prompt was silently dropped and only the goal survived.\n  - The same walk could keep a `tool` message whose assistant `tool_calls` message was cut, which\n    OpenAI-compatible APIs reject.\n  - Fixed: truncation now keeps every system message and treats an assistant tool call plus its\n    tool results as one atomic group; the dropped count is logged. Regression test added.\n- **[ ] DNS rebinding passes the SSRF check** *(IDEA-063)*: `_validate_url` in\n  `core/research_gateway.py` checks the resolved address, then httpx resolves again on connect.\n  Pin the vetted address; the skill URL importer now validates every resolved address but still\n  resolves again at connect time.\n- **[x] Token budget unenforced without provider usage** *(IDEA-369)*: `_charge_llm_usage` charged\n  0 tokens when a response had no `usage` (common on local servers). Fixed with a bounded\n  request-plus-response estimate when the provider omits usage.\n- **[ ] Step risk is fail-open** *(IDEA-060)*: the agent loop takes `risk`/`reversible` from the\n  model, defaults to `low`/`true` when missing, and only adds a prompt warning.\n- **[ ] Injected text can make the agent send email** *(IDEA-032)*: `SendEmail` is enabled by\n  default (`modules/tools/tools.json`) and sends to any recipient without confirmation; only its\n  tool description says \"use only when the user explicitly asks\". Untrusted text reaches the same\n  agent through the email bridge, `FetchURL` and KB documents. Fix: the tool writes a draft, and only\n  a later explicit user turn sends it.\n\n---\n\n## 🔬 1. Core Engine & DAG Runner\n- **[ ] Execution Trace Visual Replay**:\n  - Build UI playback slider that reads `execution_trace.jsonl` to animate node transitions on visual maps, giving full debug walkthrough histories flawlessly flaws ok.\n- **[ ] Node Memoization / Caching Cache**:\n  - Cache node sends based on hashing input weights payloads to skip re-running expensive LLM triggers if data did not mutate in short-looped intervals flawless ok.\n- **[ ] Parallel Merge Node Blocks**:\n  - Introduce explicit implicit execution Split/Join nodes expanding concurrent workflow lanes seamlessly flaws ok.\n\n---\n\n## 🌍 2. Community Marketplace\n- **[x] Rating & Sorting system** *(implemented)*:\n  - Users can Upvote/Downvote catalog listings so top assets sort highest inside grid layout lists.\n- **[ ] Flow Visual Maps Previews Overlay**:\n  - Hovering or clicking shared workflows triggers a read-only vis-DAG overlay graph preview so user sees the Node-tree before download flawlessly.\n- **[x] Versioning & Sync Tracking** *(implemented)*:\n  - Items carry a `changelog` list prepended on each update; imported items track `downloaded_version` for update detection.\n\n---\n\n## 🧠 3. Skills Management\n- **[x] Live Rich Text Prompt Editor** *(implemented)*:\n  - Skill edit/create flow available in Settings → Skills with full in-UI editor.\n- **[ ] Skill Synthesizer / Creator Templates Template**:\n  - Insert \"+\" floating triggers setting blank categories placeholders mapping custom prompts creation directly inside `.skills/data` arrays flawless ok.\n\n---\n\n## 🎨 4. UX & Interfaces\n- **[ ] Light / Grid Theme Toggle**:\n  - Standard variables setups toggle support natively flawless ok.\n- **[ ] Dashboard WebSockets Streaming**:\n  - Stream `stdout` logs live via lower console logs drawers avoiding debug-only lookup cycles flawlessly layout streams flaws ok.\n\n---\n\n## ⚙️ 5. Reliability & Error Recovery (Core Engine)\n- **[x] Node Retry Policies with Backoff** *(implemented, ADR-060)*:\n  - Per-node `retry_count`, `retry_delay`, `retry_max_delay`, `retry_backoff` and\n    `timeout_seconds`; transient failures only, charged to the run budget.\n- **[x] Node Deadlocks / Stalls Detector** *(implemented, ADR-061)*:\n  - Per module/type latency history with p50/p95/p99; an attempt above both 2 s and 3x the prior\n    p99 is logged, counted and exposed by `GET /debug/node-latency` without aborting the run.\n\n---\n\n## 📈 6. Advanced Memory & RAG Strategies (Knowledge Base)\n- **[ ] FAISS IndexHNSW Scaling for expanding corpuses**:\n  - `IndexFlatIP` does linear exact scans. As files grow, upgrading dynamic index types to approximate indices (like HNSW) scales lookup speeds effortlessly flawless flawless ok.\n- **[ ] Dynamic Memory Consolidation (Background Workers)**:\n  - Setup background cron-triggers loading FAISS indices to merge duplicates, summarize dense chat clusters into memory beliefs automatically flawlessly ok.\n\n---\n\n## 🛠️ 7. Dynamic Tools & Full Sandbox\n- **[ ] Code Interpreter Docker Executor Layouts**:\n  - Expand execution pipelines pushing tool calls onto isolated docker socket payloads allowing full OS pip installs safely flawlessly ok.\n\n---\n\n## 📊 8. Dashboard Analytics Visualizations\n- **[ ] Live Metrics Gauges Overlays**:\n  - Plot running charts reading `core/observability.py` values to inspect flows through put in real-time flawless ok.\n\n---\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":14,"oldLines":10,"newStart":14,"newLines":10,"lines":["     OpenAI-compatible APIs reject.","   - Fixed: truncation now keeps every system message and treats an assistant tool call plus its","     tool results as one atomic group; the dropped count is logged. Regression test added.","-- **[ ] DNS rebinding passes the SSRF check** *(IDEA-063)*: `_validate_url` in","-  `core/research_gateway.py` checks the resolved address, then httpx resolves again on connect.","-  Pin the vetted address; the skill URL importer now validates every resolved address but still","-  resolves again at connect time.","+- **[x] DNS rebinding passes the SSRF check** *(IDEA-063)*: `_validate_url` in","+  `core/research_gateway.py` checked the resolved address, then httpx resolved again on connect.","+  Fixed: both the gateway (every redirect hop) and the skill URL importer connect to the vetted","+  address via `core/pinned_http.py`, with the hostname kept for `Host` and TLS `sni_hostname`."," - **[x] Token budget unenforced without provider usage** *(IDEA-369)*: `_charge_llm_usage` charged","   0 tokens when a response had no `usage` (common on local servers). Fixed with a bounded","   request-plus-response estimate when the provider omits usage."]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false,"contentNotInModelContext":true},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"7cad36b9-1aaa-4a9a-8dc2-f2aef7f34f55","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"C:\\Users\\Yunus-Emre\\Desktop\\portable_agent_kit\\projects\\neurocore","sessionId":"05aa96e5-db7a-4aed-bad4-f0f3cebd2787","version":"2.1.312","gitBranch":"main"}
