{"parentUuid":"b6fde517-fcc8-480f-8e65-68b2bbe49c09","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgX7MgzWpxwgv9dLp6Pea","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014Gkcv16buuBCqyEXeiYuk8","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd \"C:/Users/Yunus-Emre/Desktop/portable_agent_kit/projects/neurocore\"; python - <<'E'\nadr = \"\"\"\n### ADR-063: SSRF-checked fetches connect to the vetted address\n- **Date**: 2026-10-29\n- **Status**: Accepted\n- **Context**: `core/research_gateway.py` and the skill URL importer resolved a hostname, rejected\n  any private, loopback, link-local or reserved answer, and then handed the hostname to httpx,\n  which resolved it again on connect. A DNS answer that changes between the two lookups (DNS\n  rebinding) therefore reached an address the check had rejected (IDEA-063). Commit e0cf494 made\n  the importer check every resolved address but kept the second lookup.\n- **Decision**: `core/pinned_http.py` builds a pinned request: the URL on the vetted IP (IPv6\n  bracketed, zone dropped, port kept), a `Host` header with the hostname, and the httpcore\n  `sni_hostname` extension for HTTPS so TLS verifies the certificate against the name.\n  `_vetted_address` in the gateway returns the first public answer and `_safe_get` pins every\n  redirect hop to its own vetted address; `_validate_url` keeps its contract. The importer pins to\n  the first address it vetted, through a short-lived `httpx.Client`.\n- **Consequences**: The connection goes to exactly the address that passed the check. A live fetch\n  from Wikipedia succeeded through the pinned path, and the same IP with the name `example.com`\n  failed certificate verification, so TLS checking is intact. Only the first vetted address is\n  tried; a host whose first answer is down is not retried on the next one.\n- Cross-principle check: no principle section changed. Serves PRINCIPLE-003 (the request goes where\n  the check looked) and PRINCIPLE-019 (no internal service is reachable through a fetch).\n\"\"\"\np='.aikit/decisions.md'\nb=open(p,'rb').read()\nopen(p,'wb').write(b + adr.replace('\\n','\\r\\n').encode('utf-8'))\nE\ncd ../..; timeout 900 python aikit.py check neurocore 2>&1 | grep -E \"^\\[PASS\\]|^\\[FAIL\\]|gates passed\" | cut -c1-90","description":"Add neurocore ADR-063 and rerun the project check","timeout":920000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":871,"cache_read_input_tokens":512806,"output_tokens":897,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":871,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":897,"cache_read_input_tokens":512806,"cache_creation_input_tokens":871,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":871},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_014Gkcv16buuBCqyEXeiYuk8":{"command":"cd \"C:/Users/Yunus-Emre/Desktop/portable_agent_kit/projects/neurocore\"; python - <<'E'\nadr = \"\"\"\n### ADR-063: SSRF-checked fetches connect to the vetted address\n- **Date**: 2026-10-29\n- **Status**: Accepted\n- **Context**: `core/research_gateway.py` and the skill URL importer resolved a hostname, rejected\n  any private, loopback, link-local or reserved answer, and then handed the hostname to httpx,\n  which resolved it again on connect. A DNS answer that changes between the two lookups (DNS\n  rebinding) therefore reached an address the check had rejected (IDEA-063). Commit e0cf494 made\n  the importer check every resolved address but kept the second lookup.\n- **Decision**: `core/pinned_http.py` builds a pinned request: the URL on the vetted IP (IPv6\n  bracketed, zone dropped, port kept), a `Host` header with the hostname, and the httpcore\n  `sni_hostname` extension for HTTPS so TLS verifies the certificate against the name.\n  `_vetted_address` in the gateway returns the first public answer and `_safe_get` pins every\n  redirect hop to its own vetted address; `_validate_url` keeps its contract. The importer pins to\n  the first address it vetted, through a short-lived `httpx.Client`.\n- **Consequences**: The connection goes to exactly the address that passed the check. A live fetch\n  from Wikipedia succeeded through the pinned path, and the same IP with the name `example.com`\n  failed certificate verification, so TLS checking is intact. Only the first vetted address is\n  tried; a host whose first answer is down is not retried on the next one.\n- Cross-principle check: no principle section changed. Serves PRINCIPLE-003 (the request goes where\n  the check looked) and PRINCIPLE-019 (no internal service is reachable through a fetch).\n\"\"\"\np='.aikit/decisions.md'\nb=open(p,'rb').read()\nopen(p,'wb').write(b + adr.replace('\\n','\\r\\n').encode('utf-8'))\nE\ncd ../..; timeout 900 python aikit.py check neurocore 2>&1 | grep -E \"^\\[PASS\\]|^\\[FAIL\\]|gates passed\" | cut -c1-90","description":"Add neurocore ADR-063 and rerun the project check","timeout":920000}},"serverClassifierRequest":"3be50906-11cb-4079-8d13-10ff6b166eec","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgX7MgcwtQ1r9r6LuuZBD","requestRef":"60cc5fea-bc4a-452e-afe6-4574b09e353e","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"aff6f538-2e2e-4b47-8aa1-d38c65b926b2","timestamp":"2026-10-29T19:51:11.479Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"C:\\Users\\Yunus-Emre\\Desktop\\portable_agent_kit\\projects\\neurocore","sessionId":"05aa96e5-db7a-4aed-bad4-f0f3cebd2787","version":"2.1.312","gitBranch":"main"}
