{"parentUuid":"5021489f-b015-48c6-a825-c19481b42780","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgX8731jxQ6K9as8Vquh4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LmDJKRJcX1myyAD7yXMrE2","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd \"C:/Users/Yunus-Emre/Desktop/portable_agent_kit/projects/neurocore\"; python - <<'E'\nadr = \"\"\"\n### ADR-064: Outbound tool calls are drafts until the user approves them\n- **Date**: 2026-10-29\n- **Status**: Accepted\n- **Context**: `SendEmail` was enabled by default and mailed any address the model named; the only\n  safeguard was its tool description. Incoming email (email bridge), `FetchURL` and knowledge-base\n  documents reach the same agent, so an injected instruction could send any content anywhere\n  (IDEA-032). Library tools run from four dispatchers: the tool dispatcher node and three agent\n  loop executors.\n- **Decision**: `modules/tools/outbound.py` names the outbound tools (`SendEmail`). Every dispatcher\n  calls `stage_if_outbound` before running a library tool; an outbound call is saved to\n  `data/outbound_drafts.json` (ledger lock, atomic write, at most 200 pending) and the model is\n  told it was NOT sent. `GET /tools/drafts` lists drafts; `POST /tools/drafts/{id}/send` requires\n  `confirm=send this draft` (the ADR-059 helper), claims the draft (`pending` to `sending`) under the\n  lock before running the tool code, and records `sent` or `failed`; `POST .../discard` drops one.\n  An unreadable draft store fails closed: nothing is drafted or sent. A test counts sandbox\n  executions against stage calls in both dispatcher files, so a new dispatcher cannot skip the gate.\n- **Consequences**: No email leaves without one explicit user action, and a draft is sent at most\n  once even when approved twice. Agent-driven email now needs that action. Replies through the\n  flow's `email_output` node are unchanged; a new outbound tool must be added to `OUTBOUND_TOOLS`.\n  There is no UI panel yet; the routes are JSON.\n- Cross-principle check: no principle section changed. Serves PRINCIPLE-019 (no exfiltration path\n  from untrusted input), PRINCIPLE-013 (claimed under a lock, written atomically) and PRINCIPLE-011\n  R6 (every refusal carries Why/Fix).\n\"\"\"\np='.aikit/decisions.md'\nb=open(p,'rb').read()\nopen(p,'wb').write(b + adr.replace('\\n','\\r\\n').encode('utf-8'))\nE\ncd ../..; python scripts/update_knowledge_base.py --workspace projects/neurocore 2>&1 | grep -E \"UPDATED|FAIL\" | head -2; timeout 900 python aikit.py check neurocore 2>&1 | grep -E \"^\\[PASS\\]|^\\[FAIL\\]|gates passed|^       \\[FAIL\\]|^ *(FAILED|E )\" | cut -c1-110 | head -12","description":"Add ADR-064, regenerate map, run project check","timeout":920000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":469,"cache_read_input_tokens":547486,"output_tokens":1140,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":469,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1140,"cache_read_input_tokens":547486,"cache_creation_input_tokens":469,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":469},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01LmDJKRJcX1myyAD7yXMrE2":{"command":"cd \"C:/Users/Yunus-Emre/Desktop/portable_agent_kit/projects/neurocore\"; python - <<'E'\nadr = \"\"\"\n### ADR-064: Outbound tool calls are drafts until the user approves them\n- **Date**: 2026-10-29\n- **Status**: Accepted\n- **Context**: `SendEmail` was enabled by default and mailed any address the model named; the only\n  safeguard was its tool description. Incoming email (email bridge), `FetchURL` and knowledge-base\n  documents reach the same agent, so an injected instruction could send any content anywhere\n  (IDEA-032). Library tools run from four dispatchers: the tool dispatcher node and three agent\n  loop executors.\n- **Decision**: `modules/tools/outbound.py` names the outbound tools (`SendEmail`). Every dispatcher\n  calls `stage_if_outbound` before running a library tool; an outbound call is saved to\n  `data/outbound_drafts.json` (ledger lock, atomic write, at most 200 pending) and the model is\n  told it was NOT sent. `GET /tools/drafts` lists drafts; `POST /tools/drafts/{id}/send` requires\n  `confirm=send this draft` (the ADR-059 helper), claims the draft (`pending` to `sending`) under the\n  lock before running the tool code, and records `sent` or `failed`; `POST .../discard` drops one.\n  An unreadable draft store fails closed: nothing is drafted or sent. A test counts sandbox\n  executions against stage calls in both dispatcher files, so a new dispatcher cannot skip the gate.\n- **Consequences**: No email leaves without one explicit user action, and a draft is sent at most\n  once even when approved twice. Agent-driven email now needs that action. Replies through the\n  flow's `email_output` node are unchanged; a new outbound tool must be added to `OUTBOUND_TOOLS`.\n  There is no UI panel yet; the routes are JSON.\n- Cross-principle check: no principle section changed. Serves PRINCIPLE-019 (no exfiltration path\n  from untrusted input), PRINCIPLE-013 (claimed under a lock, written atomically) and PRINCIPLE-011\n  R6 (every refusal carries Why/Fix).\n\"\"\"\np='.aikit/decisions.md'\nb=open(p,'rb').read()\nopen(p,'wb').write(b + adr.replace('\\n','\\r\\n').encode('utf-8'))\nE\ncd ../..; python scripts/update_knowledge_base.py --workspace projects/neurocore 2>&1 | grep -E \"UPDATED|FAIL\" | head -2; timeout 900 python aikit.py check neurocore 2>&1 | grep -E \"^\\[PASS\\]|^\\[FAIL\\]|gates 