{"parentUuid":"f0989f89-82aa-4b2f-b464-dd61588f51da","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgX8w3h1RcD7Q2cfw8SPk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've finished both P2 security items in neurocore. All four project gates pass, including the full test suite, and nothing is committed.\n\n**IDEA-063: DNS rebinding is closed.**\n- Both URL fetchers used to check that a hostname resolves to a public address, then look it up again when connecting. A domain that changed its answer between the two lookups could slip a private address past the check.\n- They now connect to the exact address that passed. The research gateway does this at every redirect step, and the skill importer does it too. The hostname is still used for TLS, so certificates are verified as before.\n- I tested this against the real Wikipedia: the fetch works, and pairing Wikipedia's address with a different hostname is refused by certificate verification.\n- One limit: only the first approved address is tried, so if that server is down the request fails rather than falling back to another.\n\n**IDEA-032: the agent can no longer send email by itself.**\n- When the agent calls `SendEmail`, it now saves a draft and is told plainly that nothing was sent. All four places the agent runs tools go through this check. A test counts those places, so a new one added later can't quietly skip it.\n- You send a draft with `POST /tools/drafts/{id}/send?confirm=send this draft`. Drafts are listed at `GET /tools/drafts` and discarded with `POST /tools/drafts/{id}/discard`. Each draft can be sent at most once, even if approved twice. If the draft store can't be read, nothing is sent.\n- **What changes for you:** any email the agent writes now needs one approval from you before it goes out. Replies through the flow's `email_output` node work as before.\n- **What's missing:** there's no approval button in the UI yet, only the API routes above. Tell me if you want a panel added.\n\n**Also done:**\n- My route test was rewriting `modules/tools/module.json` (a trailing-newline change). I restored the file and added it to the list in `tests/conftest.py` that tests back up and restore.\n- I added ADR-063 and ADR-064, updated the README, `docs/TOOL_GUIDE.md` and `docs/IDEAS.md` (both gaps now ticked), regenerated the codebase map, and set both ideas to Integrating.\n\n**Waiting on you:**\n- 15 modified and 4 new files in neurocore, uncommitted.\n- The five AIKit changes from earlier, also uncommitted.\n\nSay \"commit\" for either or both.\n\nNext in neurocore is P3: scanning memory writes for injected text (334) and marking untrusted content with boundary tags (030)."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":509,"cache_read_input_tokens":554441,"output_tokens":943,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":108},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":509,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":943,"cache_read_input_tokens":554441,"cache_creation_input_tokens":509,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":509},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"e382e25f-ac2c-44ef-b360-6f287fe4c7e6","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgX8w3HSmEziVtncfUZcm","requestRef":"6ccebb70-de42-439d-bc4e-1b9478c30d60","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"d59ad464-2654-427a-8dea-873fee46c041","timestamp":"2026-10-29T20:11:52.626Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"C:\\Users\\Yunus-Emre\\Desktop\\portable_agent_kit"