{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"05aa96e5-db7a-4aed-bad4-f0f3cebd2787","hash":"04e09c6f2caeeb07a1a51c35d9e32540cd1d88218418f572314068d5296898c5","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014yNvv311eRXEmimFsdZXeG","name":"Edit","input":{"file_path":"c:\\Users\\Yunus-Emre\\Desktop\\portable_agent_kit\\projects\\neurocore\\README.md","old_string":"separators and instruction overrides on chat input and knowledge-base chunks, credential shapes on\nevery surface, and verbatim system-prompt echoes on output. `brain_guardrail_mode` is `observe`\n(default: report and count) or `enforce` (block an injected message or document, replace a leaked\nresponse).","new_string":"separators and instruction overrides on chat input, knowledge-base chunks and every memory or goal\nwrite, credential shapes on every surface, and verbatim system-prompt echoes on output.\n`brain_guardrail_mode` is `observe` (default: report and count) or `enforce` (block an injected\nmessage, document, memory or goal, replace a leaked response)."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01VYVyuTjWr56b15qh9jSU89","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd \"C:/Users/Yunus-Emre/Desktop/portable_agent_kit/projects/neurocore\"; python - <<'E'\nadr = \"\"\"\n### ADR-065: Memory and goal writes follow the guardrail policy\n- **Date**: 2026-10-29\n- **Status**: Accepted\n- **Context**: Guardrails scanned chat input, knowledge-base chunks and tool output, but nothing\n  screened text bound for long-term memory or goals. A memory is recalled in every later session\n  and the active goal is re-injected as a system message on each turn, so injected text saved once\n  persisted indefinitely (IDEA-334).\n- **Decision**: Guardrails gain a `memory` surface; `BLOCKING_SURFACES` (`input`, `memory`) are the\n  surfaces where enforce mode refuses an injection pattern. `screen_memory_text` in\n  `modules/memory/backend.py` scans `add_entry`, `update_entry`, `create_goal` and `update_goal`\n  text before the write lock. In enforce mode `add_entry` returns `-1`, its existing \"rejected\"\n  answer that the arbiter and learning loop already handle; the others raise the new\n  `MemoryContentBlocked`, which the memory routes return as 400 with Why/Fix. Observe mode stores\n  the text, logs the rules matched and counts them under `memory:` in the guardrail status.\n- **Consequences**: The persistence path for prompt injection follows the same policy as every\n  other surface. With the default `observe` mode nothing is refused, only counted; an operator who\n  wants refusals sets `brain_guardrail_mode` to `enforce`. Text already in memory is not rescanned.\n- Cross-principle check: no principle section changed. Serves PRINCIPLE-019 (untrusted text does\n  not become trusted state) and PRINCIPLE-011 R6 (a refusal carries Why/Fix).\n\"\"\"\np='.aikit/decisions.md'\nb=open(p,'rb').read()\nopen(p,'wb').write(b + adr.replace('\\n','\\r\\n').encode('utf-8'))\nE\ncd ../..; python scripts/update_knowledge_base.py --workspace projects/neurocore 2>&1 | grep -E \"UPDATED|FAIL\"; timeout 900 python aikit.py check neurocore 2>&1 | grep -E \"^\\[PASS\\]|^\\[FAIL\\]|gates passed|^       \\[FAIL\\]|^   - \" | cut -c1-120 | head -8","description":"Add ADR-065, regenerate map, run project check","timeout":920000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
