stant","uuid":"dfe9e20d-5510-47df-ac72-1c2546ca4bcf","timestamp":"2026-10-29T20:51:58.467Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"C:\\Users\\Yunus-Emre\\Desktop\\portable_agent_kit","sessionId":"05aa96e5-db7a-4aed-bad4-f0f3cebd2787","version":"2.1.312","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"dfe9e20d-5510-47df-ac72-1c2546ca4bcf","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"417ceb17-a197-41b9-afc1-705bcfa65a6a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NDokP9i2dwcK9EeN9ayfoC","type":"tool_result","content":"#### Core Mechanism & Value\nPasted or tool-returned text is wrapped in tags carrying a per-block random id, so a payload cannot forge the closing tag. Widget state is isolated as untrusted. A lightweight classifier injects a safety reminder mid-turn only when risk is detected, keeping the base prompt lean.\n#### Potential Improvements\n- `wrap_untrusted_content(text, source)` in `modules/security/guardrails.py`, applied to every tool result and retrieved document.\n- A `maybe_safety_reminder(text)` hook that adds a reminder only on classifier hit.\n#### Potential Weaknesses\nStatic fences (`[BEGIN EXTERNAL CONTENT]`) can be spoofed by content containing the literal marker. Classifier reminders have false positives that can derail benign chats.\n#### How to Combat These\nGenerate `secrets.token_hex(8)` per block and strip any occurrence of the nonce or the tag prefix from the payload before wrapping. Keep reminders short, rate-limited to one per turn, and log trigger reasons without the content.\n#### Cold-Start Agent Implementation Blueprint\n1. **Target Workspace & Pre-Flight Command**: workspace `projects/neurocore`; `python aikit.py status neurocore`.\n2. **Target Files & Symbols**: `modules/security/guardrails.py` add `wrap_untrusted_content`, `maybe_safety_reminder`; call from the tool-result path in `modules/agents/orchestrator.py`.\n3. **Contract & DTO Specification**:\n   ```python\n   def wrap_untrusted_content(text: str, source: str, *, nonce: str | None = None) -> str:\n       \"\"\"Return '<untrusted_content_{n} source=...>...</untrusted_content_{n}>' with a fresh nonce; payload sanitized.\"\"\"\n   ```\n4. **Failing-First Test Specification**: assert two calls yield different tags; a payload containing `</untrusted_content_` and the supplied nonce cannot terminate the block early; `source` is escaped; the reminder fires for an injection phrase and not for plain text.\n5. **Step-by-Step Integration Sequence**: read guardrails and orchestrator tool-result code; write failing tests; implement; wire into the tool result path; run the suite.\n6. **Verification & Rollback**: unit tests; rollback by reverting (wrapping is additive).\n### `IDEA-031`: Capability-Stripped Read-Only `Dreamer` Memory Consolidator\n- **Target Project**: `neurocore`\n- **Priority / Effort vs. Impact**: `Med-High Impact / Med Effort`\n#### Core Mechanism & Value","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"75069635-eb2c-471c-b99c-3502bda4360d","timestamp":"2026-10-29T20:51:59.810Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"#### Core Mechanism & Value\nPasted or tool-returned text is wrapped in tags carrying a per-block random id, so a payload cannot forge the closing tag. Widget state is isolated as untrusted. A lightweight classifier injects a safety reminder mid-turn only when risk is detected, keeping the base prompt lean.\n#### Potential Improvements\n- `wrap_untrusted_content(text, source)` in `modules/security/guardrails.py`, applied to every tool result and retrieved document.\n- A `maybe_safety_reminder(text)` hook that adds a reminder only on classifier hit.\n#### Potential Weaknesses\nStatic fences (`[BEGIN EXTERNAL CONTENT]`) can be spoofed by content containing the literal marker. Classifier reminders have false positives that can derail benign chats.\n#### How to Combat These\nGenerate `secrets.token_hex(8)` per block and strip any occurrence of the nonce or the tag prefix from the payload before wrapping. Keep reminders short, rate-limited to one per turn, and log trigger reasons without the content.\n#### Cold-Start Agent Implementation Blueprint\n1. **Target Workspace & Pre-Flight Command**: workspace `projects/neurocore`; `python aikit.py status neurocore`.\n2. **Target Files & Symbols**: `modules/security/guardrails.py` add `wrap_untrusted_content`, `maybe_safety_reminder`; call from the tool-result path in `modules/agents/orchestrator.py`.\n3. **Contract & DTO Specification**:\n   ```python\n   def wrap_untrusted_content(text: str, source: str, *, nonce: str | None = None) -> str:\n       \"\"\"Return '<untrusted_content_{n} source=...>...</untrusted_content_{n}>' with a fresh nonce; payload sanitized.\"\"\"\n   ```\n4. **Failing-First Test Specification**: assert two calls yield different tags; a payload containing `</untrusted_content_` and the supplied nonce cannot terminate the block early; `source` is escaped; the reminder fires for an injection phrase and not for plain text.\n5. **Step-by-Step Integration Sequence**: read guardrails and orchestrator tool-result code; write failing tests; implement; wire into the tool result path; run the suite.\n6. **Verification & Rollback**: unit tests; rollback by reverting (wrapping is additive).\n### `IDEA-031`: Capability-Stripped Read-Only `Dreamer` Memory Consolidator\n- **Target Project**: `neurocore`\n- **Priority / Effort vs. Impact**: `Med-High Impact / Med Effort`\n#### Core Mechanism & Value","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"c32f3b00-d084-4e51-adad-ddcb9cc18294","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/c/Users/Yunus-Emre/Desktop/portable_agent_kit","root":"/c/Users/Yunus-Emre/Desktop/portable_agent_kit","branch":"main","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"AegeanWorks/AIKit","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"AegeanWorks/AIKit","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"AegeanWorks/AIKit","visibility":"public"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"AegeanWorks/research-engine","visibility