{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"05aa96e5-db7a-4aed-bad4-f0f3cebd2787","hash":"31d327fe30533c18469c626c6694d5f34d2dcab80920f88bebdeaa77e4492d24","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"All 2,002 tests pass with nothing skipped beyond the existing 7, so wrapping at the bridge broke nothing. Documentation and ADR-066 next:"},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Te8ZsZK6T4i2SZ6HT625Sb","name":"Edit","input":{"file_path":"c:\\Users\\Yunus-Emre\\Desktop\\portable_agent_kit\\projects\\neurocore\\README.md","old_string":"output and tool results in both modes. `GET /brain/guardrails/status` reports counters and","new_string":"output and tool results in both modes. Every tool result sent to a model and every retrieved\nknowledge chunk is fenced as data in an `<untrusted_content_<random id>>` block naming its source\n(`core/untrusted.py`), so text inside cannot pass for instructions or close its own block.\n`GET /brain/guardrails/status` reports counters and"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011y8XPVm5Rofs6YutYee52g","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd \"C:/Users/Yunus-Emre/Desktop/portable_agent_kit/projects/neurocore\"; python - <<'E'\nadr = \"\"\"\n### ADR-066: Untrusted text reaches the model inside a random-id fence\n- **Date**: 2026-10-29\n- **Status**: Accepted\n- **Context**: Tool output (a fetched page, an incoming email, a search result) and retrieved\n  knowledge-base chunks entered prompts as plain text, so an instruction inside them read exactly\n  like the operator's, and nothing marked where the untrusted text began or ended (IDEA-030).\n- **Decision**: `core/untrusted.py` provides `wrap_untrusted`: a one-line note that the block is\n  data from a named source, then `<untrusted_content_<16 hex>>` with a fresh `secrets` id per block;\n  tag-shaped text in the payload is neutralized and the source label is restricted to safe\n  characters. `LLMBridge.chat_completion` and `chat_completion_stream` send a copy of the messages\n  with every `role: tool` message fenced (`fence_tool_messages`, never twice), so all four tool\n  dispatchers are covered at the one exit. The knowledge-base node fences each chunk when it builds\n  `knowledge_context`. A first attempt fenced tool results where they are produced and broke stuck\n  detection, which reads the raw text; fencing on the way out keeps the agent loop's own logic\n  (stuck detection, truncation, traces) on the raw content.\n- **Consequences**: Every untrusted block is visibly data to the model and cannot be closed by its\n  own content. Prompts grow by about 120 characters per tool result or chunk. Memory recall and\n  the system prompt are not fenced: memory writes are screened instead (ADR-065). Fencing is a\n  signal to the model, not a guarantee; the guardrail scans remain the enforcement.\n- Cross-principle check: no principle section changed. Serves PRINCIPLE-019 (untrusted input stays\n  distinguishable) and PRINCIPLE-003 (the change sits at the single exit every model call uses).\n\"\"\"\np='.aikit/decisions.md'\nb=open(p,'rb').read()\nopen(p,'wb').write(b + adr.replace('\\n','\\r\\n').encode('utf-8'))\nE\nfor f in core/untrusted.py core/llm.py modules/knowledge_base/node.py modules/brain/guardrails.py tests/test_untrusted_fences.py README.md; do git ls-files --eol \"$f\" 2>/dev/null | awk '{print $2, $4}'; done; python -c \"\nfor p in ['core/llm.py','modules/knowledge_base/node.py','README.md']:\n    b=open(p,'rb').read(); print(p,'crlf',b.count(b'\\r\\n'),'lf',b.count(b'\\n')-b.count(b'\\r\\n'))\"\ncd ../..; python scripts/update_knowledge_base.py --workspace projects/neurocore 2>&1 | grep -E \"UPDATED|FAIL\"; timeout 900 python aikit.py check neurocore 2>&1 | grep -E \"^\\[PASS\\]|^\\[FAIL\\]|gates passed|^       \\[FAIL\\]|^   - \" | cut -c1-110 | head -8","description":"Add ADR-066, check line endings, run project check","timeout":920000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
