{"parentUuid":"8629a359-5f92-4699-94e6-3c274539f7a1","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgXDKNMVzqQbVUvp6SpRX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now ADR-067, which records the decision to allow autonomy, the safety rails, and what still waits for you. Then the codebase map and the full project check:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1051,"cache_read_input_tokens":681522,"output_tokens":1672,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":135},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1051,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1672,"cache_read_input_tokens":681522,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1051,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1051},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"d63df6ce-005f-4646-9e6e-93f2f4c88b12","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgXDKMwghdL3zz67WWFUi","requestRef":"667dbabc-8c53-4a2d-acd6-3a4d8cc7124b","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"f8bd7757-13ca-49cd-a7ef-92c974ffb149","timestamp":"2026-10-29T21:09:15.404Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"C:\\Users\\Yunus-Emre\\Desktop\\portable_agent_kit\\projects\\neurocore","sessionId":"05aa96e5-db7a-4aed-bad4-f0f3cebd2787","version":"2.1.312","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"f8bd7757-13ca-49cd-a7ef-92c974ffb149","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgXDKNMVzqQbVUvp6SpRX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01ELisTygcXPrrDEg8CNGKVK","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd \"C:/Users/Yunus-Emre/Desktop/portable_agent_kit/projects/neurocore\"; python - <<'E'\nadr = \"\"\"\n### ADR-067: The brain can act autonomously and be talked to from its page\n- **Date**: 2026-10-30\n- **Status**: Accepted\n- **Context**: The operator asked for a Brain section to start the brain and interact with it, with\n  chat plus structured control, and for the brain to act autonomously. The `/brain/ui` dashboard\n  (ADR-032) could start, stop and inspect the brain but offered no conversation, the navbar hid it\n  while the opt-in module (ADR-036) was off, and `set_mode` refused anything beyond\n  observe/suggest. ADR-028 had already built the kernel, ADR-041 the goal link and ADR-046 the\n  daily self-budget as the rails autonomy would need.\n- **Decision**:\n  1. A third mode, `autonomous`. Its cycles generate proposals as `suggest` does and then, outside\n     the state lock, act on pending proposals that have an entry in `AUTONOMOUS_ACTIONS`\n     (`modules/brain/autonomy.py`): record a baseline (only through `promote_baseline`, which\n     refuses anything below a perfect run), review a failing evaluation, consolidate learning,\n     check recall. Each action needs `kernel.can_run_autonomy()` and one unit of its self-budget\n     kind; at most `max_autonomous_actions_per_cycle` (default 2) run per cycle; every attempt is\n     journaled in `state.actions` (newest first, 50 kept) with actor, status and result. SAFE\n     kernel still forces `observe`. No tool, flow or outbound action is reachable; outbound tools\n     stay drafts (ADR-064).\n  2. `modules/brain/conversation.py`: `POST /brain/chat` sends the message with a bounded view of\n     the live state and asks for JSON `{reply, commands}`; at most three commands, only from\n     `COMMANDS` (the autonomous actions plus `run_cycle`, `run_evaluation`, `set_goal`). In\n     autonomous mode they run as `brain:chat` and are journaled; otherwise they return as\n     suggestions that `POST /brain/commands` runs for the requesting actor. History is kept in\n     `data/brain_chat.json` (100 messages, ledger lock, atomic write). Goal text passes the memory\n     guardrail (ADR-065).\n  3. `/brain/ui` gains a mode switch, a chat panel with Run buttons for suggestions and a journal;\n     the navbar always shows Brain, and while the module is off the link enables it and opens the\n     page, so opting in stays one deliberate click.\n- **Consequences**: The brain can now maintain its own evaluation baseline and learning without a\n  person, bounded per cycle and per day; everything it does is visible in its journal. A model that\n  answers with anything but the allow-listed commands can only talk. Proposals that need a person\n  (provider repair, flow activation, memory seeding) still wait. The chat needs the configured LLM;\n  without one it returns 502 with Why/Fix.\n- Cross-principle check: no principle section changed. Serves PRINCIPLE-013 (journal and history\n  are written atomically under a lock), PRINCIPLE-019 (no path from chat to tools or outbound\n  actions) and PRINCIPLE-011 R6 (every refusal carries Why/Fix).\n\"\"\"\np='.aikit/decisions.md'\nb=open(p,'rb').read()\nopen(p,'wb').write(b + adr.replace('\\n','\\r\\n').encode('utf-8'))\nE\ncd ../..; python scripts/update_knowledge_base.py --workspace projects/neurocore 2>&1 | grep -E \"UPDATED|FAIL\"; timeout 900 python aikit.py check neurocore 2>&1 | grep -E \"^\\[PASS\\]|^\\[FAIL\\]|gates passed|^       \\[FAIL\\]|^   - |FAILED\" | cut -c1-120 | head -10","description":"Add ADR-067, regenerate map, run project check","timeout":920000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1051,"cache_read_input_tokens":681522,"output_tokens":1672,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":135},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1051,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1672,"cache_read_input_tokens":681522,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1051,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1051},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01ELisTygcXPrrDEg8CNGKVK":{"command":"cd \"C:/Users/Yunus-Emre/Desktop/portable_agent_kit/projects/neurocore\"; python - <<'E'\nadr = \"\"\"\n### ADR-067: The brain can act autonomously and be talked to from its page\n- **Date**: 2026-10-30\n- **Status**: Accepted\n- **Context**: The operator asked for a Brain section to start the brain and interact with it, with\n  chat plus structured control, and for the brain to act autonomously. The `/brain/ui` dashboard\n  (ADR-032) could start, stop and inspect the brain but offered no conversation, the navbar hid it\n  while the opt-in module (ADR-036) was off, and `set_mode` refused anything beyond\n  observe/suggest. ADR-028 had already built the kernel, ADR-041 the goal link and ADR-046 the\n  daily self-budget as the rails autonomy would need.\n- **Decision**:\n  1. A third mode, `autonomous`. Its cycles generate proposals as `suggest` does and then, outside\n     the state lock, act on pending proposals that have an entry in `AUTONOMOUS_ACTIONS`\n     (`modules/brain/autonomy.py`): record a baseline (only through `promote_baseline`, which\n     refuses anything below a perfect run), review a failing evaluation, consolidate learning,\n     check recall. Each action needs `kernel.can_run_autonomy()` and one unit of its self-budget\n     kind; at most `max_autonomous_actions_per_cycle` (default 2) run per cycle; every attempt is\n     journaled in `state.actions` (newest first, 50 kept) with actor, status and result. SAFE\n     kernel still forces `observe`. No tool, flow or outbound action is reachable; outbound tools\n     stay drafts (ADR-064).\n  2. `modules/brain/conversation.py`: `POST /brain/chat` sends the message with a bounded view of\n     the live state and asks for JSON `{reply, commands}`; at most three commands, only from\n     `COMMANDS` (the autonomous actions plus `run_cycle`, `run_evaluation`, `set_goal`). In\n     autonomous mode they run as `brain:chat` and are journaled; otherwise they return as\n     suggestions that `POST /brain/commands` runs for the requesting actor. History is kept in\n     `data/brain_chat.json` (100 messages, ledger lock, atomic write). Goal text passes the memory\n     guardrail (ADR-065).\n  3. `/brain/ui` gains a mode switch, a chat panel with Run buttons for suggestions and a journal;\n     the navbar always shows Brain, and while the module is off the link enables it and opens the\n     page, so opting in stays one deliberate click.\n- **Consequences**: The brain can now maintain its own evaluation baseline and learning without a\n  person, bounded per cycle and per day; everything it does is visible in its journal. A model that\n  answers with anything but the allow-listed commands can only talk. Proposals that need a person\n  (provider repair, flow activation, memory seeding) still wait. The chat needs the configured LLM;\n  without one it returns 502 with Why/Fix.\n- Cross-principle check: no principle section changed. Serves PRINCIPLE-013 (journal and history\n  are written atomically under a lock), PRINCIPLE-019 (no path from chat to tools or outbound\n  actions) and PRINCIPLE-011 R6 (every refusal carries Why/Fix).\n\"\"\"\np='.aikit/decisions.md'\nb=open(p,'rb').read()\nopen(p,'wb').write(b + adr.replace('\\n','\\r\\n').encode('utf-8'))\nE\ncd ../..; python scripts/update_knowledge_base.py --workspace projects/neurocore 2>&1 | grep -E \"UPDATED|FAIL\"; timeout 900 python aikit.py check neurocore 2>&1 | grep -E \"^\\[PASS\\]|^\\[FAIL\\]|gates passed|^       \\[FAIL\\]|^   - |FAILED\" | cut -c1-120 | head -10","description":"Add ADR-067, regenerate map, run project check","timeout":920000}},"serverClassifierRequest":"d63df6ce-005f-4646-9e6e-93f2f4c88b12","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgXDKMwghdL3zz67WWFUi","requestRef":"667dbabc-8c53-4a2d-acd6-3a4d8cc7124b","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"5a825160-05ab-4695-a99e-d761c4de24dd","timestamp":"2026-10-29T21:09:27.851Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"C:\\Users\\Yunus-Emre\\Desktop\\portable_agent_kit\\projects\\neurocore","sessionId":"05aa96e5-db7a-4aed-bad4-f0f3cebd2787","version":"2.1.312","gitBranch":"main"}
