{"parentUuid":"5a99d8c1-7fdb-44a5-a589-e0984e74476d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgXE7JHwmvuMMaE7jXYrZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The Brain section works, but **your running server needs a restart.** While you were trying it, the brain was crashing on every cycle because of an older bug that I've now fixed. Your server doesn't auto-reload, so `/brain/state` keeps returning 500 until you restart it.\n\n**The bug.** On an install that has never run an evaluation, a missing pass rate was passed to `float()`. That crashed every brain cycle and every status request, so the brain could never have worked on a fresh install. Tests missed it because their fake self-model leaves the value out. I reproduced the crash on a copy of your real brain data, fixed it, and replayed the cycle on that copy. It now completes on its own: it ran the evaluation, recorded a baseline, and left two proposals waiting for you.\n\n**What you have now:**\n- **Brain in the navbar, always.** While the module is off the link reads \"Brain (off)\", and clicking it turns the module on and opens the page.\n- **Mode switch:** observe, suggest or **autonomous**.\n  - In autonomous mode, each cycle acts on its own proposals, from a fixed list: run or review the evaluation, record a baseline, consolidate learning, check recall.\n  - At most 2 actions per cycle, each needing a healthy kernel and room in the daily budget. SAFE mode forces it back to observe, and the kill switch still works.\n  - It can't use tools or send anything outward; email still waits for your approval.\n  - Proposals that need a person (fix a provider, activate a flow, add memories) wait for you.\n- **Chat.** You talk to it with its live state as context. Its replies can include commands from the same fixed list plus \"run a cycle\" and \"add a goal\". In autonomous mode it runs them; otherwise each shows a Run button.\n- **\"What it did\" journal:** every action with who triggered it, the outcome and the time.\n\n**Things to know:**\n- **Your settings are untouched.** Your clicks in the app enabled the Brain and Autonomous Agent modules on disk. I didn't change those files and kept them out of the work, so whether those modules ship enabled stays your decision.\n- **One test now checks something different.** It used to require that a disabled brain has no navbar link; your request changes that. It still checks the brain isn't routed until you turn it on. ADR-067 names the change.\n- **Chat isn't tested against a real model.** No LLM is running at `localhost:1234` right now, so the chat is only tested with a scripted model. Without a model it returns a clear 502 telling you to check the LLM URL.\n\n**Verification:** all 2,015 tests pass in a clean copy with the shipped module defaults, and the hygiene, guidelines and secrets gates pass.\n\nNothing is committed. Neurocore now holds 7 finished changes:\n- the two P2 security fixes (DNS rebinding, email drafts);\n- the two P3 fixes (memory-write scanning, untrusted-content fences);\n- the Brain section, with the drift fix included.\n\nAIKit has its 5 from earlier. Say \"commit\" when you want them in."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":855,"cache_read_input_tokens":705112,"output_tokens":1004,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":855,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1004,"cache_read_input_tokens":705112,"cache_creation_input_tokens":855,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":855},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":nul