quence, kind, subject, payload digest, previous hash, hash. A high-water counter makes a deleted tail unreusable. `ledger anchor --out FILE` commits `(seq, head)` to an external journal; `ledger verify --anchors` walks the chain and detects an edit, a gap or a truncation. The trust boundary is the published anchor, not the local file. The engine's append-only tables are ordinary rows. A probe deleted the newest eve\n982 High/Low Cascade Volume Guard :: Before `claim invalidate` or `source retract` writes, compute the whole affected set. If it is implausibly large both absolutely and proportionally, refuse the entire transaction and report a held-back event. A mistaken mass collapse is terminal for promotion and can only be repaired by revisions; the guard turns a one-command catastrophe into a reviewable decision. The engine already computes the transitive set; it simply applies it. A 30-claim program can lose 25 claims becaus\n983 High/Med Whole-State Fingerprint :: Hash schema version, counters, schema metadata and every table in canonical order. The fingerprint becomes a witness of completeness: if it does not change, no logical state changed. Use it to prove that `cascade preview`, `analysis`, `outline`, `brief`, `report` (without `--out`) and `export --check` are read-only, and that a backup is logically identical to the source. `db integrity` currently runs SQLite PRAGMAs only; it cannot tell a read-only command from a writer, and a\n984 Med-High/Low Finding-Code Registry and Capabilities Manifest :: Every finding code is one registry record: code, family, default severity, summary. A scanner finds code literals in `engine/*.py`; tests fail when a literal is unregistered, a registry entry is missing from the README, or a code appears in one but not the other. A `capabilities` command derives commands, exit codes, vocabularies and limits from live constants. The engine emits 20+ codes across `integrity.py`, but `test_docs.py` checks only 8 and t\n985 High/Med Review Provenance and Inter-Rater Agreement :: Record who decided, under which criteria version, and with what independent second opinion. Screening becomes append-only decisions rather than one mutable row. Two reviewers can screen the same source; the engine computes Cohen's kappa for two raters or Krippendorff's alpha for missing/multiple raters, and a conflict requires an explicit resolution. Verdicts and observations also carry the actor. The engine currently defaults the actor to `\"agent\"`, has n\n986 High/Med Pre-Registered Analysis Plan :: Register claim, baseline label, treatment label, direction and expected effect before the groups have data. A plan registered after data exists is accepted but marked `post_data`. `analysis stats` matches a plan, stores the plan id and observation digest, and labels an unmatched run exploratory. A `NUMERIC` promotion whose latest stats run is exploratory warns. Hypothesis pre-registration stops one step too early: the researcher can still choose the comparison after seei\n987 Med-High/Low Protocol Document Recompute :: When a protocol names a document, hash the document, not a string the operator typed. `protocol add --doc PATH` computes the digest; `protocol verify` re-reads and compares; an observation stores the protocol digest it used. A changed document is an error, a missing document a warning. The current `--doc-digest` accepts any 64-hex string and is never recomputed. A probe registered a protocol with `a`*64; `check` accepted it.\n988 Med/Low Robust Observation Summary :: Add median, quartiles, IQR, MAD and a Tukey outlier flag to the observation summary. Scale values by their largest magnitude before squaring so extreme finite inputs do not overflow. Report an outlier count as a warning; never trim or void automatically. `observation_summary` currently prints only n, min, max and mean. One corrupt value can dominate Welch/Cohen's d with no visible warning, and `statistics.variance` can raise on `[1e308, -1e308]`.\n989 Med/Low Polarity-Aware Contradiction Proposals :: Keep negation tokens out of the content set and record a polarity bit. High-overlap pairs with opposite polarity are contradiction candidates; high-overlap same-polarity pairs are paraphrases/duplicates. Rank opposite pairs first and include the shared terms in the reason. Advisory only; never auto-link. `analysis.keywords` currently treats `not`/`no` as stopwords, so it erases polarity. `unlinked_contradictions` scores pure Jaccard and can rank a paraphrase abo\n990 High/Med Comparison Family with Holm Correction :: A p-value is only interpretable inside the family of tests that were actually run. Declare a family label, record each member's raw p-value and test kind, and report the Holm-adjusted p for every member. Holm controls the family-wise error rate under arbitrary dependence and is simple enough to keep the engine standard-library only. `analysis.stats` currently warns that a single pairwise test is uncorrected when more than two groups exist, but the warning disap\n991 High/Med Verified Restore with Quarantine :: `db restore BACKUP [--force]` verifies the backup's SQLite integrity and schema first, then moves the live database and its `-wal`/`-shm` sidecars into a timestamped `.corrupt_<utc>` quarantine, copies the backup through a flushed temporary file and `os.replace`, and re-verifies the result. A failed restore puts the quarantine back. `db backup` gains a sidecar with schema, counts, SHA-256 and engine version. A backup without a tested restore path is only a copy. A re\n992 Med/Low Aggregate Context Pack :: `context RESEARCH --budget N` assembles one orientation pack from the existing line builders: header and counts, questions, strongest claims, open findings and measurement summaries. Allocate a fixed share to each section, pack each share with the existing `context.pack`, and assert the final `estimate_tokens(text) <= N`. Report per-section omitted counts and the total. Today `outline`, `brief` and `claim context` each take an independent budget; an agent that calls all three c\n993 High/Med Pre-Registration Amendment Ledger :: An amendment is an append-only row: subject kind and id, field, old value, new value, reason, actor and time. `hypothesis amend` and `protocol amend` write it; `hypothesis card` and `protocol list` show the chain. The original registration stays visible, and calibration scores the original confidence unless a new hypothesis is created. A statement or criterion change is not a cosmetic edit: it changes what the evidence was supposed to test. Without a ledger, a post-","numLines":51,"startLine":1,"totalLines":51}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"73dbd771-969d-4482-91bd-fee38b8f6e96","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"C:\\Users\\Yunus-Emre\\Desktop\\portable_agent_kit\\projects\\research-engine","sessionId":"05aa96e5-db7a-4aed-bad4-f0f3cebd2787","version":"2.1.312","gitBranch":"main"}
