{"parentUuid":"58c1e685-6ce7-43bf-8206-b966c97beea4","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"environment","snapshot":{"workingDirectory":"C:\\Users\\Yunus-Emre\\Desktop\\portable_agent_kit","isWorktree":false,"isGitRepo":true,"additionalWorkingDirectories":[],"platform":"win32","shell":"PowerShell (primary); Bash tool also available for POSIX scripts — each takes its own syntax.","osVersion":"Windows 11 Pro 10.0.26200","scratchpadDirectory":"C:\\Users\\YUNUS-~1\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\c--Users-Yunus-Emre-Desktop-portable-agent-kit\\05aa96e5-db7a-4aed-bad4-f0f3cebd2787\\scratchpad"},"changes":[{"field":"workingDirectory","from":"C:\\Users\\Yunus-Emre\\Desktop\\portable_agent_kit\\projects\\research-engine"}]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"9279f3c0-2e64-4be1-9f91-572d13bfebee","timestamp":"2026-10-30T12:35:11.525Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n# Environment update\n - Primary working directory: C:\\Users\\Yunus-Emre\\Desktop\\portable_agent_kit (was C:\\Users\\Yunus-Emre\\Desktop\\portable_agent_kit\\projects\\research-engine)\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"C:\\Users\\Yunus-Emre\\Desktop\\portable_agent_kit","sessionId":"05aa96e5-db7a-4aed-bad4-f0f3cebd2787","version":"2.1.312","gitBranch":"main"}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"05aa96e5-db7a-4aed-bad4-f0f3cebd2787","hash":"3db6833eb64d313ecb5d880b3977160765e55ae857e047e26cf0023590aacc4a","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'll record verdicts only for research-engine's 51 ideas since another agent owns that task: approving code-verified defects (evidence binding, retraction, cascade safety, statistical correctness), deferring literature-import ideas like GRADE/PICO and PaperQA, and rejecting anything assuming an LLM loop since this engine is standard-library only. I'll also note the overlap between ongoing ADR work and IDEA-964/IDEA-980 in their verdicts.\n\n","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017zhJXYskL2GengbFtTXGrB","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\YUNUS-~1\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\c--Users-Yunus-Emre-Desktop-portable-agent-kit\\05aa96e5-db7a-4aed-bad4-f0f3cebd2787\\scratchpad\\v_research-engine.py","content":"TARGET = \"research-engine\"\nA, D, R, S = \"Approved\", \"Deferred\", \"Rejected\", \"Superseded\"\nNOLLM = (\"Rejected: no consumer. Research Engine is standard-library only and makes no model or network calls; \"\n         \"an LLM retrieval or agent loop has nothing to attach to.\")\nMODEL = \"Deferred: a new evidence-reasoning model, not a defect; revisit when a real program needs it and the mined integrity fixes have landed.\"\nV = {\n    # --- mined defects, verified against HEAD 6533434 ---\n    \"980\": (A, \"P1 INTEGRITY: sources always insert, DOI is not unique, and `retracted -> active` is accepted, so a retraction \"\n                \"is bypassed by a twin row. ADR-036 (in progress) only detects split sources; retraction must cover every \"\n                \"row of one work.\", \"\", \"engine/sources.py (no DOI uniqueness); in-progress ADR-036\"),\n    \"987\": (A, \"P1 INTEGRITY: `protocol add --doc-digest` accepts any 64-hex string and nothing recomputes it \"\n                \"(engine/cli.py:157,492); hash the document and verify it.\", \"\", \"engine/cli.py:157,492\"),\n    \"979\": (A, \"P1 INTEGRITY: binding() covers the command, controls, engine code and inputs, but not the kill script, \"\n                \"expect_exit or timeout, so a test can change after its verdict.\", \"\", \"engine/evidence.py:37\"),\n    \"975\": (A, \"P2: no preview digest exists; `cascade preview` does not bind what `cascade` then executes, so the graph can \"\n                \"change between review and action.\", \"\", \"engine/cascade.py\"),\n    \"982\": (A, \"P2: cascade/retract applies the full transitive set with no volume guard; a mistaken invalidation can \"\n                \"retire most of a program in one command.\", \"\", \"engine/cascade.py\"),\n    \"981\": (A, \"P3: append-only tables are ordinary rows with no hash chain or anchor, so deleting the newest events \"\n                \"goes unnoticed.\", \"\", \"engine/events.py\"),\n    \"990\": (A, \"P3: no family-wise correction exists; the uncorrected-test warning disappears once comparisons are run \"\n                \"separately. Holm is small and standard-library.\", \"\", \"engine/analysis.py, engine/stats.py\"),\n    \"988\": (A, \"P3: observation_summary reports n/min/max/mean only, and variance can overflow on extreme finite values; \"\n                \"add robust statistics and scaling, never auto-trim.\", \"\", \"engine/analysis.py:428\"),\n    \"989\": (A, \"P3: contradiction proposals drop negation as a stopword, so paraphrases can outrank real contradictions; \"\n                \"keep a polarity bit. Advisory output only.\", \"\", \"engine/analysis.py keywords\"),\n    \"977\": (A, \"P3: GRAPH-001 checks dependency cycles but not supports/extends cycles, so two claims can corroborate \"\n                \"each other.\", \"\", \"engine/integrity.py:364\"),\n    \"978\": (A, \"P3: consensus is a support-minus-contradiction score with no coverage fraction or single-source warning; \"\n                \"check overlap with the in-progress calibration work (T-015) first.\", \"\", \"engine/synthesis.py\"),\n    \"986\": (A, \"P4: hypotheses are pre-registered but the comparison is not, so the analysis can be chosen after the data; \"\n                \"register the plan and mark unmatched runs exploratory.\", \"\", \"engine/hypotheses.py, engine/analysis.py\"),\n    \"993\": (A, \"P4: hypothesis and protocol edits leave no amendment trail; an append-only amendment ledger keeps the \"\n                \"original registration visible.\", \"\", \"engine/hypotheses.py, engine/protocols.py\"),\n    \"984\": (A, \"P4: 20+ finding codes are emitted but tests/test_docs.py checks only a few; a registry keeps code, docs \"\n                \"and severity in one place.\", \"\", \"engine/integrity.py; tests/test_docs.py\"),\n    \"974\": (A, \"P4: a moved evidence folder turns every NUMERIC claim stale at once; report one missing-volume finding \"\n                \"instead.\", \"\", \"engine/evidence.py inputs_sha256\"),\n    \"991\": (A, \"P4: `db backup` exists but there is no verified restore; a backup without a tested restore path is a copy.\",\n            \"\", \"engine/maintenance.py\"),\n    \"973\": (D, \"Deferred: bundle.verify_export already applies a semantic projection; verify which record checks are \"\n                \"missing before building more.\"),\n    \"983\": (D, \"Deferred: valuable to prove read-only commands; revisit after IDEA-981's ledger, which it complements.\"),\n    \"971\": (D, \"Deferred with IDEA-986: analysis records follow from registered plans.\"),\n    \"985\": (D, \"Deferred: single-researcher use today; revisit when two reviewers screen the same sources (actor still defaults to 'agent').\"),\n    \"972\": (D, \"Deferred: pooled effects across claims are a feature request, not a defect; revisit with a multi-study program.\"),\n    \"976\": (D, \"Deferred: convenience import; revisit when users register many sources by hand.\"),\n    \"992\": (D, \"Deferred: outline, brief and claim context each have budgets; revisit if agents overflow by calling all three.\"),\n    \"964\": (D, \"Partly in progress: task T-015 adds calibration scoring (ADR-037); revisit the hash-chained forecast ledger after it lands.\"),\n    \"952\": (D, \"Deferred: verify how a non-significant test is labelled today; adopt if it can become a negative claim.\"),\n    \"695\": (D, \"Partly in progress: ADR-036 detects split sources; revisit transitive independence groups after IDEA-980.\"),\n    \"741\": (D, \"Partly covered by engine/duplicates.py and in-progress ADR-036; revisit for equivalence classes.\"),\n    \"742\": (D, \"Partly covered by bundle export; revisit when a second export format is requested.\"),\n    \"818\": (R, \"Already implemented: verdicts are not binary (UNKNOWN, UNFALSIFIABLE and FALSIFIED exist alongside SUPPORTED).\"),\n    \"810\": (R, \"Already covered: the engine reports unknown and unfalsifiable outcomes explicitly instead of forcing an answer.\"),\n    \"697\": (R, NOLLM), \"808\": (R, NOLLM), \"809\": (R, NOLLM), \"811\": (R, NOLLM), \"812\": (R, NOLLM),\n    \"740\": (R, \"Rejected: no consumer. The engine is a set of commands over one database, not a plugin pipeline.\"),\n    \"694\": (D, MODEL), \"696\": (D, MODEL), \"698\": (D, MODEL), \"738\": (D, MODEL), \"739\": (D, MODEL),\n    \"819\": (D, MODEL), \"820\": (D, MODEL), \"821\": (D, MODEL), \"822\": (D, MODEL), \"951\": (D, MODEL),\n    \"918\": (D, MODEL), \"919\": (D, MODEL), \"920\": (D, MODEL), \"921\": (D, MODEL), \"922\": (D, MODEL),\n}\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01VkrbFzW7aaA9Z9fChNGfJD","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd \"C:/Users/Yunus-Emre/Desktop/portable_agent_kit/projects/research-engine\"; git grep -n -i -E \"UNFALSIFIABLE|UNKNOWN|FALSIFIED\" -- engine/models.py | head -4; git grep -n -i \"def backup\\|db backup\\|'backup'\" -- engine | head -3; cd ../..; S=\"C:/Users/YUNUS-~1/AppData/Local/Temp/claude/c--Users-Yunus-Emre-Desktop-portable-agent-kit/05aa96e5-db7a-4aed-bad4-f0f3cebd2787/scratchpad\"; python \"$S/apply_verdicts.py\" \"$S/v_research-engine.py\"","description":"Verify verdict-label and backup claims, dry-run verdicts"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
