MAC-SHA256 of the format-2 signature domain and the canonical payload, keyed by the\naegean_licensing/cert.py:111:    payload = _SIGNATURE_DOMAIN + compute_canonical_payload(data)\r\naegean_licensing/cert.py:112:    return hmac.new(secret_key.encode(\"utf-8\"), payload, hashlib.sha256).hexdigest()\r\naegean_licensing/cli.py:81:    for reason in result.reasons:\naegean_licensing/cli.py:82:        print(f\"  - {reason}\")\naegean_licensing/fingerprint.py:14:    allowed_algorithms: tuple = (\"sha256\", \"hmac-sha256\")\naegean_licensing/fingerprint.py:21:    \"format-2\", \"serial-64-hex\", \"type-checks-before-canonicalization\",","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"ae038317-3baa-4b0c-b43d-f2ff2a3c7906","timestamp":"2026-10-30T12:35:58.505Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"## aegean_licensing/cert.py: License Certificate Data Model and Cryptographic Hashing.\n## aegean_licensing/register.py: Public certificate register: which certificates AegeanWorks issued, and which it revoked (ADR-013).  HMAC signatures can be checked only with the signing key, so publishing that key would let anyone forge a certificate. The register is the public proof instead\n## aegean_licensing/verifier.py: Commercial License Certificate Verification Module.\n## aegean_licensing/fingerprint.py: A stable identity for the rules a verification result was produced under.\n## aegean_licensing/bounded_json.py: Bounded JSON loading for files that cross an untrusted boundary.  A certificate, register or license registry can be large, deeply nested or malformed. The schema checks are too late if reading or parsing the file already exhausts memory. This module applies a\naegean_licensing/cert.py:7:import hmac\r\naegean_licensing/cert.py:63:def _canonical_value(value: Any) -> Any:\r\naegean_licensing/cert.py:82:        return [_canonical_value(item) for item in value]\r\naegean_licensing/cert.py:86:        return {key: _canonical_value(item) for key, item in value.items()}\r\naegean_licensing/cert.py:90:def compute_ca