{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"05aa96e5-db7a-4aed-bad4-f0f3cebd2787","hash":"92c684c6002e9bc0fa416af15565b51043ad3ed9edbfdb8a51e3f309fe9b80c1","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"I've reviewed all 418 new ideas across 7 projects, each against its project's actual code, and recorded them in the register (it validates). 35 are approved, 319 deferred with a revisit condition, 44 rejected, and 20 merged as duplicates. No code was changed.\n\n| Project | New | Approved | Deferred | Rejected | Merged |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| merklock | 123 | 7 | 106 | 7 | 3 |\n| modelduck | 106 | 4 | 95 | 2 | 5 |\n| research-engine | 51 | 16 | 27 | 8 | 0 |\n| neurocore | 42 | 3 | 29 | 8 | 2 |\n| aikit | 35 | 1 | 20 | 8 | 6 |\n| aegean-licensing-ops | 33 | 2 | 21 | 8 | 2 |\n| aegean-licensing | 28 | 2 | 21 | 3 | 2 |\n\n**The most serious problems I found in the code:**\n- **Modelduck: any website can use your local API.** It can be when CORS is on: the settings allow LAN or CORS with authentication off, and CORS allows every origin. A web page open in your browser can then chat with your models or delete them (1054, P1).\n- **Modelduck: chats silently disappear.** Above 200 conversations, the oldest-inserted are dropped when loading or creating, with no warning, and that can include one you used yesterday (1047, P1).\n- **Neurocore: strangers can drive your agent.** The Telegram, Signal and WhatsApp bridges answer anyone who messages the bot, using its tools, memory and your LLM quota. I've added this to neurocore's known-bugs list (839, P2).\n- **Merklock: lost blocks and unsafe peer connections.** Two commands running at once can overwrite each other's block or pending transaction in `chain.json`. A hostile peer can also make a node connect to services on your own machine or local network (1005, 1006, P1).\n- **Research-engine: evidence integrity gaps.** A retracted source can come back through a duplicate entry. Protocol document digests are accepted without being checked. A kill test's script, expected exit code and timeout aren't part of what its verdict is bound to (980, 987, 979, P1).\n- **Licensing-ops: erasure is incomplete.** A KVKK erasure can leave the person's details in leftover database pages and in older backups (928, P2).\n- **Licensing: verifiers can trust outdated revocations.** The public register ships inside the package, so an installed verifier keeps using an old revocation list with no warning that it's stale (935).\n- **AIKit: reforge review packets aren't marked as untrusted.** Reforge can audit any repository, and the agent reading the packet isn't told that the code in it is data, so a hostile commit could address the reviewer directly (909, P2).\n\n**How I decided:**\n- **Approved** only when I confirmed the problem in the current code. For merklock and modelduck, a few claims I couldn't confirm are deferred with \"verify first\" rather than approved.\n- **Deferred** features and research directions: merklock's cryptography and networking, modelduck's product features, research-engine's argumentation and GRADE models. Each has its own revisit condition.\n- **Rejected** ideas whose premise doesn't fit the project:\n  - an LLM loop for research-engine, which makes no model calls;\n  - multi-tenant or seat licensing for single-operator tools;\n  - entity-graph tooling for neurocore memory, which has no entity graph;\n  - tools that need asymmetric signatures where a project is deliberately standard-library only. Those are deferred rather than rejected, in case that rule changes.\n- I also checked ideas against what another agent has in progress. In research-engine, the uncommitted calibration and split-source work partly covers two ideas, and their verdicts say so.\n\n**Other agents are active.** Research-engine has an uncommitted task in progress, and modelduck had commits minutes before I looked, so I only recorded verdicts there.\n\n**Left over:** 53 older Proposed ideas, all from before this batch and for other targets, weren't in scope. Nothing is committed: the register is git-ignored, and the neurocore `docs/IDEAS.md` note is uncommitted. Tell me which approved fixes to start on; modelduck's open CORS and neurocore's open bridges are the most urgent."}]}}
