{"parentUuid":"1753999f-582c-4e49-b9fe-ed20c47ba988","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgYbR1nUV151NqsXKHQs7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011e9KCrpMrWxQFfMbtDNKmm","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"tail -c 200 .aikit/decisions.md | tail -2; cat >> .aikit/decisions.md <<'EOF'\n\n### ADR-018: Refuse cross-site and rebound requests; exposure needs authentication\n- **Date**: 2026-10-30\n- **Status**: Accepted\n- **Context**: IDEA-1054. A live probe showed that with Enable CORS on, any web page in the host's browser could read server settings and mint a readable API key even with Require Authentication on, because `/api/*` trusts loopback sockets and CORS applied to every route. LAN mode skipped the Origin and Host checks, so cross-site text/plain POSTs and DNS-rebound pages reached `/api/*`. Settings accepted LAN or CORS with authentication off.\n- **Decision**: `isCrossSiteRequest` refuses any request whose Origin differs from its Host (`403 cross_site_refused`), except `/v1/*` while CORS is on; CORS headers and preflight apply to `/v1/*` only. A loopback socket must always name a loopback Host; only LAN mode admits other machines. `ServerSettingsStore.update` refuses LAN or CORS without Require Authentication (`400 auth_required_for_exposure`), and `load` switches such a saved file's LAN and CORS off with a warning and saves it.\n- **Consequences**: The same-origin UI (loopback or LAN) and Origin-less API clients are unchanged. Local pages on another port can no longer call ModelDuck unless CORS is on with a key. Contract change: the tests `server settings clamp values...` and `CORS preflight is answered only when enabled` now enable authentication alongside CORS, because CORS without it is no longer a valid setting.\nEOF\ncd ../.. && python aikit.py check modelduck 2>&1 | tail -15","description":"Append ADR-018 and run the project's Phase 4 gate","timeout":600000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":713,"cache_read_input_tokens":129015,"output_tokens":774,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":25},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":713,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":774,"cache_read_input_tokens":129015,"cache_creation_input_tokens":713,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":713},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_011e9KCrpMrWxQFfMbtDNKmm":{"command":"tail -c 200 .aikit/decisions.md | tail -2; cat >> .aikit/decisions.md <<'EOF'\n\n### ADR-018: Refuse cross-site and rebound requests; exposure needs authentication\n- **Date**: 2026-10-30\n- **Status**: Accepted\n- **Context**: IDEA-1054. A live probe showed that with Enable CORS on, any web page in the host's browser could read server settings and mint a readable API key even with Require Authentication on, because `/api/*` trusts loopback sockets and CORS applied to every route. LAN mode skipped the Origin and Host checks, so cross-site text/plain POSTs and DNS-rebound pages reached `/api/*`. Settings accepted LAN or CORS with authentication off.\n- **Decision**: `isCrossSiteRequest` refuses any request whose Origin differs from its Host (`403 cross_site_refused`), except `/v1/*` while CORS is on; CORS headers and preflight apply to `/v1/*` only. A loopback socket must always name a loopback Host; only LAN mode admits other machines. `ServerSettingsStore.update` refuses LAN or CORS without Require Authentication (`400 auth_required_for_exposure`), and `load` switches such a saved file's LAN and CORS off with a warning and saves it.\n- **Consequences**: The same-origin UI (loopback or LAN) and Origin-less API clients are unchanged. Local pages on another port can no longer call ModelDuck unless CORS is on with a key. Contract change: the tests `server settings clamp values...` and `CORS preflight is answered only when enabled` now enable authentication alongside CORS, because CORS without it is no longer a valid setting.\nEOF\ncd ../.. && python aikit.py check modelduck 2>&1 | tail -15","description":"Append ADR-018 and run the project's Phase 4 gate","timeout":600000}},"serverClassifierRequest":"d78547d8-24bd-4100-a186-63ba97e01633","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgYbR1MBXVZHJHoHaAcnv","requestRef":"1caae3a5-3a4c-48a9-bf17-ecb6308f5a09","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"1bb11dbd-baf4-4fb0-9da7-68268d33a247","timestamp":"2026-10-30T14:39:42.433Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"C:\\Users\\Yunus-Emre\\Desktop\\portable_agent_kit\\projects\\modelduck","sessionId":"05aa96e5-db7a-4aed-bad4-f0f3cebd2787","version":"2.1.312","gitBranch":"main","slug":"hidden-watching-bengio"}
