{"parentUuid":"e9025b25-0be3-429a-9edf-7ba1b939b122","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgYbUmdHntNgnLhHcxabp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've fixed 1054: a website can no longer use ModelDuck through your browser. All 92 tests and the project's 4 gates pass, and my original attack probe now gets refused every time. Nothing is committed yet.\n\n| Attack | Before | After |\n|---|---|---|\n| Another website reads settings or creates an API key (CORS on, auth on) | 200 / 201, key readable | **403** |\n| Another website sends a plain-text request in LAN mode | 201, chat created | **403**, no chat |\n| Saving LAN or CORS with auth off | 200 | **400**, with an explanation and fix |\n| A DNS-rebinding page (found while fixing) | got through | **403** |\n\nThe rebinding case was a gap I found during the fix: a site whose own hostname points at your computer counts as \"the same website\", so the first fix alone didn't catch it.\n\n**What changed:**\n- **Other websites are refused** on every route, with one exception: `/v1` when CORS is on, and that still needs an API key. CORS no longer applies to `/api`.\n- **Requests from your own computer must use a local address**, such as `localhost` or `127.0.0.1`, even in LAN mode. That blocks rebinding. Only LAN mode lets other machines connect; CORS alone no longer does.\n- **LAN and CORS require authentication.** Saving them with auth off is refused. A saved file that already has them on with auth off gets both switched off at startup, with a warning (the default I proposed).\n- **Smaller pieces:**\n  - The settings screen explains the new rule.\n  - The README is updated.\n  - I added a decision record (ADR-018).\n  - I added 7 tests and saw each fail before the fix.\n\n**Behaviour you may notice:**\n- Two existing tests turned on CORS without authentication. That setting is no longer allowed, so they now turn authentication on as well. ADR-018 names both.\n- A page on your own computer running on a different port, such as a dev server on `localhost:3000`, can't call ModelDuck anymore unless CORS is on and it sends an API key.\n\n`python aikit.py check modelduck` reports the work as not ready to deliver for two reasons: the changes are uncommitted, and the settings screen changed, so its UI task needs closing.\n\nIn the register, 1054 is now marked Integrating. 967 is corrected and raised to P1: the scan uses node-llama-cpp's JavaScript parser, and a planted file crashes the app at every launch.\n\nSay **commit** to commit this fix, or **continue** to start on 967."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":595,"cache_read_input_tokens":136077,"output_tokens":981,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":147},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":595,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":981,"cache_read_input_tokens":136077,"cache_creation_input_tokens":595,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":595},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"6b22adbb-ffc5-4025-b37e-a3a2cd537145","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgYbUmDEHiF2W2g1Go7qh","requestRef":"ec02810c-45a6-4181-a6f3-79158e29a9a5","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"5f565e10-ad34-4816-9230-e18e99415941","timestamp":"2026-10-30T14:40:36.748Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"C:\\Users\\Yunus-Emre\\Desktop\\portable_agent_kit","sessionId":"05aa96e5-db7a-4aed-bad4-f0f3cebd2787","version":"2.1.312","gitBranch":"main","