{"parentUuid":"50c1c02b-5d20-47af-b764-a9147f9a3593","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgYc5odp1jzuqM52xpmEs","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I rechecked all 96 deferred modelduck ideas against the current code and changed 13 verdicts. The rest stay deferred. One new problem is serious: clicking Download twice corrupts the model file.\n\n**Newly approved (3):**\n\n| Idea | Problem | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|\n| **882 (P1, corrupted files)** | Clicking Download twice for the same model starts two jobs that write into the same partial file. The finished `.gguf` is **twice the catalog size** and is marked complete. Nothing blocks a second click on the button. | I tested it on the code: [src/downloader.js:46-80](projects/modelduck/src/downloader.js#L46-L80), [public/app.js:1183](projects/modelduck/public/app.js#L1183) |\n| **853 (P3)** | A stalled download has no timeout. It stays at \"downloading\" forever and takes up one of the two download slots. | [src/downloader.js:198-216](projects/modelduck/src/downloader.js#L198-L216) |\n| **903 (P3)** | If the requested context size doesn't fit in memory, the engine quietly retries at 3072, 2048 and then 1024 tokens. The reason only goes to the log, so the app shows a smaller context with no explanation. | [src/engine.js:216-244](projects/modelduck/src/engine.js#L216-L244) |\n\n**Already implemented, so rejected (3):**\n- **1000:** the generation fingerprint the other agent added (`07f0c4d`) already covers it.\n- **858:** the context overflow setting already offers \"shift\" and a \"strict\" mode that refuses with a token count.\n- **1018:** the UI already asks before deleting a model or revoking a key.\n\n**Merged:**\n- **968** (address and origin checks) is now part of 1054, which I fixed in the previous step.\n\n**Still deferred, with updated notes** (partly done since my first review):\n- **1024:** a lock already allows only one instance per data folder.\n- **859:** JSON and JSON-schema output already exist as app settings.\n- **855:** single-model lookup was added.\n- **954:** there's now a Q4 KV cache warning.\n- **1031:** catalog cards show each model's license.\n- **924:** a per-launch token adds little now.\n\n**Still deferred, unchanged (83).** These are product features and performance or benchmark ideas, such as speculative decoding, retrieval, chat branching and device pairing. They have no defect behind them, and their revisit conditions still apply.\n\nThe register validates. Modelduck now has 7 approved fixes, in my order: 967 (one bad file crashes every launch), 882 (double-click corruption), 1047 (lost chats), 862 (unverified downloads), 853 and 903. 1054 is written but not committed.\n\nSay **commit** to commit 1054, or **continue** to start on 967 and 882."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2358,"cache_read_input_tokens":157765,"output_tokens":985,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":38},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2358,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":985,"cache_read_input_tokens":157765,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2358,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2358},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"885d7405-46b1-4a74-ace3-e1508c1f8975","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgYc5o93yybBFxjQFzV5t","requestRef":"5c954b3a-b39c-46f6-85a1-ba3e4f51754b","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"b6eaa412-175d-4a3c-8c9b-a32bf8f38246","timestamp":"2026-10-30T14:48:31.854Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnE