adata entries never returns, so one planted `.gguf` would crash every launch. Separately, `DownloadManager.start` accepted a second job for a model already downloading; both appended to one `.part` file and a double-size file was promoted as complete.","+- **Decision**: `src/gguf-guard.js` walks the v2/v3 header with buffered reads before the parser runs, refusing any count or length larger than the remaining file, unknown value types, nested arrays, tensors outside 1-4 dimensions and offsets past the end (`422 gguf_header_rejected`). The registry lists such files as `blocked` with the reason; the engine refuses to load them and import deletes the copy and refuses. `start` returns the existing active job for the same catalog id, and the UI disables the Download button during its request.","+- **Consequences**: The guard costs about as much as the metadata parse it precedes (107 ms for a 151k-token vocabulary) and runs only on a scan-cache miss; four real GGUF models (Qwen2.5, nomic-embed, moondream2 text and projector) pass it. Arrays of arrays are refused, matching every known GGUF writer. A repeated download request is idempotent instead of corrupting the model."]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["C:\\Users\\Yunus-Emre\\Desktop\\portable_agent_kit\\projects\\modelduck\\.aikit\\decisions.md"]}},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"e09afcfd-2db1-4572-a721-a0289d5021e2","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/c/Users/Yunus-Emre/Desktop/portable_agent_kit/projects/modelduck","root":"/c/Users/Yunus-Emre/Desktop/portable_agent_kit/projects/modelduck","branch":"master","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":13,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":2},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":null,"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"AegeanWorks/AIKit","visibility":"public"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"AegeanWorks/NeuroCore","visibility":"public"},{"host":"github.com","rem