{"parentUuid":"501aa76f-1736-434a-8480-81bbb82f1a59","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgYcmg3GzBPQPAWLm1spU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've fixed 967 and 882. A bad model file can no longer crash ModelDuck, and double-clicking Download no longer corrupts a model. All 96 tests and the project's 4 gates pass, and nothing is committed yet.\n\n**967: a bad model file crashed the app at every start**\n- **Fix:** before the model parser runs, a new check reads the file's header and refuses any count or length that couldn't fit in the file ([src/gguf-guard.js](projects/modelduck/src/gguf-guard.js)).\n- **What happens to a refused file:**\n  - It shows as **Blocked** in the model list, with the reason.\n  - It can't be loaded.\n  - Importing it is refused, and the copied file is removed.\n- **Tested:**\n  - I started the real app with a planted 64-byte file claiming 2^62 tensors. Before the fix this crashed the app at startup. Now it starts normally and lists the file as Blocked.\n  - I ran the check on 4 real models on this machine, including Qwen2.5 1.5B with its 151k-word vocabulary. All 4 pass, and the check takes about as long as the existing metadata read, around 100 ms at most, only when a file is new or has changed.\n  - The tests cover ten kinds of malformed header.\n\n**882: double-clicking Download corrupted the model**\n- **Fix:**\n  - Asking for a model that's already downloading now returns the running download instead of starting a second one ([src/downloader.js](projects/modelduck/src/downloader.js)).\n  - The Download button is disabled while its request runs, and the UI no longer lists the same download twice.\n- **Tested:** I re-ran the earlier test that produced a file twice the expected size; the file now comes out at exactly the catalog size. The new test fails without the fix and passes with it.\n\nThe README and a new decision record (ADR-019) are updated, and both ideas are marked Integrating in the register.\n\n**Waiting for your commit:** 1054 (ADR-018), and 967 and 882 (ADR-019). I'd commit them as two separate commits.\n\n**Still approved and not started:** 1047 (lost chats), 862 (unverified downloads), 853 (stalled downloads), 903 (quietly reduced context).\n\nSay **commit** to commit both fixes, or **continue** to start on 1047."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1060,"cache_read_input_tokens":196324,"output_tokens":762,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1060,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":762,"cache_read_input_tokens":196324,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1060,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1060},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"d90b3e58-c526-437e-a0f5-ff28504ce13a","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgYcmfYknyJhBEYZdqGAV","requestRef":"0f013d99-ce11-4278-81da-83716a6df92a","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"2f49d0e9-e3e9-47f6-9257-27af25e3ea90","timestamp":"2026-10-30T14:57:30.071Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"C:\\Users\\Yunus-Emre\\Desktop\\portable_agent_kit","sessionId":"05aa96e5-db7a-4aed-bad4-f0f3cebd2787","version":"2.1.312","gitBranch":"main","slug":"hidden-watching-bengio"}
