{"parentUuid":"68feb553-0d2e-45b7-a367-4e4719df1732","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgYd1TzN3pfJJtqvR1R69","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01RkkF2Ja6NpV1gxi8k5pT28","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python - <<'EOF'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np = Path(\"README.md\"); s = p.read_bytes().decode(\"utf-8\")\nnl = \"\\r\\n\" if \"\\r\\n\" in s else \"\\n\"\nold = \"| Chats | `~/.modelduck/chats.json` | `--home <folder>` |\"\nnew = \"| Chats | `~/.modelduck/chats.json` (200 most recently used) and `chats.archive.json` (older chats, restored when opened; never dropped) | `--home <folder>` |\"\nassert s.count(old) == 1\np.write_bytes(s.replace(old, new).encode(\"utf-8\"))\nEOF\ncat >> .aikit/decisions.md <<'EOF'\n\n### ADR-020: Archive chats past the limit instead of dropping them\n- **Date**: 2026-10-30\n- **Status**: Accepted\n- **Context**: IDEA-1047. `ChatStore` capped conversations at 200 by insertion order on load (`slice`) and on create (`length = 200`). A live probe showed chat 201 deleting the oldest-created chat even when it was used that day, and loading a 250-chat file dropping 50, including the most recently used. The cap exists because `chats.json` is rewritten on every message.\n- **Decision**: Keep the 200 most recently used chats in `chats.json` and move the rest to `chats.archive.json`, which is written only when the archive changes and always before `chats.json`; on load a chat found in both files keeps its active copy. `restore(id)` moves an archived chat back (counting as used now) and archives the next least recent. `GET /api/conversations` adds `archived`, `/api/state` adds `archivedConversations`, opening an archived chat restores it, and delete reaches archived chats. The sidebar lists them under an Archived group, searchable like the rest.\n- **Consequences**: No chat is lost to the cap and the per-message write stays bounded. The archive grows with history and is loaded into memory at startup; a very large archive would call for paging (out of scope). An interrupted save can at worst duplicate a chat, which load removes.\nEOF\nnpm test 2>&1 | grep -E \"^ℹ (pass|fail)\"; cd ../.. && python aikit.py check modelduck 2>&1 | grep -E \"FAIL|gates passed\"","description":"Update README and ADR, run tests and the gate","timeout":600000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":280,"cache_read_input_tokens":221793,"output_tokens":875,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":280,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":875,"cache_read_input_tokens":221793,"cache_creation_input_tokens":280,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":280},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01RkkF2Ja6NpV1gxi8k5pT28":{"command":"python - <<'EOF'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np = Path(\"README.md\"); s = p.read_bytes().decode(\"utf-8\")\nnl = \"\\r\\n\" if \"\\r\\n\" in s else \"\\n\"\nold = \"| Chats | `~/.modelduck/chats.json` | `--home <folder>` |\"\nnew = \"| Chats | `~/.modelduck/chats.json` (200 most recently used) and `chats.archive.json` (older chats, restored when opened; never dropped) | `--home <folder>` |\"\nassert s.count(old) == 1\np.write_bytes(s.replace(old, new).encode(\"utf-8\"))\nEOF\ncat >> .aikit/decisions.md <<'EOF'\n\n### ADR-020: Archive chats past the limit instead of dropping them\n- **Date**: 2026-10-30\n- **Status**: Accepted\n- **Context**: IDEA-1047. `ChatStore` capped conversations at 200 by insertion order on load (`slice`) and on create (`length = 200`). A live probe showed chat 201 deleting the oldest-created chat even when it was used that day, and loading a 250-chat file dropping 50, including the most recently used. The cap exists because `chats.json` is rewritten on every message.\n- **Decision**: Keep the 200 most recently used chats in `chats.json` and move the rest to `chats.archive.json`, which is written only when the archive changes and always before `chats.json`; on load a chat found in both files keeps its active copy. `restore(id)` moves an archived chat back (counting as used now) and archives the next least recent. `GET /api/conversations` adds `archived`, `/api/state` adds `archivedConversations`, opening an archived chat restores it, and delete reaches archived chats. The sidebar lists them under an Archived group, searchable like the rest.\n- **Consequences**: No chat is lost to the cap and the per-message write stays bounded. The archive grows with history and is loaded into memory at startup; a very large archive would call for paging (out of scope). An interrupted save can at worst duplicate a chat, which load removes.\nEOF\nnpm test 2>&1 | grep -E \"^ℹ (pass|fail)\"; cd ../.. && python aikit.py check modelduck 2>&1 | grep -E \"FAIL|gates passed\"","description":"Update README and ADR, run tests and the gate","timeout":600000}},"serverClassifierRequest":"a3127de2-e26f-4fc5-bba2-59f3a53af206","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgYd1TXLfWdDMFdDags46","requestRef":"f817dbd2-1557-405b-a797-5e5c26c0d8fe","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"dcbca812-9600-43c4-9c29-ef4e537f581a","timestamp":"2026-10-30T15:00:37.735Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"C:\\Users\\Yunus-Emre\\Desktop\\portable_agent_kit\\projects\\modelduck","sessionId":"05aa96e5-db7a-4aed-bad4-f0f3cebd2787","version":"2.1.312","gitBranch":"main","slug":"hidden-watching-bengio"}
{"parentUuid":"dcbca812-9600-43c4-9c29-ef4e537f581a","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"2a56c922-1680-4d82-9036-cc1b505d17af","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RkkF2Ja6NpV1gxi8k5pT28","type":"tool_result","content":"ℹ pass 101\nℹ fail 0\n4/4 gates passed for 'modelduck'","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"48724b3e-1bd6-493c-9965-5a2625789394","timestamp":"2026-10-30T15:00:46.298Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"ℹ pass 101\nℹ fail 0\n4/4 gates passed for 'modelduck'","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\Yunus-Emre\\Desktop\\portable_agent_kit\\projects\\modelduck\\.aikit\\decisions.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":147,"oldLines":3,"newStart":147,"newLines":10,"lines":[" - **Context**: IDEA-967 and IDEA-882. A live probe showed that node-llama-cpp 3.22.2's `readGgufFileInfo`, which every scan runs (including at startup), trusts header counts: a 100-byte file claiming 2^62 tensors exhausts the heap and one claiming 2^62 metadata entries never returns, so one planted `.gguf` would crash every launch. Separately, `DownloadManager.start` accepted a second job for a model already downloading; both appended to one `.part` file and a double-size file was promoted as complete."," - **Decision**: `src/gguf-guard.js` walks the v2/v3 header with buffered reads before the parser runs, refusing any count or length larger than the remaining file, unknown value types, nested arrays, tensors outside 1-4 dimensions and offsets past the end (`422 gguf_header_rejected`). The registry lists such files as `blocked` with the reason; the engine refuses to load them and import deletes the copy and refuses. `start` returns the existing active job for the same catalog id, and the UI disables the Download button during its request."," - **Consequences**: The guard costs about as much as the metadata parse it precedes (107 ms for a 151k-token vocabulary) and runs only on a scan-cache miss; four real GGUF models (Qwen2.5, nomic-embed, moondream2 text and projector) pass it. Arrays of arrays are refused, matching every known GGUF writer. A repeated download request is idempotent instead of corrupting the model.","+","+### ADR-020: Archive chats past the limit instead of dropping them","+- **Date**: 2026-10-30","+- **Status**: Accepted","+- **Context**: IDEA-1047. `ChatStore` capped conversations at 200 by insertion order on load (`slice`) and on create (`length = 200`). A live probe showed chat 201 deleting the oldest-created chat even when it was used that day, and loading a 250-chat file dropping 50, including the most recently used. The cap exists because `chats.json` is rewritten on every message.","+- **Decision**: Keep the 200 most recently used chats in `chats.json` and move the rest to `chats.archive.json`, which is written only when the archive changes and always before `chats.json`; on load a chat found in both files keeps its active copy. `restore(id)` moves an archived chat back (counting as used now) and archives the next least recent. `GET /api/conversations` adds `archived`, `/api/state` adds `archivedConversations`, opening an archived chat restores it, and delete reaches archived chats. The sidebar lists them under an Archived group, searchable like the rest.","+- **Consequences**: No chat is lost to the cap and the per-message write stays bounded. The archive grows with history and is loaded into memory at startup; a very large archive would call for paging (out of scope). An interrupted save can at worst duplicate a chat, which load removes."]}]},{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\Yunus-Emre\\Desktop\\portable_agent_kit\\projects\\modelduck\\README.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":196,"oldLines":7,"newStart":196,"newLines":7,"lines":[" | Item | Default | Override |\r"," |---|---|---|\r"," | Models | `~/.modelduck/models` | `--models <folder>` |\r","-| Chats | `~/.modelduck/chats.json` | `--home <folder>` |\r","+| Chats | `~/.modelduck/chats.json` (200 most recently used) and `chats.archive.json` (older chats, restored when opened; never dropped) | `--home <folder>` |\r"," | Settings | `~/.modelduck/settings.json` | `--home <folder>` |\r"," | Server settings + key hashes | `~/.modelduck/server-settings.json` | `--home <folder>` |\r"," | Downloads | `~/.modelduck/models/*.part` | `--models <folder>` |"]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["C:\\Users\\Yunus-Emre\\Desktop\\portable_agent_kit\\projects\\modelduck\\.aikit\\decisions.md","C:\\Users\\Yunus-Emre\\Desktop\\portable_agent_kit\\projects\\modelduck\\README.md"]}},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"a3127de2-e26f-4fc5-bba2-59f3a53af206","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/c/Users/Yunus-Emre/Desktop/portable_agent_kit/projects/modelduck","root":"/c/Users/Yunus-Emre/Desktop/portable_agent_kit/projects/modelduck","branch":"master","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":16,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":2},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":null,"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"AegeanWorks/AIKit","visibility":"public"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"AegeanWorks/NeuroCore","visibility":"public"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"AegeanWorks/Research-Engine","visibility":"public"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"AegeanWorks/Aegean-Licensing","visibility":"public"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"AegeanWorks/Aegean-Licensing-Ops","visibility":"private"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"AegeanWorks/Merklock","visibility":"private"}]}},"live_cwd":"/c/Users/Yunus-Emre/Desktop/portable_agent_kit/projects/modelduck","platform":"windows"}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"dcbca812-9600-43c4-9c29-ef4e537f581a","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"C:\\Users\\Yunus-Emre\\Desktop\\portable_agent_kit","sessionId":"05aa96e5-db7a-4aed-bad4-f0f3cebd2787","ver