{"parentUuid":"4699c72f-eac3-4a31-915d-ae175514e78e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgYd3PKdc3T7TQanXRarX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've fixed 1047: chats past 200 are now archived instead of deleted. All 101 tests and the project's 4 gates pass, and the lost-chat test from earlier now keeps both the chat you just used and the newest one. Nothing is committed yet.\n\n**How it works:**\n- **Nothing is deleted.** Past 200 chats, the ones you haven't used for the longest move to a new file, `chats.archive.json`, next to `chats.json`. Before, the oldest-*created* chats were simply deleted, even ones you'd used that day.\n- **Archived chats stay visible.** They appear in the sidebar under an **Archived** heading, and search covers them. Opening one moves it back to the main list, and the next least recently used chat takes its place in the archive. Deleting an archived chat works as usual.\n- **A crash can't lose a chat.** The archive file is saved before the main file. If the app is interrupted between the two, a chat can end up in both files, and the duplicate is removed on the next start.\n- **Saving stays fast.** `chats.json` is rewritten on every message and still holds at most 200 chats. The archive is only rewritten when something moves in or out of it.\n\n**What I didn't check:** I tested this through the code and the server routes, not by clicking through the sidebar in a browser.\n\n**Trade-off:** the whole archive is loaded into memory at startup, which is fine for normal use. A history of many thousands of chats would eventually need the archive to load in pages; ADR-020 records this.\n\n**Waiting for your commit, as three separate commits:**\n- 1054, website access (ADR-018)\n- 967 and 882, blocked model files and duplicate downloads (ADR-019)\n- 1047, chat archive (ADR-020)\n\n**Still approved and not started:**\n- 862: verify downloads against a SHA-256 hash. This needs the real hashes from Hugging Face, so it means going online once.\n- 853: a timeout for stalled downloads.\n- 903: say when the context size was quietly reduced.\n\nSay **commit** to commit these, or **continue** to start on 853 and 903, which need no network. For 862, I'll fetch the five catalog hashes from Hugging Face if you approve going online."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":715,"cache_read_input_tokens":223202,"output_tokens":724,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":715,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":724,"cache_read_input_tokens":223202,"cache_creation_input_tokens":715,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":715},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"e38ba6c3-9c9e-46c2-a2c4-48facdfb4dd4","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgYd3NxJjj8LwhwAGNCtZ","requestRef":"af9db0ac-5cd5-40ec-87c2-71f6d767b4b6","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"9d1db90b-fa01-4d75-a81a-2854921eb83f","timestamp":"2026-10-30T15:01:02.658Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"C:\\Users\\Yunus-Emre\\Desktop\\portable_agent_kit","sessionId":"05aa96e5-db7a-4aed-bad4-f0f3cebd2787","version":"2.1.312","gitBranch":"main","slug":"hidden-watching-bengio"}
