{"parentUuid":"902ccc45-7aae-4a4d-bbcc-8abbf1bf3c7a","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"77902c58-ab0d-45be-9a54-10ce222b753c","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DumKCWqRKRASPuzG7SANqN","type":"tool_result","content":"## What the set implies\n\nThe eight “adopt now” ideas share a property: each one either makes a measurement\ntrustworthy or protects a claim the product already makes. None requires a new model\nor a new inference backend. The four prototypes are deliberately narrow, each with a\nkill criterion. The three defer/reject items are the ones most likely to be proposed\nagain because they demo well; the briefs exist so the decision can be reopened with\nevidence rather than enthusiasm.\n\nIf only three things are built this quarter, build the per-item logging and\n`suiteFingerprint`, the memory-fit card, and prompt/KV caching. They make every later\nquality claim cheaper to defend, prevent the worst support failure, and improve the\nthing users feel on every turn.\n458:## Open decisions\n459-\n460-1. **Prompt storage:** hashes and counts only (recommended), or full prompt text for replay?\n461-   Full text makes replay exact but writes user content to disk; an opt-in debug export is the\n462-   safer default.\n463-2. **Gate behaviour:** should a prompt fingerprint change without a suite bump fail the gate\n464-   (recommended) or only warn? Failing enforces the \"prompt edit is a test edit\" rule; it also\n465-   forces a baseline update on every legitimate prompt improvement.\n466-3. **Presets:** user-editable presets, or only built-in presets? Idea 2 assumes user presets.\n467-4. **HF pull:** is arbitrary Hugging Face acquisition planned? Idea 7 is a dependency, not a\n468-   standalone feature.\n469-5. **MCP:** is MCP in the near-term roadmap? If not, idea 6 is parked.\n470-6. **Metrics surface:** a JSON `/api/metrics` plus a Doctor panel, or keep stats in the UI only?\n471-\n472----","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"2dfdb761-4400-40c0-8139-89bbbf776884","timestamp":"2026-10-30T15:02:56.045Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"## What the set implies\n\nThe eight “adopt now” ideas share a property: each one either makes a measurement\ntrustworthy or protects a claim the product already makes. None requires a new model\nor a new inference backend. The four prototypes are deliberately narrow, each with a\nkill criterion. The three defer/reject items are the ones most likely to be proposed\nagain because they demo well; the briefs exist so the decision can be reopened with\nevidence rather than enthusiasm.\n\nIf only three things are built this quarter, build the per-item logging and\n`suiteFingerprint`, the memory-fit card, and prompt/KV caching. They make every later\nquality claim cheaper to defend, prevent the worst support failure, and improve the\nthing users feel on every turn.\n458:## Open decisions\n459-\n460-1. **Prompt storage:** hashes and counts only (recommended), or full prompt text for replay?\n461-   Full text makes replay exact but writes user content to disk; an opt-in debug export is the\n462-   safer default.\n463-2. **Gate behaviour:** should a prompt fingerprint change without a suite bump fail the gate\n464-   (recommended) or only warn? Failing enforces the \"prompt edit is a test edit\" rule; it also\n465-   forces a baseline update on every legitimate prompt improvement.\n466-3. **Presets:** user-editable presets, or only built-in presets? Idea 2 assumes user presets.\n467-4. **HF pull:** is arbitrary Hugging Face acquisition planned? Idea 7 is a dependency, not a\n468-   standalone feature.\n469-5. **MCP:** is MCP in the near-term roadmap? If not, idea 6 is parked.\n470-6. **Metrics surface:** a JSON `/api/metrics` plus a Doctor panel, or keep stats in the UI only?\n471-\n472----","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"48345903-35a3-4247-b731-0a08de1abf8c","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/c/Users/Y