{"parentUuid":"2dfdb761-4400-40c0-8139-89bbbf776884","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgYdCGYM5cnANU62yXU2L","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1623,"cache_read_input_tokens":243555,"output_tokens":1518,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":26},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1623,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1518,"cache_read_input_tokens":243555,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1623,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1623},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":7471,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"bcaf2fa4-c61b-4be3-8cb6-41c4d2613935","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgYdCFrRnLvpMA5JYPqwu","requestRef":"b87f885d-5fdd-4e1a-ae27-54cbbad3fee5","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"3fab477f-0183-41fb-8918-caccac7ecd6f","timestamp":"2026-10-30T15:03:04.464Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"C:\\Users\\Yunus-Emre\\Desktop\\portable_agent_kit\\projects\\modelduck","sessionId":"05aa96e5-db7a-4aed-bad4-f0f3cebd2787","version":"2.1.312","gitBranch":"main","slug":"hidden-watching-bengio"}
{"parentUuid":"3fab477f-0183-41fb-8918-caccac7ecd6f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgYdCGYM5cnANU62yXU2L","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Your reports agree with the register on most points. The exception is the ModelDuck literature review's top advice: it says to build three things first, and I deferred all three with a stock \"revisit later\" reason, without weighing the evidence the reports collected. I haven't changed anything yet.\n\nThe reports are in `reports/`: the ModelDuck literature review and its idea briefs, a \"what ModelDuck can borrow from neurocore\" report, and a research-engine report. Together with the notes in `research_notes/`, they're about 350 KB. Neither folder is tracked by git yet.\n\n**What the reports say to build first, compared with the code today:**\n\n| Report's priority | In the register | What the code does now |\n|---|---|---|\n| **#1: log every test item, with proper statistics** | 1037, deferred | The benchmark fails a run if the overall score drops by more than 0.01 points ([benchmarks/run.mjs:679](projects/modelduck/benchmarks/run.mjs#L679)). It covers about 14 prompts, with no per-item comparison and no confidence interval. So a single flipped check fails the gate, and a pass doesn't prove there was no regression. |\n| **#2: check whether a model fits in memory, and refuse if not** | 903, approved but narrowed to \"tell the user\" | The engine quietly retries at smaller context sizes. The report wants a memory-fit card plus a refusal. |\n| **#3: reuse the prompt and its cache between turns** | 873, deferred | Chat sessions are now reused (`a56065e`). But the default \"Context overflow: shift\" discards that cache, which the report names as the cost. |\n\n**Where the reports already shaped what we did:**\n\n| Report advice | Status |\n|---|---|\n| Lock the local API down (literature idea 4) | Done today as 1054 |\n| Fingerprint every generation (neurocore report, tier 1) | The other agent built it; 1000 is rejected as already done |\n| Default to a 4K context, with 8-bit KV in the Balanced preset; reject 32K (idea 14) | The code already matches |\n| Don't add autonomous agents (15), small-model draft decoding (13) or Medusa-style multi-token decoding | Rejected or deferred, as the reports advise |\n| The fast \"n-gram\" decoding, retrieval and memory prototypes (9–11) | Deferred, which fits the reports' \"prototype with a clear stop condition\" |\n\n**What the reports flag that I missed:**\n- **The \"Token saver\" preset still uses the 4-bit KV cache** ([src/config.js:61](projects/modelduck/src/config.js#L61)). Both the literature and ModelDuck's own baseline show a large quality drop with it. The preset only carries a warning, and the report recommends 8-bit instead. Changing it would need a benchmark run.\n- **Undisclosed network use (idea 5, \"honest egress ledger\").** ModelDuck calls `getLlama()` with no build option, so node-llama-cpp defaults to building from source when no prebuilt binary fits ([src/engine.js:181](projects/modelduck/src/engine.js#L181)). That build would download llama.cpp from GitHub, which an \"offline, no telemetry\" app should never do silently. This comes from the library's documentation; I haven't triggered it.\n- **Research-engine report:** it recommends tier 1 items 971–976 next. I approved 974 and 975 but deferred 971, 972, 973 and 976. It also says that project's test suite was failing because of a README length limit. Another agent is working there, so I haven't checked whether that's still true.\n\n**What I'd change in the register:**\n- **1037 (per-item benchmark statistics) → approve, P2.** The report ranks it #1, and the code confirms the gate is a raw threshold.\n- **903 → widen** to the full memory-fit check that refuses to load, per the report.\n- **New idea, P2:** set `build: \"never\"` (or ask first) so loading a model can never silently download and compile code.\n- **New idea, P3:** switch the Token saver preset from 4-bit to 8-bit KV cache, gated on a benchmark run.\n- **Keep 873 deferred,** with a note that it's the report's #3 and depends on the shift setting.\n- **Research-engine 971–976:** re-review them against the report once that project's in-progress task is finished.\n\nShould I apply these register changes? Separately, I'd also recommend committing `reports/` and `research_notes/` so the research isn't lost. Today they exist only as untracked files."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1623,"cache_read_input_tokens":243555,"output_tokens":1518,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":26},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1623,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1518,"cache_read_input_tokens":243555,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1623,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1623},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"bcaf2fa4-c61b-4be3-8cb6-41c4d2613935","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgYdCFrRnLvpMA5JYPqwu","requestRef":"b87f885d-5fdd-4e1a-ae27-54cbbad3fee5","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"bba4d5b9-416c-45b8-94b7-f0b8efb5b5dc","timestamp":"2026-10-30T15:03:12.506Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"C:\\Users\\Yunus-Emre\\Desktop\\portable_agent_kit\\projects\\modelduck","sessionId":"05aa96e5-db7a-4aed-bad4-f0f3cebd2787","version":"2.1.312","gitBranch":"main","slug":"hidden-watching-bengio"}
