{"parentUuid":"1e9e7a1c-b289-41c9-8dc4-e3447ece6cac","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"70a75a41-7888-4c77-bc13-5ad4f9e80b7c","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JkT9Noq9XWX5PTrcPGp5K1","type":"tool_result","content":"18\t## Executive summary\n19\t\n20\t1. **Do not port NeuroCore's architecture.** It is a multi-module Python control plane with\n21\t   flows, a brain, memory, messaging and a marketplace. ModelDuck is one Node process and a\n22\t   browser UI. What transfers is a handful of **invariants** that NeuroCore learned to enforce.\n23\t2. **The strongest fit is benchmark integrity.** ModelDuck's `testHash` covers the suite and\n24\t   matrix settings, but not the system prompt, per-variant system prompt, GGUF chat template,\n25\t   or `node-llama-cpp` version. A change there can move quality without the gate noticing.\n26\t   A **generation manifest / prompt fingerprint** closes that gap and reuses the existing\n27\t   `engine.chat` path for both the app and the benchmark.\n28\t3. **Second: versioned prompts and presets with benchmark-gated trust.** NeuroCore records\n29\t   every prompt-material change under its SHA-256, bounds history, and treats rollback as a\n30\t   new version. ModelDuck's presets are hardcoded and nothing records that a preset earned\n31\t   trust. This is a direct extension of the benchmark moat.\n32\t4. **Third: a deterministic pre-flight load plan.** NeuroCore's flow simulator returns\n33\t   blocking/warning findings and a cost envelope without executing anything. ModelDuck silently\n34\t   tries four context sizes and reports a generic OOM. A load plan makes the fallback\n35\t   inspectable and gives the benchmark matrix a shared report shape.\n36\t5. **Fourth: a per-request and JIT-load budget.** One context and one process are deliberate;\n37\t   an API client can still hold the model with a long prompt or thrash JIT loads. NeuroCore's\n38\t   shared allowance, \"lower never raise\" overrides and `pressure` snapshot fit this exactly.\n39\t6. **Later, and only with MCP/RAG:** fence untrusted tool/retrieval text, guard repeated tool\n40\t   calls, and make arbitrary Hugging Face acquisition SSRF-safe. These are prerequisites, not\n41\t   standalone features.\n42\t7. **Do not copy** the brain/self-evolution loop, meta-flows, marketplace, multi-platform\n43\t   messaging, memory evidence graph, actor roles, daily self-modification quotas, or the\n44\t   FAISS/RRF stack. They add surface area ModelDuck deliberately does not want.\n45\t\n46\t---\n47\t\n48\t## What ModelDuck already has\n49\t\n50\tThe table exists to stop the report from re-proposing existing work.\n51\t\n52\t| Area | Current state | NeuroCore analogue | Verdict |\n53\t|---|---|---|---|\n54\t| Prompt stats | Token counts, TTFT, tok/s, stop reason per reply (`src/engine.js:479-490`) | Trace spans, token counters (`core/observability.py`) | Add a prompt manifest |\n55\t| History window | Silent truncation at 40 messages / 48k chars (`src/engine.js:41-57`) | Pinned system prefix with a digest (`modules/agent_loop/prompt_digest.py`) | Expose the truncation |\n56\t| Session reuse | Signature = model id + system prompt + context size + history length (`src/engine.js:521-527`) | System prefix re-hashed before every model call | Hash the content, not the length |\n57\t| Benchmark provenance | `suiteVersion`, `testHash`, matrix settings, app version, git, machine (`benchmarks/run.mjs:422-458,531-568`) | Baseline requires provenance (`modules/brain/improvement.py:378-401`) | Add runtime/template/prompt hashes |\n58\t| Presets | Three hardcoded presets (`src/config.js:48-109`); README claims they earn trust after both phases | Content-addressed versions + eval-gated promotion (`modules/skills/versions.py`, `modules/brain/improvement.py:279-349`) | Version and record trust |\n59\t| Load | Context fallback loop `[wanted, 3072, 2048, 1024]` (`src/engine.js:257-287`) | Deterministic pre-flight with blocking findings (`core/flow_simulation.py`) | Add a load plan |\n60\t| Budget | `maxTokens` and `contextOverflow: strict` (`src/engine.js:429-439`) | Shared execution budget with pressure (`core/execution_budget.py`) | Add wall/JIT budgets |\n61\t| Metrics | Last generation only (`engine.js` state) | Bounded p50/p95/p99 + p99 stall detection (`core/node_stall.py`) | Add a live monitor |\n62\t| Security | Loopback/Host/Origin guard, CSP, 8 MB body cap, SHA-256 API keys (`src/http.js`, `src/server-settings.js`) | Pinned HTTP, untrusted fencing, confirmation phrases | Partial; add the missing pieces |\n63\t| MCP/RAG | Two persisted switches, no tools (`README.md:208`) | Fence + loop guard + tool tiers | Prerequisite work |\n64\t| Downloads | Curated catalog, `.part` resume, size check, `redirect: \"follow\"` (`src/downloader.js:155-163,222-229`) | SSRF-safe pinned fetch + content hash (`core/pinned_http.py`, `core/research_gateway.py`) | Harden with HF pull |\n65\t\n66\t---\n67\t\n68\t## Tier 1 — do first\n69\t\n70\t### 1. Generation manifest and prompt fingerprint\n71\t\n72\t**What NeuroCore does.** `modules/agent_loop/prompt_digest.py` snapshots the leading system\n73\tmessages when a loop starts, hashes their contents, verifies them before every model call,\n74\trestores the pinned prefix if compaction or truncation changed it, and records\n75\t`integrity_violation` in the iteration trace (`modules/agent_loop/node.py:720-722`). The point\n76\tis not display: the governing prompt is treated as a value that must survive every rewrite.\n77\t`core/observability.py` adds trace IDs, spans, token counters and a JSONL trace sink.\n78\t\n79\t**Why it fits ModelDuck.** The benchmark gate is ModelDuck's moat, but its `testHash` is\n80\tcomputed from `SUITE_VERSION`, the prompts, and the matrix settings (`benchmarks/run.mjs:422-458`).\n81\tIt does not include:\n82\t\n83\t- the global `SYSTEM_PROMPT` (`benchmarks/run.mjs:26-28,551`) or a per-variant `systemPrompt`\n84\t  (`run.mjs:254,353`);\n85\t- the GGUF chat template — the registry only stores a boolean\n86\t  (`src/model-registry.js:124`), not the template text;\n87\t- the `node-llama-cpp` version (`package.json:23`);\n88\t- the exact history after truncation (`src/engine.js:41-57`).\n89\t\n90\tAny of those can change the tokens the model sees while the suite version and test hash stay\n91\tthe same. The gate then attributes a quality delta to the wrong parameter. The same gap exists\n92\toutside the benchmark: a reply's `stats` do not say which prompt produced it.\n93\t\n94\t**What to add.**\n95\t\n96\t- `src/prompt-manifest.js`, pure and dependency-free:\n97\t  - `sha256Hex(value)` over canonical JSON.\n98\t  - `historyWindow(messages)` returns `{ messages, droppedMessages, droppedChars, truncated }`\n99\t    and becomes the single truncation implementation used by `engine.js`.\n100\t  - `fingerprintPrompt({ systemPrompt, history, templateText, settings })` returns\n101\t    `{ promptDigest, systemPromptDigest, historyDigest, templateDigest, chars, messages }`.\n102\t- `engine.chat` attaches a `manifest` to `stats`:\n103\t  - model `{ id, fileName, size, modifiedAt }`;\n104\t  - runtime `{ nodeLlamaCpp: \"3.22.2\", node: process.version }`;\n105\t  - system prompt hash, template hash (hash the GGUF `tokenizer.chat_template` string, not a\n106\t    boolean), history hash, kept/dropped counts;\n107\t  - the settings that affect prompt rendering (`reasoning`, `promptRepeat`, `structuredOutput`,\n108\t    `jsonSchema` hash, `contextSize`);\n109\t  - a `requestId` (also used in logs).\n110\t- `chat-store` already persists `stats` on a message (`src/chat-store.js:73,121`), so no\n111\t  schema migration is needed; add `stats.manifest` only when present.\n112\t- Benchmark:\n113\t  - add `promptFingerprint` and `runtime.nodeLlamaCpp` to the run result\n114\t    (`benchmarks/run.mjs:531-568`);\n115\t  - include the global/per-variant system prompt and the model template hash in `testHash`\n116\t    (or in a new `promptSetHash` that is part of the comparability check);\n117\t  - if a run's `promptFingerprint` differs from the baseline while `suiteVersion`/`testHash`"}]},"uuid":"3553158d-441f-46bf-a405-72730eb4a1ad","timestamp":"2026-10-30T15:03:57.290Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"c:\\Users\\Yunus-Emre\\Desktop\\portable_agent_kit\\reports\\modelduck-neurocore-research.md","content":"## Executive summary\n\n1. **Do not port NeuroCore's architecture.** It is a multi-module Python control plane with\n   flows, a brain, memory, messaging and a marketplace. ModelDuck is one Node process and a\n   browser UI. What transfers is a handful of **invariants** that NeuroCore learned to enforce.\n2. **The strongest fit is benchmark integrity.** ModelDuck's `testHash` covers the suite and\n   matrix settings, but not the system prompt, per-variant system prompt, GGUF chat template,\n   or `node-llama-cpp` version. A change there can move quality without the gate noticing.\n   A **generation manifest / prompt fingerprint** closes that gap and reuses the existing\n   `engine.chat` path for both the app and the benchmark.\n3. **Second: versioned prompts and presets with benchmark-gated trust.** NeuroCore records\n   every prompt-material change under its SHA-256, bounds history, and treats rollback as a\n   new version. ModelDuck's presets are hardcoded and nothing records that a preset earned\n   trust. This is a direct extension of the benchmark moat.\n4. **Third: a deterministic pre-flight load plan.** NeuroCore's flow simulator returns\n   blocking/warning findings and a cost envelope without executing anything. ModelDuck silently\n   tries four context sizes and reports a generic OOM. A load plan makes the fallback\n   inspectable and gives the benchmark matrix a shared report shape.\n5. **Fourth: a per-request and JIT-load budget.** One context and one process are deliberate;\n   an API client can still hold the model with a long prompt or thrash JIT loads. NeuroCore's\n   shared allowance, \"lower never raise\" overrides and `pressure` snapshot fit this exactly.\n6. **Later, and only with MCP/RAG:** fence untrusted tool/retrieval text, guard repeated tool\n   calls, and make arbitrary Hugging Face acquisition SSRF-safe. These are prerequisites, not\n   standalone features.\n7. **Do not copy** the brain/self-evolution loop, meta-flows, marketplace, multi-platform\n   messaging, memory evidence graph, actor roles, daily self-modification quotas, or the\n   FAISS/RRF stack. They add surface area ModelDuck deliberately does not want.\n\n---\n\n## What ModelDuck already has\n\nThe table exists to stop the report from re-proposing existing work.\n\n| Area | Current state | NeuroCore analogue | Verdict |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Prompt stats | Token counts, TTFT, tok/s, stop reason per reply (`src/engine.js:479-490`) | Trace spans, token counters (`core/observability.py`) | Add a prompt manifest |\n| History window | Silent truncation at 40 messages / 48k chars (`src/engine.js:41-57`) | Pinned system prefix with a digest (`modules/agent_loop/prompt_digest.py`) | Expose the truncation |\n| Session reuse | Signature = model id + system prompt + context size + history length (`src/engine.js:521-527`) | System prefix re-hashed before every model call | Hash the content, not the length |\n| Benchmark provenance | `suiteVersion`, `testHash`, matrix settings, app version, git, machine (`benchmarks/run.mjs:422-458,531-568`) | Baseline requires provenance (`modules/brain/improvement.py:378-401`) | Add runtime/template/prompt hashes |\n| Presets | Three hardcoded presets (`src/config.js:48-109`); README claims they earn trust after both phases | Content-addressed versions + eval-gated promotion (`modules/skills/versions.py`, `modules/brain/improvement.py:279-349`) | Version and record trust |\n| Load | Context fallback loop `[wanted, 3072, 2048, 1024]` (`src/engine.js:257-287`) | Deterministic pre-flight with blocking findings (`core/flow_simulation.py`) | Add a load plan |\n| Budget | `maxTokens` and `contextOverflow: strict` (`src/engine.js:429-439`) | Shared execution budget with pressure (`core/execution_budget.py`) | Add wall/JIT budgets |\n| Metrics | Last generation only (`engine.js` state) | Bounded p50/p95/p99 + p99 stall detection (`core/node_stall.py`) | Add a live monitor |\n| Security | Loopback/Host/Origin guard, CSP, 8 MB body cap, SHA-256 API keys (`src/http.js`, `src/server-settings.js`) | Pinned HTTP, untrusted fencing, confirmation phrases | Partial; add the missing pieces |\n| MCP/RAG | Two persisted switches, no tools (`README.md:208`) | Fence + loop guard + tool tiers | Prerequisite work |\n| Downloads | Curated catalog, `.part` resume, size check, `redirect: \"follow\"` (`src/downloader.js:155-163,222-229`) | SSRF-safe pinned fetch + content hash (`core/pinned_http.py`, `core/research_gateway.py`) | Harden with HF pull |\n\n---\n\n## Tier 1 — do first\n\n### 1. Generation manifest and prompt fingerprint\n\n**What NeuroCore does.** `modules/agent_loop/prompt_digest.py` snapshots the leading system\nmessages when a loop starts, hashes their contents, verifies them before every model call,\nrestores the pinned prefix if compaction or truncation changed it, and records\n`integrity_violation` in the iteration trace (`modules/agent_loop/node.py:720-722`). The point\nis not display: the governing prompt is treated as a value that must survive every rewrite.\n`core/observability.py` adds trace IDs, spans, token counters and a JSONL trace sink.\n\n**Why it fits ModelDuck.** The benchmark gate is ModelDuck's moat, but its `testHash` is\ncomputed from `SUITE_VERSION`, the prompts, and the matrix settings (`benchmarks/run.mjs:422-458`).\nIt does not include:\n\n- the global `SYSTEM_PROMPT` (`benchmarks/run.mjs:26-28,551`) or a per-variant `systemPrompt`\n  (`run.mjs:254,353`);\n- the GGUF chat template — the registry only stores a boolean\n  (`src/model-registry.js:124`), not the template text;\n- the `node-llama-cpp` version (`package.json:23`);\n- the exact history after truncation (`src/engine.js:41-57`).\n\nAny of those can change the tokens the model sees while the suite version and test hash stay\nthe same. The gate then attributes a quality delta to the wrong parameter. The same gap exists\noutside the benchmark: a reply's `stats` do not say which prompt produced it.\n\n**What to add.**\n\n- `src/prompt-manifest.js`, pure and dependency-free:\n  - `sha256Hex(value)` over canonical JSON.\n  - `historyWindow(messages)` returns `{ messages, droppedMessages, droppedChars, truncated }`\n    and becomes the single truncation implementation used by `engine.js`.\n  - `fingerprintPrompt({ systemPrompt, history, templateText, settings })` returns\n    `{ promptDigest, systemPromptDigest, historyDigest, templateDigest, chars, messages }`.\n- `engine.chat` attaches a `manifest` to `stats`:\n  - model `{ id, fileName, size, modifiedAt }`;\n  - runtime `{ nodeLlamaCpp: \"3.22.2\", node: process.version }`;\n  - system prompt hash, template hash (hash the GGUF `tokenizer.chat_template` string, not a\n    boolean), history hash, kept/dropped counts;\n  - the settings that affect prompt rendering (`reasoning`, `promptRepeat`, `structuredOutput`,\n    `jsonSchema` hash, `contextSize`);\n  - a `requestId` (also used in logs).\n- `chat-store` already persists `stats` on a message (`src/chat-store.js:73,121`), so no\n  schema migration is needed; add `stats.manifest` only when present.\n- Benchmark:\n  - add `promptFingerprint` and `runtime.nodeLlamaCpp` to the run result\n    (`benchmarks/run.mjs:531-568`);\n  - include the global/per-variant system prompt and the model template hash in `testHash`\n    (or in a new `promptSetHash` that is part of the comparability check);\n  - if a run's `promptFingerprint` differs from the baseline while `suiteVersion`/`testHash`","numLines":100,"startLine":18,"totalLines":511}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"1e9e7a1c-b289