{"parentUuid":"2eab7e29-206b-4a3b-9a26-9321d045de79","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgYdibQFFCstoC8soWG6R","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01JqBAifmfaXij9bg6sLcrFU","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"c:\\Users\\Yunus-Emre\\Desktop\\portable_agent_kit\\.idea-catcher\\dossiers\\report-analysis-modelduck.md","content":"# Dossier: Report Analysis Follow-ups (ModelDuck)\n\n- **Source URL**: `reports/Report analysis 2026-10-30.md` (private local analysis of the four research reports)\n- **Source License**: `Local analysis; cited papers and specifications retain their own licenses`\n- **Analyzed Commit / Date**: `modelduck 1c9876d + uncommitted ADR-018..020` / `2026-10-30`\n- **Primary Stack**: Node.js 20+ ESM, `node-llama-cpp` 3.22.2, vanilla UI.\n\n## 1. Executive Summary & Core Architecture\n\nChecking the literature review's claims against ModelDuck's code confirmed three gaps that no register entry covered. First, `getLlama()` is called without a `build` option, so node-llama-cpp's default (`\"auto\"`) may download and compile llama.cpp when no prebuilt binary fits; the README promises \"Everything stays on your computer.\" Second, the Token saver preset still uses q4_0 KV, which ModelDuck's own baseline measured at 19.1 % against 85.7 %. Third, three README claims overstate what the code guarantees.\n\n## 2. Target Routing Matrix\n\n> The routing below records the first analysis. `../ideas.json` and the generated `../MATRIX.md` are authoritative for the current target and decision status.\n\n| Idea ID | Concept Name | Target Project | Value Score (1-5) | Complexity (Low/Med/High) | Recommended Action |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `IDEA-NEXT-1` | No Silent Runtime Build or Download | `modelduck` | 4 | Low | Adopt |\n| `IDEA-NEXT-2` | Token Saver Preset on q8_0 KV | `modelduck` | 3 | Low | Adopt after benchmark |\n| `IDEA-NEXT-3` | Evidence-Scoped README Claims | `modelduck` | 3 | Low | Adopt |\n\n---\n\n## 3. Extracted Ideas & Cold-Start Implementation Blueprints\n\n### No Silent Runtime Build or Download\n- **Target Project**: `modelduck`\n- **Source**: `src/engine.js:181,197` (`getLlama` without `build`); node-llama-cpp `getLlama.d.ts` (`build` defaults to `\"auto\"`)\n- **Priority / Effort vs. Impact**: High Impact / Low Effort\n\n#### Core Mechanism & Value\nPass `build: \"never\"` so the runtime uses only the installed prebuilt binaries. A missing binary becomes an actionable error instead of a hidden GitHub download and a long compile.\n\n#### Potential Improvements\nMakes the \"no network except downloads you start\" claim true; removes a multi-minute hang on unusual CPUs.\n\n#### Potential Weaknesses\nA machine without a matching prebuilt binary can no longer load models automatically.\n\n#### How to Combat These\nMap the failure to a Why/Fix error that names `npx node-llama-cpp source download` as an explicit, user-started step; keep the existing GPU-to-CPU fallback.\n\n#### Cold-Start Agent Implementation Blueprint\n1. Add `build: \"never\"` to both `getLlama` calls in `src/engine.js`.\n2. Map a binary-not-found failure to an AppError with Why/Fix.\n3. Document network use in the README.\n\n### Token Saver Preset on q8_0 KV\n- **Target Project**: `modelduck`\n- **Source**: `src/config.js:61`; README benchmark table (Q4 KV 19.1 % vs 85.7 %)\n- **Priority / Effort vs. Impact**: Medium Impact / Low Effort\n\n#### Core Mechanism & Value\nSwap the preset's KV cache from q4_0 to q8_0, which the baseline shows is close to F16, keeping the small context and batch that save memory.\n\n#### Potential Improvements\nThe lightest preset stops destroying quality on the 0.5B model.\n\n#### Potential Weaknesses\nUses more KV memory than q4_0 (about 2× the q4 KV size).\n\n#### How to Combat These\nRun both benchmark phases and update the README table before shipping (generation changes are benchmark-gated).\n\n#### Cold-Start Agent Implementation Blueprint\n1. Change `kvCache` to `q8_0` in `token_saver`; update its description.\n2. Run `npm run bench:model` and `npm run bench:chat`; record the run.\n\n### Evidence-Scoped README Claims\n- **Target Project**: `modelduck`\n- **Source**: `README.md:6` (\"Everything stays on your computer\"), `:99` (\"deterministic\"), `:135` (presets \"only earn trust after both phases pass\")\n- **Priority / Effort vs. Impact**: Medium Impact / Low Effort\n\n#### Core Mechanism & Value\nState what is measured or enforced: chats and prompts stay local, network use is limited to downloads the user starts; the benchmark is seeded at batch 1 with single runs; presets are benchmark-first but trust is not recorded.\n\n#### Potential Improvements\nRemoves claims the review's Table 6 flags as indefensible.\n\n#### Potential Weaknesses\nPlainer copy reads less impressive.\n\n#### How to Combat These\nKeep each claim with its evidence, which is the product's stated differentiator.\n\n#### Cold-Start Agent Implementation Blueprint\n1. Rewrite the three sentences; keep the README under its size budget.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2627,"cache_read_input_tokens":300808,"output_tokens":2325,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":78},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2627,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2325,"cache_read_input_tokens":300808,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2627,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2627},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01JqBAifmfaXij9bg6sLcrFU":{"file_path":"c:\\Users\\Yunus-Emre\\D