{"parentUuid":"70398b80-2a12-4a9f-8445-887e055b7009","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"0e3c382b-9f12-4236-8c9e-f3361946ffd3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01447j9trgCrqD2o3Hf5yPJB","type":"tool_result","content":"4/4 gates passed for 'modelduck'","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"2ffbba00-3336-4438-9851-e50e98e49f21","timestamp":"2026-10-30T15:17:03.714Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"4/4 gates passed for 'modelduck'","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\Yunus-Emre\\Desktop\\portable_agent_kit\\projects\\modelduck\\.aikit\\decisions.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":154,"oldLines":3,"newStart":154,"newLines":23,"lines":[" - **Context**: IDEA-1047. `ChatStore` capped conversations at 200 by insertion order on load (`slice`) and on create (`length = 200`). A live probe showed chat 201 deleting the oldest-created chat even when it was used that day, and loading a 250-chat file dropping 50, including the most recently used. The cap exists because `chats.json` is rewritten on every message."," - **Decision**: Keep the 200 most recently used chats in `chats.json` and move the rest to `chats.archive.json`, which is written only when the archive changes and always before `chats.json`; on load a chat found in both files keeps its active copy. `restore(id)` moves an archived chat back (counting as used now) and archives the next least recent. `GET /api/conversations` adds `archived`, `/api/state` adds `archivedConversations`, opening an archived chat restores it, and delete reaches archived chats. The sidebar lists them under an Archived group, searchable like the rest."," - **Consequences**: No chat is lost to the cap and the per-message write stays bounded. The archive grows with history and is loaded into memory at startup; a very large archive would call for paging (out of scope). An interrupted save can at worst duplicate a chat, which load removes.","+","+### ADR-0