{"parentUuid":"8b07c482-d40f-4e0b-b032-b1b027fb1095","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgYeHa9mUqvP2JWwuZUSd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've made reports and notes private, recorded the analysis in the register, and implemented four more ModelDuck fixes. All 111 tests and the 4 project gates pass. Nothing is committed yet.\n\n**Private files:** `reports/` and `research_notes/` are listed in `.git/info/exclude`. That file stays on this machine, so they won't be committed and `git status` no longer lists them. Since git never stores them, they're also lost if this folder is deleted or re-cloned; keep a backup elsewhere if they matter.\n\n**Register changes:**\n- 1037 (benchmark statistics) approved as P2.\n- 903 widened to the full memory check.\n- Three new approved ideas from the analysis, each with a dossier:\n  - 1061: the runtime never downloads or builds anything on its own.\n  - 1062: the Token saver preset moves to 8-bit KV.\n  - 1063: honest README claims.\n- 971 (research-engine) marked to revisit once that project's active task finishes.\n\n**What I built** (decision record ADR-021):\n- **1061: no hidden downloads.** Model loading now uses only the runtime files already installed and never fetches or compiles llama.cpp. If those files are missing, you get an explanation and a fix. I loaded the real Qwen2.5 1.5B model this way, from the binary that ships with ModelDuck.\n- **1063: honest README claims.**\n  - \"Everything stays on your computer\" now names the one exception: model downloads you start yourself.\n  - \"Deterministic\" benchmark becomes \"seeded, batch-1\".\n  - The presets sentence now says ModelDuck doesn't record which preset passed.\n- **853: stalled downloads.** After 60 seconds without data, a download stops as \"stalled\" and frees its slot. The partial file is kept, so clicking Download again resumes it.\n- **903: memory check before loading.**\n  - ModelDuck estimates the model's memory need (weights, KV cache at your context size, plus a reserve).\n  - Above 75% of free RAM it refuses, and the message names the largest context that would fit. A **Load anyway** button overrides this.\n  - If the context still has to shrink while loading, a notice says what you asked for and what you got.\n  - On the real model with 4.19 GiB free, both a 4K and a 32K context were rated \"comfortable\". I haven't yet checked the estimate against measured memory use, which the research brief asks for (within 15%).\n\n**Waiting for your commit**, as four separate commits: ADR-018 (website access), ADR-019 (bad model files and duplicate downloads), ADR-020 (chat archive) and ADR-021 (this batch).\n\n**Left, each needing something I can't do offline:**\n- **862 (verify downloads by hash):** fetching the real hashes from Hugging Face means going online once.\n- **1062 (Token saver preset) and 1037 (benchmark statistics):** both need a real benchmark run, which needs the three benchmark models downloaded.\n\nDo you want me to download those models and the catalog hashes, about 1.7 GB from Hugging Face?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":923,"cache_read_input_tokens":357428,"output_tokens":1470,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":454},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":923,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1470,"cache_read_input_tokens":357428,"cache_creation_input_tokens":923,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":923},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"b3a74c7e-5f91-4947-a77d-2e82aa3dff3c","apiBloc