{"parentUuid":"221b02be-9283-4389-9f20-9057a6e7a93d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgYfiM14HhoFJthYCTPd3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Ud8RRt5Dz4JepqeJqFJPhs","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python - <<'EOF'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np = Path(\"benchmarks/README.md\"); s = p.read_bytes().decode(\"utf-8\"); nl = \"\\r\\n\" if \"\\r\\n\" in s else \"\\n\"\nstart = s.index(\"The fourteen tasks cover exact instruction following\")\nend = s.index(\"## Test identity\")\nnew = nl.join([\n \"Suite v5 has 57 items in ten categories:\",\n \"\",\n \"| Category | Items | What is measured |\",\n \"|---|---:|---|\",\n \"| code | 12 | 10 functions run against 3–4 test cases each, plus the original add/repair checks |\",\n \"| bugfix | 8 | Off-by-one, wrong initial value, wrong divisor, inverted parity, missing join, inverted filter, wrong split, wrong formula; the repair must pass the tests |\",\n \"| comprehension | 8 | Who/what, event order, negation, time arithmetic, two-step inference, main idea, close distractor, abstaining when the answer is absent |\",\n \"| recall | 7 | Locker-register lookups at the start, middle and end, a reverse lookup, two needles, list position, latest value wins |\",\n \"| facts | 10 | Capitals, a chemical symbol, a planet, an author, a year, a boiling point, continents, photosynthesis |\",\n \"| instruction, reasoning, knowledge, format, context | 12 | The original v1–v2 tasks |\",\n \"\",\n \"Executable checks run the generated JavaScript in a child process started with\",\n \"`node --permission` and no allow flags, so file, child-process, worker and network\",\n \"access are denied, and a 5-second timeout kills runaway loops. Each test case is one\",\n \"check, so a partly correct function earns partial credit.\",\n \"\",\n \"Speed-only variants (threads, batch, pool, sequences, context size, mmap,\",\n \"checkpoints, GPU layers) run a 14-item cross-family smoke subset\",\n \"(`SMOKE_PROMPT_IDS`); model, quantization, KV cache, flash attention and presets\",\n \"run the full suite.\",\n \"\",\n \"## Statistics and the gate\",\n \"\",\n \"Check percentages stay in the report, but the gate works on **items**: an item\",\n \"passes when all of its checks pass. Every run reports the item pass rate with a\",\n \"Wilson 95% interval, overall, per model and per category (`items` in the result).\",\n \"\",\n \"Against the baseline, items are paired by variant and prompt. For each variant\",\n \"the runner counts items that regressed and improved and runs an exact McNemar\",\n \"test; p-values are Holm-corrected across variants (`benchmarks/stats.mjs`). The\",\n \"run **fails** when the paired item pass rate drops by 5 points or more, or when a\",\n \"variant's decline is significant at 0.05 after correction. Any smaller decline is\",\n \"a **warning** that names the regressed items. This replaces the old rule that\",\n \"failed on any 0.01-point drop in the check score.\",\n \"\",\n \"\",\n])\ns = s[:start] + new + s[end:]\ns = s.replace(\"Quality is the percentage of deterministic checks passed. Speed is the median\" + nl, \"Quality is the percentage of checks passed; the gate uses item outcomes (below). Speed is the median\" + nl, 1)\np.write_bytes(s.encode(\"utf-8\"))\nEOF\ngrep -n \"Suite v5\\|## Statistics\\|Quality is\" benchmarks/README.md","description":"Document suite v5 and the statistics gate"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":851,"cache_read_input_tokens":432003,"output_tokens":1398,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":91},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":851,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1398,"c